350009	301	2020-12-30 11:51:27	1.   Ruggedized UAV Jammer (Eagle Hunt-01).  \r\n\r\na.   1st Batch Deployment. EH-01 batch-I is successfully deployed and tested at following sites vide letter PN/NCW/03/2496144 dated 18 Sept 20. Point Recommended to be dropped. \r\n\r\n(1)   GKA- Greater KARSAZ Area (4th FP) on 28 Sep 20 – 3 Oct 20\r\n(2)   PN Dockyard (2nd FP) on 5 - 11 Oct 20\r\n(3)   NRC, ISB (1st FP) on 12 – 18 Oct 20\r\n\r\nb.   During the deployment following activities were performed by INTELL Team. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n(1)   Presentations/ Tutorials. Presentations were given to Marines covering all the details related to EH-01 system, its functionality, operating instructions and maintenance instructions for better operational understanding of the complete EH-01 system. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n(2)   Handing over of Documentation. All necessary jammer documents (Technical manual and Operator manuals) were handed over to the teams. The documents include all aspects of operation, troubleshooting, maintenance and software details. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n(3)   Training. EH-01 ruggedized jammer handling, operation and safety training were provided to Marines. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n(4)   Trials. Jamming trials were also conducted in presence of Marines for the Proof of Concept and better understanding of system operation. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n(5)   Exam. An exam was conducted by the INTELL team for assessing the understanding of Marines on EH-01 system operation. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   2nd Batch. \r\n\r\na.   Procurement. All the local and international procurement for 2nd batch, comprising of 03 ruggedized jammers against commercial drones, is completed. \r\n\r\nb.   Assembly Process. \r\n(1)   Ruggedized casing assembly and internal wiring of components for 2nd batch of jammers is completed.\r\n\r\n(2)   The mold for ruggedized jammer box is developed from local industry in lines with INTELL design. Raw material for ruggedized casing has also been procured. The layup process on mold paint job is also completed.\r\n\r\n(3)   Directional RF antennas. In-house development and testing of transmitting LPDA and Yagi antenna for 2nd batch is completed.\r\n\r\n(4)   Readiness for deployment of jammers under batch II has been reported vide letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND WING/03/7791782.\r\n\r\n3.   Maintenance Routines. A meeting was held at NRDI INTELL on 10 Nov 20 between INTELL NRDI, NCMA and PSSRF teams to discuss the maintenance roles of NRDI INTELL and PSSRF for Eagle Hunt 01 routed through NCMA. In meeting, it was apprised that:\r\n\r\na.   Level 1 & 2 maintenance will be undertaken by user as prescribed by the details provided by NRDI INTELL in EH-01 technical manual.\r\n\r\nb.   Level 3 & 4 maintenance requires detailed knowledge of fault diagnosis along with the suitable test equipment. Currently, NRDI INTELL is undertaking Level 3 & 4 maintenance tasks. Level 3 & 4 maintenance capability will be handed over to PSSRF after availability of maintenance setup which includes test equipment along with trained HR. \r\n\r\nc.   Level 3 & 4 Maintenance. The development of troubleshooting flowgraphs and maintenance routines has been completed at NRDI INTELL and forwarded to NCMA/PSSRF vide letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND WING/03/7720037for undertaking Level 3 & 4 maintenance.\r\n   \r\nd.   Level 5 maintenance activity requires in depth knowledge of the modules used in EH-01. Therefore, Level 5 repair activity, as of now, be undertaken by NRDI INTELL to avoid any unintended damage.\r\n\r\ne.   List of test equipment to be procured by PSSRF for undertaking level 3 & 4 maintenance is also forwarded to NCMA vide letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND WING/03/7791782.\r\n\r\n4.   Serial Production Facility (SPF). Construction of Layup facility/ paint shop (shed and floor) is completed. Point Recommended to be dropped.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-01-06 12:54:54	25	Dec 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
