350003	533	2021-08-31 10:41:36	1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Small Scale Weapon Demonstrator. \r\n\r\n(1)   Demonstration of the irreversible damage caused on an electronic circuit through combined power of 02x 1 kW magnetrons is being planned. The experimental assembly will be housed in an aluminum casing along with proper jigs and holders for waveguide and coaxial components. CAD models of the casings and of the pertinent assemblies have been prepared. Casing to house the waveguide setup for one of the magnetrons have been developed, and its QC is in progress.\r\n\r\n(2)   Site selection for weapon demonstration is also in progress. HQ COMPAK suggested to use RDS NATHIAGALI AOR as the site vide letter No. PN/HQ COMPAK/ 03/9526808 dated 18 Jun 21. The demonstration will be conducted with adequate safeties in place, for which QC sheets are being prepared.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Power Amplifier. Three stages of the Preamplifier are required for requisite RF power input to the 100 Watt MOSFET. All stages of the preamplifier circuits have been designed. Procurement of IC and pertinent components has been completed. Design optimization of all 3 stages and their fabrication is currently in progress. Multiple manufacturing facilities have been contacted for fabrication.\r\n\r\n2.   Following procurement actions are in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement Completed. Experimental components including 1 kW magnetrons, coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs, FPGA boards, Spectrum Analyzer, Switch Mode Power Supplies, 1 kW waveguide terminations, N52 magnets, Oscilloscope, 2.5 kW waveguide terminations, E-field probe, Signal Generator, and DC power supply have been completed.\r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in Progress. Procurement of replacement magnets, and high power refractory material is in progress. Due COVID-19 pandemic, delay is expected in delivery of these components.\r\n\r\n3.   Following studies are being conducted to formulate research plans for X-band in the ensuing year: \r\n\r\na.   Research on Ceramic Materials for high power high frequency operation\r\nb.   Research on Ferrimagnetic Materials for circulators at high power and high frequency operation\r\n\r\nc.   Commercial 25 kW X-band pulsed magnetrons are procured to study pulsed emission characteristics. Injection locking will be undertaken to furnish frequency locking requirements for pulsed magnetrons.\r\n\r\nd.   A pulsed power supply based on Pulsed Forming Networks (PFN) required to drive the pulsed magnetrons is currently being designed.\r\n\r\ne.   Preliminary design of RF devices including circulators and directional couplers at X-band (9 GHz) has been finalized.\r\n\r\n4.   Technical proposal amounting 260M for Phase II pertaining to power combination of multiple J-band pulsed magnetrons of redundant AM-39 has been submitted to NHQ for approval.\r\n\r\na.   An RF anechoic chamber will be designed and fabricated to enable shielded high power testing of the magnetron combination experiment with adequate safety measures.\r\n\r\nb.   Civil Works are required for development of a test site to carry-out the high power microwave experiments with 25 kW pulsed magnetrons. The proposed test site will be developed, comprising of an experimentation room with adequate concrete wall thickness to ensure minimal penetration of the EM waves.\r\n\r\n5.   Miscellaneous Study. \r\n\r\na.   EMC/EMI Survey. Upon directions of HQ COMLOG, GM RD&TA approached NRDI R&D Wing to conduct EMC/EMI survey to finalize antenna location onboard PNS ALAMGIR vide letter number PN/PN Dockyard/PE AND D WING/ GM(RD AND  TA)/03/7895873 dated 06 Jan 21. The required E-field probe has been procured. Frequency compatible antennas are required for testing, which are currently being finalized. Test procedures for Radiated Emission tests RE-102 and RE-103; Conducted Emission tests CE-101 and CE-102; Conducted Susceptibility Tests CS-101, CS-114, CS-116; and Radiated Susceptibility Tests RS-103 have been finalized.\r\n\r\nb.   SR60 Study. RF team visited PN ship and conducted a survey to determine functional replacement of the SR60 Radar. PPF form raised by PN DY is under process at NHQ.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-09-24 11:32:54	25	Aug 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
