350013	739	2022-06-04 05:56:50	1.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI. The civil work required for installation of GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI, undertaken by M/s FAST team, has been completed successfully. Tower construction, Radome mounting on tower, GT&RS equipment installation, integration of Directional Antenna Director (DAD) system and testing activities have been successfully completed. The GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI is made fully operational as reported vide reference PN/ NRDI/ R AND D WING/ 03/12348866 dated 11 Feb 22. Trial was conducted with P3C MPA on 10 Feb 22 and smooth video received with a range over 100NM. Subsequently, the same is being used in ongoing ISR missions. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS MIANWALI. Nominated reps of NRDI INTELL and CDR JNB conducted joint trials of RDS MIANWALI for site finalization of permanent installation of Ground Terminal and Receiver Station (GT&RS) on 10 Mar 22. The trials of LoS VTS system with P3C indicates normal operation of GT&RS station without any system glitches (Video & GPS data) while positioning aircraft at different locations. The mission route of P3C for undertaking the trials covered TURBAT, ORMARA, TP1 (At Sea), TP2 (At Sea), TP3 (At Sea), NATHIAGALI, MAKRAN, and TURBAT. The maximum range for the trials was 112 NM. Moreover, there is adequate power supply and availability of network at the proposed site neither there is any interference observed with nearby installations or equipment. In this regard, site between CDR JNB HUT & DEFCOM building (25.1903 N, 64.6008E) has been finalized for installation of said system. The same location is confirmed by HQ COMCOAST vide Letter no PN/HQ COASTAL COMMAND/03/12810179 dated 21 Mar 22. The finalized site/ location for GT & RS at Hammerhead Ormara has been included in updated draft master plan for RDS MIANWALI vide PN/HQ COASTAL COMMAND/03/13108823 dated 28 Apr 22.\r\n\r\n3.   GT&RS Location Finalization for NAS TURBAT. Identification of suitable site (Roof top of Admin Block) for installation of GT&RS at NAS TURBAT under Project Raven-I has been forwarded vide letter PN/HQ COMNAV/03/12508931 dated 24 Feb 22. CMES(N) COMPAK has asked DW&CE (NHQ) for suitability of proposed permanent installation site w.r.t existing load bearing capacity vide letter no PN/HQ COMPAK/CMES (N) COMPAK/03/12771728 dated 16 Mar 22. The same has been reported by HQ COMNAV for information vide letter no PN/HQ COMNAV/03/12799310 dated 18 Mar 22.  GT&RS installation on roof top of Admin block is not structurally feasible as reported vide Letter no PN/DWCE/03/3741909 dated 28 May 22 and Letter no PN/NCW (TECH)/ 03/3701439 dated 25 May 22. CO SIDDIQ has proposed 02 optional sites (on ground) i.v.o Admin Block to NRDI INTELL for concurrence and feasibility vide letter no PN/HQ COMNAV/PNS SIDDIQ/03/13399703 dated 31 May 22. NRDI INTELL plans to visit the proposed sites for site finalization. In this regard, facilitation has been requested to visit PNS SIDDIQ vide Letter no. PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13411808 dated 01 June 22.\r\n \r\n4.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at GWADAR. NRDI INTELL has requested HQ COMCOAST to share the report pertaining to Geo Hazard study of the area, if available, to evaluate the alternate suitable location vide PN/ DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11409842 dated 30 Nov 21. NHQs has been requested to pursue approval vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12557270 dated 25 Feb 22. HQ COMCOAST has requested NRDI for a survey to alternate site selection vide letter PN/HQ COASTAL COMMAND/03/13077056 dated 18 Apr 22. NRDI in response has nominated NRDI team for the survey vide reference PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13142045 dated 27 Apr 22 and have asked HQ COMCOAST PoC to attend a session on 28 Apr 22 at NRDI INTELL, R&D Wing at PNS Jauhar. The objective of the session is to brainstorm the alternate possible locations for placement of GT&RS and to discuss possible locations marked on the map (GWADAR AOR) to ensure line of sight of ground station with aircraft. A meeting was held at NRDI INTELL on 28 Apr 22 regarding finalization of site/ location for GT&RS installation at GWADAR vide PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13175108 dated 29 Apr 22. Based on the NRDI requirement rep of HQ COMWEST agreed to conduct a survey of GWADAR Hammerhead and subsequently share the possible location for installation of GT&RS. Letter has been sent to HQ COMWEST for updated status on possible locations for installation of GT&RS. Letter no PN/ DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13317167 dated 21 May 22 and Letter no PN/NCW (TECH)/03/3701439 dated 25 May 22 refer. In response to this, PNS AKRAM suggested two possible sites vide letter PN/HQ COASTAL COMMAND/03/13395641 dated 01 June 22. For site finalization, NRDI INTELL has requested to visit PNS AKRAM vide Letter no. PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13426658 dated 02 June 22.\r\n\r\n5.   Milestones Timeline Amendment. Due delays in site allocation, the milestones are being amended as requested by M/s MTSS vide MTSS/20/42 dated 09 Feb 22. A request to expedite approval for smooth execution of the project was also sent by NRDI INTELL vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12551993 dated 25 Feb 22. The approval of milestone timeline amendment is still awaited. It is pertinent to mention that milestones M7 and M10 are already completed but the corresponding payment cannot be filed due to pending amendment case.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-08-02 23:16:17	25	May 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
