350002	305	2020-12-30 12:03:44	1.   GPS Spoofing Hardware Development.\r\n\r\na.   Development of End user GUI. The GUI has been updated to make it more user friendly. Beta testing on the software is completed and subsequently associated recommendations have been implemented. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nb.   Laboratory Trials. Using the newly assembled ruggedized housing and spoofing PoC assembly, successful in-house trials have been conducted. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nc.   Product Manuals. The technical and operator manuals for the product have been developed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nd.   Acceptance Trials. Acceptance trials have been conducted successfully in the field on 13 Nov 20, at PN GHARO site. Acceptance by the committee has been reported vide letter PN/HQ PAK MARINES/2ND FP BN/03/7405148 dated 25 Nov 20. This trial successfully concluded all planned trials of PROJECT EAGLE HUNT. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Serial Production. Deployment of Drone Jammers and Spoofing systems while considering FP and GBAD setups vis-à-vis functionality of Project Eagle Hunt deliverables was presented to COMCOAST on 16 Nov 20 vide letter PN/ HQ COSTAL COMMAND/03/7250666. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Force Majeure has been invoked by DITD due COVID pandemic. The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR is also delayed due to export permit processing delays caused by COVID 19 pandemic. Once 3D X-band RADAR will be received, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of Eagle Hunt -3C version (autonomous GPS spoofing using X-band RADAR). 3D RADARs from other OEMs are also being explored and two of them are also shortlisted.\r\n\r\n4.   Housing of reactive jamming equipment in the marinized container is in progress. e equipment installation activity will be completed by end-Jan 21.\r\n\r\n5.   Miscellaneous Studies Supporting PN Fleet and Repair Agencies undertaken during reporting period.\r\n\r\na.   PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) training. OJT of 07 Dockyard Lab staff comprising of theory classes and demonstration labs on Omniscan MX2 PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) equipment is completed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nb.   Ultrasonic Testing (UT) of Besconds used in the cable hull passage onboard S/Ms. UT of a locally developed Balezona & Neoprene based besconds, along with NG besconds was undertaken. No flaws / defects were found in NG bescond, while locally developed besconds were found defected. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nc.   500 Watt High Power Antenna for PAF. PAF 606 Workshop conducted thermal testing of the antenna during high power operation, which revealed satisfactory results. Measurement of radiation pattern and range testing are in progress. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nd.   RF Testing of SATCOM Systems onboard PNS/Ms. INTELL team visited PNS/M HASHMAT and PNS/M HURMAT for RF path testing of SATCOM systems, with coaxial terminations replacing antennas. Two antennas from these S/Ms were also tested in INTELL Lab on VNA and a detailed report was submitted to GM W & S for facilitation in defect rectification.\r\n\r\ne.   Air Drop Logistics Container (ADLC). NHQ assigned study is being undertaken to determine drop trajectory, descent rate / terminal velocity and selection of optimal parachute system for ADLCs. Detailed structural analysis will also be undertaken for design assessment and determination of stress concentration regions. Subsequently, a manufacturing plan will be developed for serial production of ADLCs.	DSensors	Edited	2021-01-06 12:53:46	25	Dec 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
