350002	168	2020-09-03 10:04:26	1.   Reactive Jamming. QA/QC has been carried out on the reactive jamming code. Improvements in UI based on the feedback are being integrated into the code. \r\n\r\n2.   GPS Spoofing.\r\na.   Three versions of Eagle Hunt 3 i.e. GPS spoofing is proposed by INTELL to NHQ. The following are the details of versions:\r\n\r\n1)   Eagle Hunt 3A - Manual operation\r\n2)   Eagle Hunt 3B - Semi autonomous operation\r\n3)   Eagle Hunt 3C - Fully autonomous operation\r\n\r\nb.   Currently INTELL is involved in finalization of PoC for ruggedization. The target completion date is by mid Sep 20.\r\n\r\nc.   HOTAS Field Trials. Successful GPS spoofing trials using HOTAS joystick (Eagle Hunt 3A) for hostile UAV control have been conducted.\r\n\r\nd.   Internet Independent Spoofing (IIS). The capability is developed to generate internet independent spoofing signals for unlimited time duration by continuously offloading the memory in real time.\r\n\r\ne.   Development of End user GUI.  A user friendly UI is being finalized for linking the spoofing code, user inputs such as spoofing time and location. The UI incorporates digital maps for feeding the spoofing locations.\r\n\r\nf.   Acceptance trials. Trial sheets compilation are also in process and will be finalized by mid Sep 20 for final PoC.\r\n\r\ng.   Force Majeure has been invoked by DITD due COVID pandemic. The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR is also delayed due to export permit processing delays caused by COVID 19 pandemic. Once 3D X-band RADAR will be received, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of GPS spoofing milestone.\r\n\r\n3.   Housing of Project Eagle Hunt equipment in Marinized Container will be used as Technology demonstrator.\r\n\r\na.   Design of container along with the final layout has been completed. \r\n\r\nb.   A PoC of reactive jamming is being installed in marinized container at the M/s RIMS facility in presence of INTELL team (24th Aug- 3rd Sep 20).\r\n\r\n4.   Miscellaneous Studies Supporting PN Fleet and Repair Agencies undertaken during reporting period \r\n\r\na.   Development of training modules of PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) equipment Omni Scan MX2 for Dockyard Lab staff is under progress. First set of notes will be completed by end Sep 20. Dockyard staff is also attached for OJT.\r\n\r\nb.   Testing of AB Seats.  The AB seats are used in submarine hull and backup valves ensuring water tightness integrity at high pressures.  DT-Destructive Testing (Toughness, hardness and tensile testing) & NDT- Non Destructive Testing (attenuation measurement through ultrasonic testing- UT) of AB seat seal of original manufacturer and local manufacturer were undertaken to furnish material qualification. A detailed report recommending the qualification of locally developed AB seats’ seals is submitted for formal qualification.\r\n\r\nc.   Ultrasonic Testing (UT) of Besconds used in the cable hull passage onboard S/Ms. UT of Neoprene based locally developed besconds was undertaken. The bescond is rejected due presence of flaws / voids at multiple locations.	DSensors	Finalized	2020-09-07 12:37:22	30	Aug 20	-20-25-30-25-20-25-30-	-20-25-30-25-20-	f	\N
