350014	734	2022-06-04 05:41:43	1.   Design. A detailed study on engineering design of ship-based gyro stabilized platform has been carried out. It is being optimized for PN ships. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Modelling and Simulation. A detailed CAD model of GSP has been developed based on URD. Forward kinematics equations have been generated for the platform. A study on inverse kinematics is underway. Sim-scape® simulations have been carried out. The obtained model has been used to generate a control loop in Matlab and Simulink. Hardware integration of the controller with the Matlab environment has been carried out. \r\n\r\n3.   Design Engineering Study. Design Engineering Study has been submitted against milestone M3. The same will be processed by acceptance committee, upon its formulation, as per the requirement of work order. NHQ comments on DES vide reference letter no. NCW/WO/LOS VTS/II/664 are adequately responded and updated DES has been submitted. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n4.   Development of Scaled Down Model of GSP. A scaled down model of GSP has been developed in-house to validate the calculated range of motion and forces for the platform and linkages. It is designed so to retain the full range of motion in roll (± 25?) and pitch (± 15?) as outlined in the URD, along with a capability to carry up to 1kg of payload. Electronic components for scaled down model have been procured along with raw materials for structure and frame and construction has been completed. The range of motion in roll and pitch for the system acquired using kinematics models have been validated using the scaled down model. Development of scaled down model will provide confidence in full scale GSP development. Point recommended to be dropped.  \r\n\r\n5.   Algorithm Development. The control algorithm for GSP has been extensively studied and different approaches have been implemented in MATLAB. The most optimized approach in terms of system response time was observed using the inverse kinematics model along with PID. Fine tuning of parameters for PID has been carried out. Additionally, an optimized, lightweight version of algorithm to run it on industrial mini PC in the field has also been developed. The algorithm has been tested on industrial PC. Furthermore, the industrial PC has been enabled with remote connection over IP to allow operator to remotely view the status of GSP hardware in real time. \r\n\r\n6.   PN Ship Visit for Finalization of Installation Option/Mechanism On-board PN Ship. Upon directions from NHQ to select feasible options shared by NRDI INTELL for installation of Ship based Line of Sight (LoS) Video Telemetry System (VTS) with Gyro Stabilized Platform (GSP), GM NCW recommended Option-1 (Portable platform) with Radome for relaying of LoS VTS vide letter no PN/PN DOCKYARD/W AND S WING/ GM (C4I)/03/12818126 dated 21 Mar 22. INTELL is pursuing the development in lines with the proposed approach. \r\n\r\n7.   Assembly of Full-Scale Model. Design of full-scale model was completed and design QC has been carried out. Parts are manufactured according to design and assembly has been carried out. QC of assembled parts has also been carried out. Integration of electronics in full scale model is completed. Developed algorithms have also been used to verify movement and stabilization capabilities of full scale GSP model. Integration of MOTUS IMU has been carried out in full scale model. Load testing of full scale model with antenna tracker has been carried out and performance of the platform was found satisfactory and within the full operating range of the platform. Field testing of full scale GSP on board a moving vehicle has been planned to test system performance. During these trials, LOS VTS system will also be integrated alongside GSP. The video reception antenna and tracker will be installed onboard GSP and the performance of reception system as well as stabilization will be evaluated. The trials will be conducted in Jun 22. Design activities are also underway for the installation of GSP onboard PNS platform. CAD models of final installation are being developed and will be completed in Jun 22.\r\n\r\n8.   Development of Test Bench. A test bench is being developed to verify the range of motion of full-scale model of GSP. Updated parameters for this design have been used in forward kinematics equations to verify the range of motion. CAD design of the model has been developed based on the calculated values. QC of design and simulation of stress and forces has also been carried out. Manufacturing of metal linkages and parts has been completed and a few remaining structural components will be completed during Jun 22. Additionally, control algorithm of test bench, which includes multiple testing protocols and extensive reporting on performance of GSP platforms is also under development. A Graphical User Interface (GUI) for ease of operator usage is also developed for GSP test bench. Testing of GUI is undertaken in lab. Complete system testing will be carried out in Jun 22 along with the developed hardware and payload.  \r\n\r\n9.   Machine Shop. Manufacturing of all parts of GSP (scaled down model, full scale model and test bench) is being carried in house. A dust collector has been designed to efficiently remove manufacturing debris from the facility and to improve operator safety. Order for dust collector has been placed and installation will be completed in Jun 22.\r\n\r\n10.   Procurement. Shortlisted stepper motors and drivers for full-scale models as well as the universal joints have also been procured. High torque motors and drivers for test bench have been received and tested in lab. Integration with hardware components is underway.\r\n\r\n11.   Lab & Field trials. Testing of full scale model of GSP is under process. For field testing, Gharo trials have been requested vide Letter no. PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13413611 dated 01 June 22. Approval for said trials is received vide Letter no. PN/HQ COMPAK/03/13418960 dated 02 June 22	DSensors	Finalized	2022-08-02 23:15:54	25	May 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
