200004	694	2022-04-29 04:39:58	1.   Work on all subsystems of ELINT DZ9000S has been completed and lab trials have been conducted successfully.\r\n\r\n2.    The system installation and setting to work has been completed on site on 10 Feb 22.\r\n\r\n3.   Phase I of ATPs (testing of system sensitivity and parameter measurement accuracy) has been successfully completed. \r\n\r\n4.  Procedure of phase II of the ATPs (on air trials) has been finalized with PND and forwarded to NHQ.\r\n\r\n5.   Work will continue on recovery of modules made good using spares from PN inventory as well as on addressing observations by SS/PAT till July 2022\r\n\r\n6.   Two work orders have been issued for this project. All milestones for both projects have been completed pending acceptance by PAT. System is under use for operations since Feb 2022	DCom	Finalized	2022-05-10 22:23:33	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	683	2022-04-27 02:45:18	1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Small Scale Weapon Field Testing. Preliminary Field testing was of 2.5 KW setup was conducted at RDS NATHIAGALI vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12427313 dated 16 Feb 22. The interference was observed with drone as target. Multiple targets such as Low Noise Amplifiers (LNAs) and Phase Frequency Detectors (PFDs) are being evaluated for disruptive demonstration. \r\n\r\nb.   Horn Antenna Improvement. Horn antenna has been redesigned and fabricated resulting in better efficiency.  A testing was carried out at SPF with one horn antenna used for transmission, and another used for reception. A 47 dBm signal was transmitted at 2.45 GHz, and 13 dBm was received at reception antenna at 10 m, resulting in propagation loss of 34 dB. The exercise was aimed to simulate the in-band damage effect on a missile seeker. The 13 dBm signal is disruptive for LNAs and PFDs used in RADAR systems of missile seekers.\r\n\r\nc.   X-Band Experiment. RF devices are being designed and fabricated at X-band for use in power combination of pulsed M1475A 25 kW magnetrons. Power supplies and pulse modulators have been procured and are undergoing extensive testing before use in experimentation.\r\n\r\n2.   RF Power Amplifier. Biasing circuit PCB has been redesigned with adequate track width suitable for high drain current. The Matching networks of the 100 Watt amplifier have been redesigned employing Simplified Real Frequency Technique (SRFT) for output MN and Bounded Performance Technique (BPT) for input MN. PCB fabrication has been completed; PCB component population is in progress and will available for testing in Apr 22.\r\n\r\n3.   Submission of Hardware Purchase Order. Hardware purchase order for experimental components for Magnetron Combination against Milestone M2 has been submitted. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n \r\n4.   Procurement in Progress. Lumped components for in-house designed RFPA, PCB fabrication services and adequate heatsink for the RFPA have been completed. Point recommended to be dropped. \r\n\r\n5.   Following studies are being conducted to formulate research plans for combination of X-band magnetrons for more effective DEW design: \r\n\r\na.   A pulsed power supply based on Pulsed Forming Networks (PFN) required to drive pulsed magnetrons is currently being designed.\r\n\r\nb.   Preliminary design of RF devices including circulators and directional couplers at X-band (9 GHz) has been finalized. \r\n\r\n6.   Technical proposal amounting PKR 232M for Phase II pertaining to power combination of multiple J-band pulsed magnetrons of redundant AM-39 has been submitted to NHQ for approval. An anechoic RF chamber will also be designed and fabricated to enable shielded high-power testing of the magnetron combination experiment with adequate safety measures. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n7.   The proposal for future plan was also submitted vide Ref no PN/DGNRDI/RNDWING/03/11409776 dated 21ST Nov 21 in which Power Combination of multiple 25Kw pulsed J-band magnetrons, to achieve 150 kW combined power, is to be undertaken. Following are the salient highlights of the approach. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\na.   Pulsed operation philosophy will yield lower operational cost, lesser cooling requirement, higher lethality compared to CW.\r\n\r\nb.   J-band RF devices will be smaller in size and can be efficiently tailored for installation onboard naval platform.	DSensors	Draft	\N	19	Apr 22	-19-	\N	t	\N
