350004	637	2022-01-02 15:48:48	\r\n1.   Change in The Scope of Project. The project scope has been revised in VCNS IHD meeting, vide reference PN/ NDR DIV/ R AND D DTE/03/3240447 dated 05 Oct 21. Operating range of UCAV is limited to 200 km and BLOS operation requirements are eliminated. In this regard, SATCOM and EOIR systems are also removed from the scope. The timeline is also revised to 18 months. Following documents have been submitted in lines with the requirement of IHD meeting:\r\n\r\na.   Revised timeline and itemized cost vide letter PN/DG NRDI/ R AND D Wing/03/11125889 dated 02 November\r\n\r\nb.   Itemized cost estimates for procurement plan and pertinent details related to procurement source vide reference PN/DG NRDI/ At PNS JAUHAR/03/11526644 dated 29 Nov 21. \r\n\r\nc.   Combine draft work order amounting to PKR 238M and corresponding technical and budgetary proposal vide letter PN/DG NRDI/At JAUHAR/03/11715770 dated 10 Dec 21\r\n\r\n\r\n2.   Critical Design of UCAV. Study on selection of actuators for control surfaces and landing gear is being undertaken. Electrohydraulic servo valve systems are being considered to implement a fully redundant control system for control surfaces. Upon conclusion of study, quotations will be requested from vendors for relevant components/systems. Circuit design of fuel supply system is completed. Design of linkage for retraction mechanism of landing gear is in progress. Actuators for control surfaces and landing gear will be selected after design studies are completed. \r\n\r\n3.   Test Bench for ROTAX Engine. Construction of test bench along with integration of mechanical and electrical components has been completed. Custom designed instrument panel for monitoring engine parameters during testing has also been completed. A gascolator was required for the fuel circuit in order to filter the fuel before reaching the engine. This component was not available earlier, but it has been procured as it became available. Integration of this component has been completed as well. Final QC and safety checks will be carried out and the ROTAX engine will be started in Jan 22.\r\n\r\n4.   Mission Computer Test Bench. Study on algorithms for mission computer is ongoing and development of algorithm will follow the conclusion of study. Integration of sensors with available flight controller will be carried out and different interfaces available (CAN, RS232, RS485, GPIO) will be used to integrate sensors.\r\n\r\n5.   Machine Shop. Initial survey for the onboarding of Hartford CNC has been carried out by M/s DTS. Requirements for air compressor have been raised. An external enclosed area will be designated outside machine shop for the compressor. Design of enclosure is in progress based on recommended dimensions and specifications. A curing oven for the manufacturing of large parts has been designed in-house. Design specifications have been forwarded to vendor and item has been designed. Initial QC will be carried out once oven is ready.\r\n\r\n6.   Team development. In-house interviews for hardware design engineers have been conducted and suitable candidates for hiring have been shortlisted.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-01-04 14:45:29	25	Dec 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
