350013	252	2020-11-09 14:58:28	1.   The pending export license from Germany for Profi tracker to be used in Directional Antenna Director (DAD) has been recently issued. EDD is mid Nov 20. \r\n\r\n2.   Following activities were undertaken in the development of Radome for housing GT&RS. \r\n\r\n   a.   Radome composite lay-up for 1st batch is completed at Serial Production Facility (SPF). Sanding/refining of slices for Paint job is completed. Bolts and connectors have been procured to assemble the individual slices. Assembly of slices will be completed by early Nov 20.\r\n\r\n   b.   A test has been conducted successfully to ensure the communication between VTS Transmitter and Receiver while shielding receiver with radome.\r\n\r\n3.   Following activities were undertaken in the development of tower at RDS NATHIAGALI for mounting Ground Tracking and Receiving Station (GT&RS).\r\n\r\n   a.   INTELL team visited the installation site at RDS NATHIAGALI on 10 Oct 20 along with local vendor for analysis of Radome tower base construction  in lines with NRDI INTELL design.\r\n\r\n   b.   A reminder has been sent vide letter PN/NCW/03/2539023 dated 15 Oct 20 in sequel to previous letter PN/NCW/03/2490723 dated 16 Sep 20 for ensuring the existing load bearing capacity of ELINT station along with the review of proposed Radome installation design. The response received vide NHQ Letter PN/DWCE/03/2551311 dated 20 Oct 20 mentioning that the structural drawings & specifications of the existing ELINT station are not available. Therefore, NRDI INTELL should mount GT&RS Radome on a dedicated tower in vicinity of ELINT station at RDS NATHIAGALI. Consequently the design at the newer location as proposed is finalized. The construction will kick off shortly.\r\n\r\n4.   Vans modification to house VTS receiving station for ISR Operations. The modified van along with all the installed equipment is received from the local vendor. The INTELL team has successfully tested the modifications and functionality of the equipment installed in the van. The field trials of the van are planned in near future.\r\n\r\n5.   LoS VTS airborne unit installation onboard MPA ATR. In-house designed transmitter rack and GPS Radome manufactured by AED workshops have been received at serial production facility. The response from DNAM Dte is still awaited for the qualification of VTS transmission in the vicinity of installed ESM detectors on board marinized ATRs as requested vide PN/HQ COMPAK/03/6522890 dated 08 Sep 20.\r\n\r\n6.   GPS Parser development. \r\n\r\n   a.   GT&RS. GPS Parser PCBs and casing for GT&RS have been developed from the local industry in lines with NRDI INTELL designs.  \r\n\r\n   b.   Vehicle. GPS Parser PCBs fabrication for modified van in lines with INTELL design is under progress. EDD is early Nov 20.\r\n\r\n7.   Video Streaming Server (VSS) casing development. In-house designed casing has been developed to house Video Streaming Server (VSS). The NRDI INTELL developed VSS casing is handed over to C4I department at Dockyard on 21 Oct 20. The VSS casing was tested successfully during recent LWF coverage in Oct 20. \r\n\r\n8.   Live Weapon Firing (LWF). The INTELL team provided coverage during LWF on 27 Oct 20 at RDS MIANWALI. The following are the activities involved during LWF:\r\n\r\n   a.   The newly developed Transmitter unit was installed on nominated LRMP for LWF coverage. Ground & Aerial trials were conducted successfully. \r\n\r\n   b.   The two newly developed Receiver units were also tested successfully.	DSensors	Finalized	2020-11-11 10:33:24	25	Oct 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350012	743	2022-06-04 05:38:09	1.   Acquisition of Environmental data. The NRDI team retrieves the environmental data from PN Ship/vessel from the deployed data loggers on monthly basis. NRDI INTELL team also replaces battery packs of the data loggers during the retrieval activity to ensure continued operation. The data will be acquired by NRDI team upon availability of the PN Ship/vessel, request for said activity has been made vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12124832 dated 18 Jan 2022. \r\n\r\n2.   Historical Database Development. A historical database is being developed to record the acquired environmental and NDT data from PN ships/vessels. The database is being analyzed at NRDI. Subsequently, data analytics is being performed on the database for estimation of degradation parameters. Data provided by FMG was not suitable; the same has been communicated to the PoC for rectification vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12119861 dated 18 Jan 2022. The availability of PN platforms to perform data acquisition activity by NRDI team in the presence of FMG reps is requested vide reference PN/NRDI/ R AND D WING/03/12449213 dated 21 Feb 22.\r\n\r\n3.   Implementation of RUL Prediction Algorithms on Historical Database (MS-5). A detailed report on “Implementation of RUL Prediction Algorithms on historical database” has been submitted on 10 Jan 22 according to milestone 5 of the project. A presentation on the same was requested by NCMA vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12240914 dated 01 Feb 22. Subsequently, a detailed presentation was given in a meeting between NRDI NDT & Reliability Engineering Center, NCMA and FMG teams, held at NRDI INTELL on 21 Feb 22 vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12499265 dated 22 Feb 22.  Queries from NCMA on delivered presentation was received vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12629885 dated 04 Mar 22. Detailed response on raised queries was provided by NRDI vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12737531 dated 11 Mar 22. Further clarification on milestone 5 report was again requested by NCMA vide letter PN/NCMA/03/12744668 dated 14 Mar 22. Further details were forwarded vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12766316 dated 15 Mar 22 in which diligent reading of work order is requested. Further clarification was requested by NCMA w.r.t understanding of milestone 5 report vide letter PN/NCMA/03/12816140 dated 18 Mar 22. The itemized response on each point was forwarded vide PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12898610 dated 25 Mar 22. Subsequently, NCMA has forwarded the response to FMG ME, FMG WE and GM RD and TA for feedback vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12958496 dated 31 Mar 22. To expedite the acceptance of milestone 5, a meeting (chaired by DILS) was conducted on 26 May 22 at NCMA to discuss way forward on acceptance of M-5 vide reference PN/NCMA/03/133442109 dated 24 May 22. NCMA recommended that payment against M-5 “Implementation of RUL Prediction Algorithms on Historical Database” be approved to facilitate smooth progress of R&D project vide reference PN/NCMA/03/13367096 dated 26 May 22.\r\n\r\n4.   Non-Availability of PN platforms for Data Acquisition. During the conduct of said project, sufficient historical data could not be collected by FMG teams due non availability of PN platforms. Following references are relevant is this regard. Recently, tentative sea program for ZULF/SHMR was requested by NCMA for boarding of NRDI team vide PN/NCMA/03/13371602 dated 27 May 22.\r\n\r\na.   PN/HQ COMPAK/03/12879578 dated 24 Mar 22\r\nb.   PN/NCMA/03/12878153 dated 24 Mar 22\r\nc.   PN/DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11285138 dated 12 Nov 21\r\nd.   PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12008222 dated 06 Jan 22\r\n\r\n5.   Extension in Project Timeline.\r\n\r\na.   A case for extension of the project for 06 months is suggested after acceptance of milestone 5 and subject to availability of PN platforms vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12655448 dated 21 Mar 22. The same has not been acceded to vide NHQ letter PN/ILS Dte /03/3616326 dated 25 Mar 22. \r\n\r\nb.   Recently, it was informed that the PN platforms are not available for data acquisition activity until end May 22 due Ops dictates. It is therefore requested to revisit the decision pertaining to six-month timeline extension vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13038794 dated 09 Apr 22. \r\n\r\nc.   6 months extended revised timeline has been forwarded to NHQ vide reference PN/HQ NRDI/ R AND D WING/03/13389071 dated 30 May 22 due non-availability of PN platforms owing to various operational commitments.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-08-02 23:16:01	25	May 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350004	740	2022-06-04 05:51:06	1.   Change in The Scope of Project. The project scope has been revised in VCNS IHD meeting, vide reference PN/ NDR DIV/ R AND D DTE/03/3240447 dated 05 Oct 21. Operating range of UCAV is limited to 200 km and BLOS operation requirements are eliminated. In this regard, SATCOM and EOIR systems are also removed from the scope. The timeline is also revised to 18 months. Following documents have been submitted in lines with the requirement of IHD meeting:\r\n\r\na.   Revised timeline and itemized cost were forwarded vide letter PN/DG NRDI/ R AND D Wing/03/11125889 dated 02 Nov 21.\r\n\r\nb.   Itemized cost estimates for procurement plan and pertinent details related to procurement source was forwarded vide reference PN/DG NRDI/ At PNS JAUHAR/03/11526644 dated 29 Nov 21. \r\n\r\nc.   Combined draft work order amounting to PKR 238M and corresponding technical and budgetary proposal were forwarded vide letter PN/DG NRDI/At JAUHAR/03/11715770 dated 10 Dec 21.\r\n\r\n2.   Phase-II Work Order. Work order for phase 2 is still awaited. Earliest issuance of WO is requested in order to retain the trained project HR. \r\n\r\n3.   Critical Design of UCAV. Study on selection of actuators for control surfaces and landing gear is underway. Electrohydraulic servo valve systems are being considered to implement a fully redundant control system for control surfaces. Upon conclusion of study, quotations will be requested from vendors for relevant components/systems. Design for integration of fuel circuit and engine into airframe is underway. Design of linkage for retraction mechanism of landing gear is also in progress. Actuators for control surfaces and landing gear will be selected after design studies are completed. \r\n\r\n4.   Test Bench for ROTAX Engine. Construction of test bench along with integration of mechanical and electrical components has been completed. Custom designed instrument panel for monitoring engine parameters during testing has also been completed. A gascolator which is required for the fuel circuit in order to filter the fuel before reaching the engine has also been procured. Design of Bowden cable and throttle control mechanism has also been completed and manufacturing of components will be initialized in Jan ’22. Final QC and safety checks will be carried out once manufactured parts are received. Addition of engine oil, oil purging and cooling system setup has been carried out. Fuel circuit integration, pressure testing of oil system and turbo synchronization has also been carried out. Additionally, instrument panel has been powered on and sensor values, fuel pump operation etc. have been verified. Engine start up is planned in Jun 22.\r\n\r\n5.   Machine Shop. Hartford CNC has been received at serial production facility and placed in the designated area.  Commissioning of the CNC has been completed. Compressor is also procured and installed in a purpose built enclosure. A plasma cutter from M/s Avid CNC has also been procured. Commissioning of this machine has been completed and initial testing/operation will be carried out in Jun 22. Moreover, an in-house designed curing oven has also been procured and installed on site. Commissioning of PLC based control system for the oven is now underway. On-site testing of oven has been initiated; the same will be concluded in Jun 22.\r\n\r\n6.   Team development. Hiring of individuals is in process. In-house interviews for some candidates for hardware design engineers hve been conducted.\r\n\r\n7.   Shifting of SPF. Serial Production Facility (SPF)/ Manufacturing Facility (MF), which is presently located in E-type house in NORE-IV is required to be shifted to an alternate site on ops immediate basis due to delays in construction of NRDI complex. CNS has suggested to evaluate feasibility of shifting the SPF/MF in drill shed of PNS BAHADUR. The proposed option has been analyzed and found feasible for shifting of NRDI SPF/MF to drill shed of BAHADUR. The proposed site offer cost effective and efficient solution to the challenge posed w.r.t space requirement to develop/assemble UAVs/UCAV. This availability of said facility was requested vide letter PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13355399 dated 26 May 22. Moreover, NAM div is also willing to offer an alternate space and information was requested in this regard. Views and comments of NAM div were solicited for alternate space vide Letter no. PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13411379 dated 02 Jun 22\r\n\r\n8.   Miscellaneous Studies.\r\n\r\na.   Air Drop Logistics Container (ADLC). URD for the development of ADLC, for safe carriage/ drop of essentially required spares / medical kits / SARs equipment etc. through PN fixed wing Platforms at extended ranges, is received from NHQ. Based on the URD, NRDI INTELL proposal comprising of technical approach, timeline and budgetary requirements is developed. The project requires wind tunnel testing of ADLC / store separation and airworthiness certification. Such wind tunnel testing capability is not available with in-country facilities; therefore, foreign wind tunnel facilities are being engaged for the conduct of testing. Additionally, PACA has been approached for pertinent airworthiness certification.\r\n\r\nb.   LUNA NG UAS. URD for in-country maintenance of LUNA NG is received from PN. In this project, repair / maintenance (preventive/ corrective) mechanisms & calibration protocol / methods will be devised. This will enhance LUNA NG UAS operational availability and eliminate OEM dependency in conduct of scheduled maintenance (ML 3/4). Preparation of NRDI INTELL proposal is under progress.\r\n\r\nc.   Scan Eagle Antenna. In-house development of datalink antenna for Ground Control Station (GCS) of Scan Eagle UAV is required. NRDI INTELL team visited PNS MAKRAN on 15 Apr 22 for undertaking technical feasibility required for Project Proposal Form (PPF) / URD w.r.t physical parameters, dimensions of antenna and associated accessories / connection requirements. Preparation of NRDI INTELL proposal is under progress. \r\n\r\nd.   Hawker Hunter. Duly signed PPF from DG NRDI has been forwarded to NHQ for further processing.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-08-02 23:16:08	25	May 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
