350005	571	2021-11-01 19:44:36	1.   Conclusion of First Work Order. The first work order has been successfully completed and the subsequent second work order is awaited. Upon issuance of this work order test benches for HSTD subsystem components will be developed, ILS/ documentation will be handed over and ground/ aerial tests will be conducted in lines with ATPs.\r\n\r\n2.   Design / Development Activities.\r\n\r\na.   MARLIN-01 UAV.  Airframe manufacturing, assembly, avionics/ control/ data link integration and testing activates are completed.  Ground tests of airframe, propulsion, data link and control system are also completed.\r\n\r\nb.   MARLIN-01 Backup. Manufacturing of an additional MARLIN-01 (as backup), is in the final stages. Machining of structural parts and curing of airframe skin are completed. Assembly of airframe and integration of avionics, control system assembly and painting work are also completed. Work is under progress on avionics cooling system.\r\n\r\nc.   UAV Launcher. Design and manufacturing of MARLIN-01 Launcher/ pneumatic circuit testing bench are complete. Design and assembly/ fitting of carriage deceleration and braking system is completed as well. Testing of braking system is also successful.\r\n\r\nd.   Jet Engine Testing. Bench testing of P220 Turbo jet engine (for MARLIN-01) has been conducted. The tests indicated requirement of improvement in intake duct design. Pertinent design improvement and manufacturing of modified intake are completed. Bench testing of engine with upgraded intake is also conducted and results are within acceptable margins. \r\n\r\ne.   Backup P220 Engine. Maiden testing of backup P220 engine (MARLIN-01 backup) is also successfully completed.\r\n\r\nf.   UAV Launcher Testing.   Initial testing of launcher with integrated control system and pneumatic circuit at low and medium pressure are completed. Field testing for dead weight and dummy UAV launcher are also planned at PN GHARO facility. Co-ordination for relevant permission is under progress.\r\n \r\ng.   Design of MARLIN-02 (full-scale HSTD). The design is being revised based on the learnings from design / manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01. Detailed design of airframe components and integration with launch / recovery systems are also completed. Integration of avionics systems, data link, control mechanism and modifications pertaining to propulsion system is under progress. \r\nh.   MARLIN-02 launcher. MARLIN-02 launcher is being re-designed based on the learning from design / development of MARLIN-01 Launcher. In this regard, imperative considerations are being given to weight reduction, ease of assembly and transportation. Design of cost-effective launcher angle positioning mechanism is also completed. Export of manufacturing drawings and market surveys for COTs items are under progress. \r\n\r\nj.   Material Testing. Destructive Testing (DT) of composite material samples are being carried out using PNEC and PCSIR equipment. Tensile tests and first phase of bending tests are completed. Manufacturing process is improved in lines with the test results. Bending tests of improved samples are under progress. Testing of different composite coring materials are planned and samples are being prepared to finalize MARLIN-02 coring scheme. \r\n\r\nk.   Wind Tunnel Testing. Computer Aided Design (CAD) model for development of testing model has been shared, as required by M/s DESTO.  Estimated of quotation & timeline of 190 working days is received from the firm. M/s DESTO has been requested to reduce timeline. Foreign WTT facilities are also being explored for the pertinent testing. \r\n\r\n3.   Hardware Procurement Status.\r\n\r\na.   Order is already placed for procurement of JetCat P-1000 (Germany based 1100N) turbo jet engine. Engine is ready at OEM facility while export license is being processed for shipment to Pakistan. EDD for the engine is Dec 21.\r\n\r\nb.   Veronte flight controller (of M/s Embention) excluding air antenna is received at INTELL NRDI. Individual components have been tested and radio link is established. Firmware update has also been received for tracker, which will be tested soon. Currently, development of controls for HSTD are being studied.\r\n\r\nc.   Material for finishing of MARLIN-01 UAV and Launcher are being purchased/ procured as per requirement of manufacturing standards.\r\n\r\nd.   Orders are placed for raw material & COTs items for MARLIN-02 UAV and Launcher. The procurement is under progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-02 11:35:41	25	Oct 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	573	2021-11-01 19:45:05	\r\n1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Small Scale Weapon Demonstration. \r\n\r\n(1)   Demonstration of the irreversible damage caused on an electronic circuit through combined power of 02x 1 kW magnetrons is being planned. Casing to house waveguide setup of both magnetrons has been developed. QC of casing has also been completed.\r\n\r\n(2)   Suitable location has been selected for weapon demonstration at RDS NATHIAGALI AOR. The demonstration will be conducted with adequate safeties in place, for which QC sheets have been prepared.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Power Amplifier. Biasing circuit PCB has been redesigned with adequate track width suitable for high drain current. Matching networks of 100Watt amplifier have been redesigned employing Simplified Real Frequency Technique (SRFT). Layout design of amplifier is in progress.\r\n\r\n2.   Following procurement actions are in progress to undertake required experimentation. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement Completed. Experimental components including 1 kW magnetrons, coaxial circulators/terminations, Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs, FPGA boards, Spectrum Analyzer, Switch Mode Power Supplies, 1 kW waveguide terminations, N52 magnets, Oscilloscope, 2.5 kW waveguide terminations, E-field probe, Signal Generator, and DC power supply have been completed. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in Progress. Procurement of high-power refractory material is completed. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Following studies are being conducted to formulate research plans for combination of X-band magnetrons in ensuing years: \r\n\r\na.   A pulsed power supply based on Pulsed Forming Networks (PFN) required to drive pulsed magnetrons is currently being designed.\r\n\r\nb.   Preliminary design of RF devices including circulators and directional couplers at X-band (9 GHz) has been finalized.\r\n\r\n4.   Technical proposal amounting PKR 260M for Phase II pertaining to power combination of multiple J-band pulsed magnetrons of redundant AM-39 has been submitted to NHQ for approval. \r\na.   An anechoic RF chamber will be designed and fabricated to enable shielded high-power testing of the magnetron combination experiment with adequate safety measures. \r\n\r\nb.   Civil Works are required for development of a test site to carry-out the high-power microwave experiments with 25 kW pulsed magnetrons. The proposed test site will be developed, comprising of an experimentation room with adequate concrete wall thickness to ensure minimal penetration of the EM waves. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n5.   Miscellaneous Study. \r\n\r\na.   EMC/EMI Survey. Upon directions of HQ COMLOG, GM RD&TA approached NRDI R&D Wing to conduct EMC/EMI survey to finalize antenna location onboard PNS ALAMGIR vide letter No. PN/PN Dockyard/PE AND D WING/ GM(RD AND  TA)/03/7895873 dated 06 Jan 21. The required E-field probe has been procured. Frequency compatible antennas are required for testing, which are currently being finalized. Test procedures for Radiated Emission tests RE-102 and RE-103; Conducted Emission tests CE-101 and CE-102; Conducted Susceptibility Tests CS-101, CS-114, CS-116; and Radiated Susceptibility Tests RS-103 have been finalized. Point Recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nb.   SR-60 Study. RF team visited PN ship and conducted survey to determine functional replacement of the SR-60 RADAR antenna. PPF form is awaited from NHQ. Point Recommended to be dropped.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-02 11:35:47	25	Oct 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350011	608	2021-12-31 10:12:44	1.   URD Finalization. Comments and queries on technical proposal of Chinese VTOL CSC-005H have been forwarded by NRDI INTELL, vide letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/10909376 dated 18 Oct 21, to help in URD finalization. Also, financial proposal of the same is requested for better evaluation of the Chinese VTOL. Requirement by Ops branch binge reviewed at NHQ.	DR&D	Finalized	2021-12-31 10:12:53	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
350013	669	2022-03-03 15:09:31	\r\n1.   VTS qualification in vicinity of ESM Detectors onboard PN ATR. M/s RAS highlighted that the high-power density and E-Field of LoS VTS transmission will affect the performance of onboard ESM system. It is recommended that both systems should not be operated simultaneously to ensure smooth operation. The same recommendation has been forwarded to NHQ vide letter PN/DGNRDI/RANDDWING/03110878134 dated 15 Oct 21. Point recommended to be dropped. \r\n\r\n2.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI. The civil work required for installation of GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI, undertaken by M/s FAST team, has been completed successfully. Tower construction, Radome mounting on tower, GT&RS equipment installation, integration of Directional Antenna Director (DAD) system and testing activities have been successfully completed. The GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI is made fully operational as reported vide reference PN/ NRDI/ R AND D WING/ 03/12348866 dated 11 Feb 22. Trial was conducted with P3C MPA on 10 Feb 22 and smooth video received with a range over 100NM. Subsequently, the same is being used in ongoing ISR missions.\r\n\r\n3.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS MIANWALI. Site proposed by NRDI INTELL at RDS MIANWALI for installation of Antenna Radome was not recommended by HQ COMCOAST, being close to the edge of the cliff vide letter PN / HQ COASTAL COMMAND /03/11311292 dated 16 Nov 21. HQ COMCOAST suggested 02 x alternate sites near Defcom building for the installation of said system. However, the alternate sites proposed by the HQ COMCOAST are not considered feasible as receiving system will be subjected to blanking due to higher terrain on seaward side. HQ COMCOAST has been requested to review the site proposed by NRDI vide PN/ DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11409842 dated 30 Nov 21. NHQs has been requested to pursue approval vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12557270 dated 25 Feb 22.\r\n\r\n\r\n4.   GT&RS Location Finalization for NAS TURBAT. Identification of suitable site (Roof top of Admin Block) for installation of GT&RS at NAS TURBAT under Project Raven-I has been forwarded vide letter PN/HQ COMNAV/03/12508931 dated 24 Feb 22. Upon concurrence by field (MES Authorities) regarding feasibility and load bearing capacity of the proposed site, permanent installation will be undertaken.  \r\n\r\n5.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at GWADAR. All construction works at GWADAR Hammerhead have been halted due to some cracks being observed, as informed vide letter PN / HQ COASTAL COMMAND /03/11311292 dated 16 Nov 21. NRDI INTELL has requested HQ COMCOAST to share the report pertaining to Geo Hazard study of the area, if available, to evaluate the alternate suitable location vide reference PN/ DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11409842 dated 30 Nov 21. NHQs has been requested to pursue approval vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12557270 dated 25 Feb 22.\r\n\r\n6.   Timeline amendment milestones. Pertaining to delays in case file approvals, NHQs has been requested to expedite amendment of milestones timeline by M/s MTSS vide letter MTSS/20/42 dated 09 Feb 22. A request to expedite approval for smooth execution of the project was also sent by NRDI INTELL vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12551993 dated 25 Feb 22. \r\n\r\n7.   ISR Mission Activity. Owing to volatile security situation in Baluchistan, NRDI INTELL team as directed vide NHQ letter No PN/ NCW (TECH)/ 03/ 3506199 dated 04 Feb 22 established Ty GT&RS setup at PNS MAKRAN and PNS SIDDIQ for live video relay from P3C to COCs, with effect from 5 Feb 22. NRDI INTELL team has successfully installed temporary setups of GT&RS at both sites, however the teams engaged for the said purpose mainly comprises of project contractual civilian research officers (ROs) and research technicians (RTs), along with PN officers. NRDI INTELL requested DA and PNCA for nomination of service personnel for on job training of the LOS VTS system vide letter PN/ NRDI/ R AND D WING/ 03/ 12424979 dated 17 Feb 22, to facilitate subsequent takeover of the system. The nomination of service personnel was received from DA vide letter PN/ Drafting Authority/03/12500297 dated 22 Feb 22. The OJT is currently in progress at PNS SIDDIQ and PNS MAKRAN. In addition, LOS VTS transmitter system was installed by NRDI ITNELL team on PC86 MPA (3rd aircraft) for the subject activity, vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/03/ 12267923 dated 5 Feb 22.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-03-30 08:52:51	25	Feb 22	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	348	2021-03-01 16:13:52	1.   During the reporting period, research focus was laid on preparation for experimentation in which power output of two S-band 1 KW magnetrons will be combined. Project experimentation based on injection locking experimentation of a single magnetron will first be carried out to validate simulated results. \r\n\r\n2.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation preparation were carried out:\r\n \r\na.   Control System Designing for Frequency Pushing.\r\n\r\n(1)   A new control circuit PCB for frequency locking of the magnetron has been designed with requisite modifications in values of the loop filter components and OPAMP stages. The new PCB will also house an onboard microcontroller for efficient programming of the PLL IC.\r\n\r\n(2)   Procured Switch Mode Power Supplies will be used to excite the magnetron in frequency locked mode. In the default configuration, the onboard IGBT controller board optimizes the magnetron’s frequency response with respect to the magnetron’s load. The existing controller board will be replaced with an indigenously developed controller board which adjusts the magnetron’s frequency response with respect to a control voltage. Requisite modifications in the power supply are currently in progress.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Devices. Following in-house design and development of RF devices has been completed: \r\n(1)   Waveguide circulators. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks and high power magnets. High Power Testing of the fabricated circulators is being planned. Fabrication of x02 circulators and x04 directional couplers has been completed. VNA Testing revealed satisfactory results.\r\n(2)   Waveguide directional couplers. High power testing of waveguide directional couplers is being undertaken.\r\n(3)   Waveguide Termination. Design and development, as well as multiphysics thermal simulation of high power waveguide termination based on wedged scheme has been completed. Testing is in progress.\r\n(4)   Phase Shifter. A 360o Phase Shifter was procured and has been tested on VNA with satisfactory results. The phase shifter will be used in phase matching of the response signals of two injection locked magnetrons in order to accomplish effective power combining. In-house design of phase shift is also completed, and fabrication is in progress.\r\n\r\n\r\nc.   RF Power Amplifier. \r\n\r\n(1)   In-house design optimization of 100 Watt power amplifier (PA) has been completed. Soldering of components on manufactured PCB has been completed, and required heat sink is fabricated. \r\n\r\n(2)   QC sheets for safe testing of the designed and developed RF PA has also been prepared. Procurement of 100 Watt MOSFET has been completed. \r\n\r\n(3)   Gate biasing circuit has been designed to ensure controlled safe testing and operation of the 100 Watt depletion mode transistor. PCB manufacturing of the same is in progress.\r\n\r\n(4)   Three stages of the Preamplifier are required for requisite RF power input to the 100 Watt MOSFET. All stages of the preamplifier circuits have been designed. Procurement of IC and pertinent components is in progress. Fabrication of PCBs is also in progress.\r\n\r\n(5)   A 30 Watt PA for 2.45 GHz has been designed that can be used in place of stage 2 and stage 3 of pre-amplifier. \r\n\r\n3.   Following procurement actions are in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement Completed. Experimental components including 1 kW magnetrons, coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs, FPGA boards and Switch Mode Power Supplies have been completed.\r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in Progress. Procurement of analog ring mixer, waveguide terminations, E-field probe, Oscilloscope and DC power supply is in progress. Due COVID-19 pandemic and Chinese New Year, delay is expected in delivery of these components.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-03-04 11:20:09	25	Feb 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
250003	621	2021-12-31 12:31:12	1.   Competent authority has approved indigenous development of STLT at a cost of Rs 34.68M vide PN/NRD Div/TD DTE/01/2176376.\r\n\r\n2.     Requirement of funds during CFY has been forwarded to NHQ vide PI letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/6894086 dated 09 Oct 2020.  Amount of Rs 12.5 Million has been approved for 2020-2021 as per the verbal information shared by concerned authority.  However, request for enhancement/ revision of funds to cater for MTSS/ PNBA / Bahria Foundation share has also been forwarded to NHQ. PI letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/8641220 dated 11 March 2021 refers. \r\n\r\n3.    Project team has visited the submarine installed at Pakistan Maritime museum on 19 Jan 2021, for awareness and understanding of Submarine assembly and its functionality. Team has also visited STC and Navigation School on 21 Jan 2021 and observed various simulators installed at STC/ Navigation School. Meeting of Director ET with MTSS team was held to brief them about the scope and modalities of the project. \r\n\r\n4.   Draft Work Order and Technical Proposal of STLT has been forwarded to MTSS.\r\n\r\n5.   MTSS HQ, after due process at its end, has forwarded the work order to NHQ for further necessary action.\r\n\r\n6.  Some very basic work has been initiated using VR Headset.\r\n\r\n7.  T0 yet to be established. Development work will be initiated upon availability of allocated funds.\r\n\r\n8.  Meeting chaired by VCNS was held on 14 Sep 21 MoM and subsequent decisions regarding STLT work order are awaited.\r\n\r\n9.  Minutes of meeting as mentioned vide para 8/N, has been received vide reference PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3240447 dated 05 Oct 2021.\r\n\r\n10. As per Para 12-C of MoM of IHD held On 14 SEP 2021, Development of STLT may be considered after development of Virtual Reality (VR) Center.\r\n\r\n11. RDW has initiated a letter w.r.t processing of VRC and STLT cases separately. RDW letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/11015633 dated 27 Oct 21 is relevant in this regard. Salient of the letter are provided below:\r\na.   VR based STLT is an ops requirement raised by STC and supported by COMPAK Command being the end user. \r\nb.   Current basic VR facility at R&D Wing (i.e an extension of VA Lab at PG Block of PNS JAUHAR) is ready to develop STLT simulator. Therefore, STLT and VRC may be processed as separate projects, independent of each other. \r\nc.   Budgetary proposal of VRC mainly includes hardware infrastructure. Whereas, VR based projects like STLT mostly covers processing and delivery equipment along-with HR requirement with an aim to enhance capacity and capability. \r\nd.   DSMO, being Sponsoring Dte, may be approached for processing and issuance of STLT Work Order as per procedure in vogue. \r\ne.   In parallel, relevant sponsoring directorate may be approached for processing of funds and work order issuance for VRC Project.  In this regard, draft PPF and URD have also been shared with Dir R&D.\r\n\r\n12.     STLT PPF and URD, as forwarded by Dir STC through COMKAR has been received after signature by DCNS(O).  D Rand D letter PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3364653 dated 3 Dec refers in this regard. The same, duly recommended by DG NRDI, has been forwarded to ACNS (NRD) at NHQ on 7 Dec 21 for further processing. RDW Letter PN/DG NRDI/At PNS JAUHAR/03/11643713 dated 7 Dec refers in this regard.	DEnab	Finalized	2022-01-04 14:44:32	25	Dec 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
