350003	304	2020-12-30 12:00:00	1.   During the reporting period, research focus was laid on preparation for experimentation in which power output of two S-band 1KW magnetrons will be combined. Project experimentation based on injection locking experimentation of a single magnetron will first be carried out to validate simulated results. \r\n\r\n2.   Following activities pertaining to in-house design and development were carried out:\r\n \r\na.   Control System Designing for Frequency Pushing.\r\n\r\n(1)   PCB fabrication of control circuit PCB based on PLL IC, required for frequency locking has been completed, and testing is in progress.\r\n\r\n(2)   Design of control circuitry required for phase matching of magnetron response with the phase of injection signal is in progress.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Devices. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks, and waveguide directional couplers, are required in project experimentation. As limited funds have been released, in-house design and development of RF devices is in progress whereas industrial grade high power magnets required for biasing ferrite disks in waveguide circulators are being procured.\r\n\r\n(1)   Fabrication of x01 waveguide circulator and x01 directional coupler has been completed for preliminary design verification. The waveguide components were tested on VNA; and observed results were found to match well with computer simulations, and hence, were declared satisfactory. Fabrication of x04 circulators has been completed whereas fabrication of x03 directional couplers is in progress.\r\n\r\n(2)   Fabrication of x03 waveguide adapters is completed, and VNA testing has revealed satisfactory results.\r\n\r\nc.   RF Power Amplifier. \r\n\r\n(1)   In-house design optimization of 100 Watt power amplifier (PA) has been completed. Soldering of components on manufactured PCB has also been completed, and required heat sink has been fabricated. \r\n\r\n(2)   QC sheets for safe testing of the designed and developed RF PA has also been prepared. Procurement of 100 Watt MOSFET is in progress. Gate biasing circuit is also being designed to ensure controlled safe testing of the depletion mode transistor. \r\n\r\n(3)   Three stages of the Preamplifier are required for requisite RF power input to the 100 Watt MOSFET. Stage 2 of the pre-amplifier has been designed, while stage 1 and stage 3 are in progress. Procurement of IC and pertinent components is also in progress. \r\n\r\n3.   Following procurement actions are also in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement completed. Experimental components including 1 kW magnetrons, coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs and FPGA boards have been completed.\r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in progress. Procurement of analog ring mixer, waveguide terminations, phase shifter ICs and programmable switch mode power supplies is in progress. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n?	DSensors	Finalized	2021-01-06 12:53:39	25	Dec 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
