350004	306	2020-12-30 12:04:49	1.   Critical Design of UCAV. Studies on airfoils for wings and empennage are underway and required lift/drag characteristics are being used to select the best candidates for wings and empennage. \r\n\r\n2.   Procurement of engine for UCAV is also planned and will be initiated by mid Jan 21.\r\n\r\n3.   Data Links. A long range data link, with built-in OFDM video, RC and telemetry transmission from M/s TAISYNC is being procured. This data link will provide transmission distance of upto 30 km. Procurement will be initiated in early January.\r\n\r\n4.   Scaled Down UCAV Model (GANNET)\r\n\r\na.   Taxi Runs. Multiple taxi runs have been carried out for GANNET in controlled trials to verify the avionics setup and the stability of the airframe. During initial trials, it was found that the stability of the landing gear needs improvement. \r\n\r\nb.   The mounting points of the landing gear were upgraded and a marked improvement in the stability of airframe, even at full speed taxi runs.\r\n\r\nc.   Data links. Range improvement of existing COTS data links commonly used with flight controllers was carried out through the development of in-house antennas for L-band frequencies. These high-gain antennas were used to increase the output power of the RC transmitter (X9D) and the ground telemetry receiver (RFD 900). A custom pedestal was designed and developed to combat mutual interference between the in-house developed antennas. \r\n\r\nd.   Way Forward. Preparations are underway to carry out first flight of GANNET at GHARO site. A 50m-by-50m area of land is being prepared for take-off and landing during the planned flight operations in collaboration with NSOTC. Flight plans have been developed for the testing and tuning flight parameters, and trials will be conducted by early January. \r\n\r\n5.   Machine Shop. The design of Machine Shop is finalized. The construction is expected to begin by early January. Following machinery is under procurement.\r\n\r\n6.   Team development. Hiring of additional engineers has been initiated to further develop the capabilities of HR at INTELL lab. 01 Research Engineer will join the UAV team on 1st January, 2021.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-01-06 12:54:45	25	Dec 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
