350004	325	2021-02-01 10:54:44	1.   Critical Design of UCAV. CAD modelling of fuselage, including placement of avionics components has been initiated. Weight distribution of fuselage components will be finalized once component placement has been completed.\r\n\r\n2.   Procurement of engine for UCAV is under process and order will be placed by mid-Feb 21. Fresh quotations and specifications for avionics components such as mission computer, flight controller and SATCOM are also being enquired from vendors.\r\n\r\n3.   Scaled Down UCAV Model (GANNET)\r\n\r\na.   Gannet Flight Trials. Trials have been planned for flight of GANNET and will be carried out once 50-by-50 m area of land has been prepared at GHARO site for take-off and landing. Tuning of Proportional, Integral and derivative (PID) gains will be carried out and flight controller will be calibrated for autonomous operations. Trials will be conducted in Feb 21.\r\n\r\nb.   Data links. Range improvement of existing COTS data links commonly used with flight controllers was carried out through the development of in-house antennas for L-band frequencies. Testing of this setup will be carried out along with flight trials of GANNET in Feb 21. \r\n\r\n4.   Machine Shop. Construction of Machine Shop is underway and will be completed by end of Feb 21. A Prusa Mk III 3D printer and Wegstr desktop CNC have been acquired. Calibration of both pieces of equipment has been completed and initial jobs have been carried out. HAAS CNC could not be procured due export restrictions imposed by Canadian government. Procurement process for alternate CNC machine has been initiated.\r\n\r\n5.   Team development. Hiring of additional engineers has been initiated to further develop HR strength at INTELL. Review of CVs is underway to shortlist suitable candidates.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-02-17 09:25:16	25	Jan 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	326	2021-02-01 10:54:53	1.   During the reporting period, research focus was laid on preparation for experimentation in which power output of two S-band 1KW magnetrons will be combined. Project experimentation based on injection locking experimentation of a single magnetron will first be carried out to validate simulated results. \r\n\r\n2.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation preparation were carried out:\r\n \r\na.   Control System Designing for Frequency Pushing.\r\n\r\n(1)   The control circuit was tested to frequency lock a low power VCO by stabilizing frequency control voltage. The testing results revealed required modifications in values of the loop filter components and OP-AMP stages. A new PCB is now being designed with these modifications. The new PCB will also house an onboard microcontroller for efficient programming of the PLL IC.\r\n\r\n(2)   Design of control circuit PCB for matching of the magnetron with a reference oscillator frequency is also in progress. \r\n\r\nb.   RF Devices. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks, and waveguide directional couplers, are required in project experimentation. In-house design and development of RF devices is in progress whereas industrial grade high power magnets required for biasing ferrite disks in waveguide circulators are being procured.\r\n\r\n(1)   Fabrication of 01 x waveguide circulator and 01 x directional coupler has been completed for preliminary design verification. The waveguide components were tested on VNA and observed results were found to match well with computer simulations, and hence, were declared satisfactory. Fabrication of 04 x circulators has been completed whereas fabrication of 03 x directional couplers is in progress. Testing of the waveguide circulators is also in progress.\r\n\r\n(2)   Design of PCB for testing of phase shifter IC has been completed and testing is in progress.\r\n\r\n(3)   Design of high power waveguide termination based on inductive choke schemes has been completed. Thermal simulation and preparation of production drawings is in progress.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nc.   RF Power Amplifier. \r\n\r\n(1)   In-house design optimization of 100 Watt power amplifier (PA) has been completed. Soldering of components on manufactured PCB has also been completed and required heat sink has also been fabricated. \r\n\r\n(2)   QC sheets for safe testing of the designed and developed RF PA has also been prepared. Procurement of 100 Watt MOSFET has been completed. \r\n\r\n(3)   Gate biasing circuit has been designed to ensure controlled safe testing and operation of the 100 Watt depletion mode transistor. PCB manufacturing of the same is in progress.\r\n\r\n(4)   Three stages of the Preamplifier are required for requisite RF power input to the 100 Watt MOSFET. All stages of the preamplifier circuits have been designed. Procurement of IC and pertinent components is in progress. Fabrication of PCBs is also in progress.\r\n\r\n(5)   A 30 Watt PA for 2.45 GHz has also been designed that can be used in place of stage 2 and stage 3 of pre-amplifier. Procurement of the high power LDMOS and pertinent components is in progress. \r\n\r\n3.   Following procurement actions are also in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement completed. Experimental components including 1 kW magnetrons, coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs and FPGA boards have been completed.\r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in progress. Procurement of analog ring mixer, waveguide terminations, E-probe, and programmable switch mode power supplies is in progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-02-17 09:25:08	25	Jan 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
