350003	386	2021-04-27 09:24:46	1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation preparation were carried out:\r\na.   Control System Designing.\r\n\r\n(1)   The control circuit PCB for frequency locking of the injection signal source has been fabricated with requisite modifications in values of the loop filter components and OPAMP stages. The circuit board also includes an onboard microcontroller for efficient programming of the PLL IC. \r\n\r\n(2)   A new control circuit PCB for phase locking of the magnetron is being designed. The control circuit will enable phase control of the magnetron through a reference signal generator such as SDR.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Devices. Following in-house design, development and high power testing of RF devices is in progress: \r\n\r\n(1)   Waveguide circulators. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks and high power magnets are required in project experimentation. Fabrication of x02 circulators has been completed. VNA Testing revealed satisfactory results. The fabricated circulators were also tested at 1 kW and were declared satisfactory. The circulators are successfully being used in experimentation involving injection locking of a single 1 kW magnetron. Fabrication of x02 more circulators has been initiated which are required for injection locking of the second magnetron. \r\n\r\n(2)   Waveguide directional couplers. High power testing of waveguide directional couplers has been completed. Fabrication of x04 directional couplers have been completed. \r\n\r\n(3)   Waveguide Termination. Design as well as multiphysics thermal simulation of high power waveguide termination based on wedged scheme has been completed. \r\n\r\n(4)   Phase Shifter. IC for a 360o Phase Shifter has been procured, and the PCB has been fabricated. Testing of the phase shifter on VNA is in progress.\r\n\r\n(5)   Power Combiner. An H-plane power combiner is required for power combination of x02 1 kW magnetrons. Design of the power combiner is completed and multiphysics analysis is in progress. \r\n\r\nc.   Experimentations.\r\n\r\n(1)   High Power Testing of RF Devices. Testing of the in-house developed circulators and directional couplers has been completed at 1 kW. All RF devices performed satisfactorily at 1 kW. \r\n\r\n(2)   Injection Locking of a Single Magnetron. An experimental scheme was developed to accomplish injection locking of single magnetron. Experiments have been conducted with RF signal generator as injection source. The injection signal was fed to a free running magnetron through series of high power circulators. The bandwidth of the magnetron was observed to reduce within 10 Hz. Similar experiments will be planned with SDRs as injection sources, at different power levels. This will offer selection of an efficient injection source.\r\n\r\nd.   RF Power Amplifier. \r\n\r\n(1)   QC checks for safe testing of the designed and developed RF PA has also been completed. \r\n\r\n(2)   Procurement of IC and pertinent components along with fabrication of PCBs for 100 Watt MOSFET is completed.\r\n\r\n3.   Following procurement actions are in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement Completed. Procurement of switch mode power supplies, waveguide terminations and DC power supply have been completed.\r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in Progress. Procurement of waveguide terminations required for injection locking of the second magnetron, E-field probe and Oscilloscope is in progress. Due COVID-19 pandemic, delay is expected in delivery of these components.	DR&D	Finalized	2021-04-27 09:25:54	25	Mar 21	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
350004	387	2021-04-27 09:26:54	1.   Critical Design of UCAV. CAD modelling of fuselage, including placement of avionics components is in progress. Weight distribution of fuselage components will be finalized once component placement has been completed. Design of landing gear is in progress, with detailed analysis of components. \r\n\r\n2.   Austrian origin ROTAX 914 turbo engine has been procured. Design of engine test bench has been initiated. Further, a dedicated testing facility, at SPF, for this engine is also being designed to carry out in-depth testing. \r\n\r\n3.   Quotations and specifications for avionics components such as mission computer, flight controller, ELINT receiver, EO/IR devices and SATCOM are being enquired from vendors.\r\n\r\n4.   Scaled Down UCAV Model (GANNET).\r\n\r\na.   Gannet Flight Trials. Taxi trials have been carried out for GANNET at the PN GHARO facility. However, due to unavailability of designated landing strip, alternate facility is being evaluated to carry out flight trials. Tuning of Proportional, Integral and Derivative (PID) gains will be carried out during flight trials. Flight controller will also be calibrated for autonomous operations.\r\n\r\nb.   Data links. Range improvement of existing COTS data links commonly used with flight controllers was carried out through the development of in-house antennas for L-band frequencies. Testing of this setup has been carried out along with taxi trials. Further trials will be conducted along with flight trials of GANNET. \r\n\r\n5.   Machine Shop. Containers that will house the machine shop have been received at serial production facility. External structure has been completed, however, internal work is underway, including wiring, false ceiling etc. HAAS CNC could not be procured due export restrictions imposed by Canadian government. Procurement process for alternate CNC machine from M/s DOOSAN (South Korean OEM) has been initiated. Order for Lathe Machine, Drill Press, Lifter and Bench Grinder has also been placed.\r\n\r\n6.   Team development. Hiring of additional engineers and students has been initiated to further develop HR strength at INTELL. Final interviews of shortlisted candidates have been carried out and hiring is under process.	DR&D	Finalized	2021-04-27 09:28:38	25	Mar 21	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
350005	388	2021-04-27 09:29:53	1.   Design / Development Activities.\r\n\r\na.   Design activities of Scaled Down Model HSTD, named as MARLIN-01, are completed. Pattern machining, finishing and mold fabrication activities are also completed. Subsequently, the manufacturing of airframe is under progress.\r\n\r\nb.   Concrete flooring is constructed at Serial Production Facility (SPF) for composite layup and related manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01.\r\n\r\nc.   Design of MARLIN-02 (full scaled HSTD) is being revised based on the learnings from design / manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01. Detailed design of airframe is completed. Integration of avionics, launch and recovery systems are under progress.\r\n\r\nd.   Jet Engine Test Bench. Detailed designs of test bench for P-1000 and P-220 turbo jet engines are completed. Manufacturing of the test bench is under progress. SOPs and safety procedures are being drafted for subsequent engine testing at SPF. \r\n\r\ne.   UAV Launcher. Design and analysis activities of MARLIN-01 Launcher/ pneumatic circuit testing bench are complete. The assembling of UAV launcher mechanical parts is in progress at SPF. Leveled concrete flooring is also constructed at SPF for assembly and testing of MARLIN-01 launcher / pneumatic circuit test bench. \r\n\r\nf.   Design of MARLIN-02 launcher is being upgraded based on the knowledge from design / development of MARLIN-01 Launcher. In this regard, imperative consideration is given to weight reduction, ease of assembly and transportation. Local industry is engaged for the manufacturing of pneumatic actuator in lines with the INTELL design. \r\n\r\ng.   Material Testing. Destructive Testing (DT) of composite material samples is being carried out using PNEC and PCSIR equipment. The test results will furnish material strength data for consolidation of design and improvement of indigenous manufacturing quality.\r\n\r\nh.   Wind Tunnel Testing. DESTO was approached for the wind tunnel testing and experimental validation of performance parameters of HSTD. In this regards, detailed meetings held at DESTO office. Performance specification, design details and testing requirements of HSTD were furnished by NRDI INTELL team. Also, the feasibility of requisite testing was discussed in detail. Moreover, a Computer Aided Design (CAD) model, for development of testing model, is also shared as per the requirements of DESTO. The case is under processing at DESTO for timeline / quotation of model development & subsequent testing.\r\n\r\n2.   Hardware Procurement Status.\r\n\r\na.   Order is placed for procurement of JetCat P-1000 (Germany based 1100N) turbo jet engine. The procurement is under progress with EDD in Apr 21. \r\n\r\nb.   Order is placed for procurement of Veronte Flight controller of M/s Embention. The procurement is under progress with EDD in Apr 21.\r\n\r\nc.   JetCat P-220 (Germany based 220N) turbo jet engine for MARLIN-01 is procured.\r\n\r\nd.   Material for manufacturing of MARLIN-01 UAV are being purchased / procured as per the requirement of manufacturing under progress.	DR&D	Finalized	2021-04-27 09:30:28	25	Mar 21	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
