350002	98	2020-06-01 13:22:26	1.   Ruggedized UAV Jammer (Eagle Hunt-1)\r\n \r\n   a.   Work order for serial production of 10 jammers is still awaited. \r\n\r\n   b.   The proposed costing is based on project raw material. Therefore, the availability of funds prior three months before delivery of jammers is the requirement. \r\n\r\n   c.   The facility for serial production has been taken over by INTELL. Maintenance and renovation of labs for serial production will be undertaken partly in June 20 through make shift arrangements due to COVID-19 pandemic.\r\n\r\n2.   Reactive Jamming\r\n \r\n   a.   Equipment required for field trials received during Apr and May 2020. The received equipment is tested and being integrated in the ruggedized casing at INTELL.\r\n\r\n   b.   HORN Antenna developed as well as received and being tested at INTELL\r\n\r\n   c.   Long range field trials will be carried out during Jun – Jul 20 at GHARO site.\r\n\r\n3.   GPS Spoofig\r\n\r\n   a.   Testing is in progress for smooth implementation of Carry-Off Attack using the counterfeit GPS signals generated from Ephemeris predicted data.\r\n\r\n   b.   The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR is still awaited due to COVID 19 pandemic. The revised EDD is end Jun 20. Thereafter, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of GPS spoofing milestone upon receipt of requisite equipment.\r\n\r\n4.   Scaled-Down UCAV Model\r\n \r\n   a.   Manufacturing of tail has been completed. The finished surface have been installed with the ribs to provide the structural integrity. Tail servos have been installed inside the tail for controlling of control surfaces.\r\n\r\n   b.   Skin of wings have been completed. However completing the wings would require ribs to be sandwiched between the skins, which is soon to be undertaken\r\n\r\n   c.   Laser cutting and welding of engine test bench has been completed. Electronics setup of the test bench is in progress, after which the test bench will be able to provide thrust data (in grams) w.r.t. applied throttle, engine temperature and engine RPM\r\n\r\n   d.   Manufacturing of fuselage is to be undertaken along with CNC machining of nose landing gear mechanism in Jun 20.\r\n\r\n5.   Marinized Container to house Project Eagle Hunt equipmnt\r\n\r\nThe marinized container with EMI/EMC shielding received. Equipment for Reactive Jamming and GPS Spoofing will be integrated onboard container after field trials	DSensors	Cancelled	2020-06-02 09:34:06	20	May 20	-20-	\N	f	\N
