350003	138	2020-08-08 15:37:35	1.   GPP is completed and submitted. Milestones acceptance is received. Case is forwarded for funds disbursement.\r\n2.   Hiring is finalized and case file is under process at NRDI.\r\n\r\n3.   The aim of the project is to generate high power microwaves for directed energy weapon applications, through phase matching and power combining of multiple high power injection-locked magnetrons. Following activities have been undertaken during the current month:\r\n\r\na.   Magnetron Study. Commercially available microwave oven magnetrons were purchased to study operation and working principles. Magnetron cavity was first cut open at Serial Production Facility, following all required safety procedures. Dimensions were measured to reverse-engineer and simulate magnetron cavity.\r\n\r\nb.   Computed Aided Design (CAD). Magnetron cavity CAD model was developed for subsequent eigen-mode (frequency domain) and transient (Time-domain) analysis.\r\n\r\nc.   Frequency Domain Study  Eigenvalue analysis (frequency domain study) was performed and the resonating frequency was successfully computed to be 2.45 GHz.\r\n\r\nd.   Transient Analysis. Time domain transient analysis of the magnetron was performed using Multiphysics couplings and Particle in Cell (PiC) simulation. The resonating magnetron has been successfully analyzed as a free running oscillator at 2.45 GHz with 10 MHz working bandwidth.\r\n\r\ne.   Way Forward Multiphysics simulation study to model magnetron injection locking principle, will be undertaken to investigate locking bandwidth efficiency.\r\n\r\n4.   RF Devices.  High frequency RF devices including waveguide ferrite circulators, directional couplers and phase shifters are required to accomplish project experimentation. Indigenous design and fabrication of these devices are being undertaken. \r\na.   Electromagnetic & thermal multiphysics coupled modelling of waveguide ferrite circulators and directional couplers have been successfully completed. These devices will be fabricated in-house after purchasing required raw material.\r\nb.   Design of analog phase shifters required for phase matching of multiple magnetrons has been undertaken. Preliminary design study is completed. Advanced design and fabrication are currently pursued.\r\n\r\n5.   Power Amplifier. In-house design of 100W amplifier required for injection locking of magnetrons is completed. Fabrication is currently under process.\r\n\r\n6.   Anechoic Chamber. Full scale design and electromagnetic simulation of anechoic chamber is currently under consideration. Study will soon be undertaken.\r\n\r\n7.   Procurement. \r\na.   Measurement equipment including spectrum analyzer, power meters and E-field strength probe have been shortlisted. Final quotes are awaited.\r\nb.   Experimentation equipment including power attenuators, power amplifiers, water loads, coaxial and waveguide circulators, magnetron power supplies, power combiners, waveguide transitions, and waveguide launchers for magnetrons have also been shortlisted. Final quotes are awaited.	DSensors	Cancelled	2020-09-02 12:50:46	20	Jul 20	-20-25-30-20-	\N	f	\N
