250006	600	2021-12-09 11:14:46	1.   PI reply on technical comments of M/s Horizon Tech has been forwarded to concerned Dte. PI letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/7343114 dated 19 Nov 2019 refers. VA-SNIDS pilot integration at PNS JAUHAR will be initiated upon approval of modalities proposed in said PI letter.\r\n\r\n2.    01 X WEM has been released on 05 May 2021 upon receiving of NI security clearance.\r\n\r\n3. Coordination meeting among all stakeholders of VA-SNIDs integration project was tentatively scheduled in last week of June 2021 at NHQ. D Sec (Ops) letter PN/Security Ops Dte/03/2995695 dated 11 June 2021 refers. However, the same could not be conducted. Fresh date is being coordinated.\r\n\r\n4.   DSO informed about implementation of VA- SNIDs case under process at NSEPC and solution at Field units. Also DSO highlighted that R&D Dte may process the case to meet approval and related requirements as project implemented. D Security letter PN/Security Ops Dte/03/2995695 dated 11 June 2021 refers.\r\n\r\n5.    RDW requested DSO to process and issue necessary instructions as requested and arrange meeting with stakeholders being sponsoring Dte vide letter PN/ DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/9516278 dated 18 June 2021. However, DSO replied with no change in stance as highlighted vide para 3 above. PN/Security Ops Dte/03/3011709 dated 22 June 2021 refers.\r\n\r\n6.   A case file w.r.t permission from NI for sharing VA-SNIDs data was processed at NHQ vide PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/02/2955478 dated: 13 Aug 2021.\r\n\r\n7.    Apropos MD IAC directions in light of remarks on above mentioned casefile, an IHD was held between MD IAC along-with core developers of SNIDs Phase -II and Director ET Div with VA technical team on 31 Aug 21 at RDW NRDI. Discussion w.r.t feasibility of system level integration of VA with SNID phase-II, technical constraints in achieving the same and modalities involved was held therein. Subsequent to discussion, the recommended option along-with modified URD has been forwarded to DSO for approval. Letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/10499051 dated 20 Sep 2021 refers in this regard.\r\n\r\n8. Draft order of 01 x WEM has also been received vide PN/Drafting Authority/03/11403905 dated: 19 Nov 2021.	DEnab	Edited	2021-12-31 10:19:00	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	427	2021-05-05 09:35:28	1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n \r\na.   Control System Designing.\r\n\r\n(1)   Control circuit PCB for phase difference detection between two magnetrons has been fabricated. The PCB will communicate the phase detection signal to Single Board Computer (SBC) through ADC. \r\n\r\n(2)   Algorithms are being developed for phase matching of two magnetrons and will be implemented on SBC.  DAC and ADC cards have been procured and tested. \r\n\r\nb.   RF Devices. Following in-house design, development and high power testing of RF devices have been completed: \r\n\r\n(1)   Waveguide circulators. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks and high power magnets are used in the project experimentation. In house design and fabrication of 04x circulators has been completed. VNA Testing revealed satisfactory results. The fabricated circulators were also tested at 1 kW and were declared satisfactory. The circulators are successfully being used in experimentation involving injection locking and power combining of x02 1 kW magnetrons. The inhouse design and development activity resulted in a cost saving equivalent to PKR 5 Million. \r\n\r\n(2)   Waveguide directional couplers. High power testing of fabricated waveguide directional couplers has been completed. The inhouse design and development activity resulted in a cost saving equivalent to PKR 2.3 Million.\r\n\r\n(3)   Waveguide Termination. Design as well as multiphysics thermal simulation of high power waveguide termination based on wedged scheme has been completed.  Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n(4)   Phase Shifter. IC for a 360o Phase Shifter has been procured, and the PCB has been fabricated. Testing of the phase shifter on VNA has also been completed.\r\n\r\n(5)   Power Combiner. An H-plane power combiner is required for power combination of x02 1 kW magnetrons. Inhouse design and fabrication of power combiner followed by high power testing has been successfully completed. The indigenous design and development of power combiner resulted in cost saving equivalent to PKR 0.5 Million. \r\n\r\n\r\nc.   Experimentations.\r\n\r\n(1)   Injection Locking of a Single Magnetron. An experimental schematic was developed to accomplish injection locking of a single magnetron. Experiments were conducted with R&S signal generator as injection source. The injection signal was fed to a free running magnetron through a series of high power circulators, and the bandwidth of the magnetron was observed to reduce within 10 Hz. Experiments have also been completed with SDR B200 as injection source. The experiment was conducted with adequate safeties in place. The procedure and safeties were counter-checked by the QC teams following appropriate QC sheets.\r\n\r\n(2)   Power Combining of x02 Magnetrons. Experimental schematic was developed to combine power of two injection locked magnetrons. The experiment has been conducted wherein power of each magnetron was fed to a waveguide combiner through series of high power circulators and directional couplers. Both magnetrons were injection locked through a 3 dB 90o strip-line coupler using a single oscillator (R&S Signal Generator). A cable offering 90 degree counter phase shift was also introduced to ensure injection of both magnetrons at same phase. Bandwidth of the combined injection locked magnetrons was measured to be less than 10 Hz. Power combining efficiency was achieved to be 95%. The experiment was conducted with adequate safeties in place. The procedure and safeties were counter-checked by the QC teams following appropriate QC sheets.\r\n\r\nd.   RF Power Amplifier. \r\n\r\n(1)   In-house design optimization of 100 Watt power amplifier (PA) has been completed. Soldering of components on manufactured PCB has also been completed. The required heat sink has been designed and fabrication is in progress. \r\n\r\n(2)   QC sheets for safe testing of the designed and developed RF PA has also been prepared. Procurement of 100 Watt MOSFET has been completed. \r\n\r\n(3)   Gate biasing circuit has been designed to ensure controlled safe testing and operation of the 100 Watt depletion mode transistor. PCB manufacturing of the same has also been completed.\r\n\r\n(4)   Three stages of the Preamplifier are required for requisite RF power input to the 100 Watt MOSFET. All stages of the preamplifier circuits have been designed. Procurement of IC and pertinent components is in progress. Fabrication of PCBs is also in progress.\r\n\r\n3.   Following procurement actions are in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement Completed. Experimental components including 1 kW magnetrons, coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs, FPGA boards, Switch Mode Power Supplies, waveguide terminations, N52 magnets, Oscilloscope and DC power supply have been completed.\r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in Progress. Procurement of E-field probe, Spectrum Analyzer and Signal Generator is in progress. Due COVID-19 pandemic, delay is expected in delivery of these components. \r\n\r\n4.   Miscellaneous Study. On directions of HQ COMLOG, GM RD&TA approached NRDI R&D Wing to conduct EMC/EMI survey to finalize antenna location onboard PNS ALAMGIR vide letter number PN/PN Dockyard/PE AND D WING/ GM(RD AND  TA)/03/7895873 dated 06 Jan 21. The survey requires an E-field probe, already under procurement in project DEW (EDD Jun 21). Same probe will additionally be used for this EMC/EMI survey.	DR&D	Finalized	2021-05-05 09:35:50	25	Apr 21	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
350003	588	2021-12-03 09:10:38	\r\n1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Small Scale Weapon Demonstration. \r\n\r\n(1)   Demonstration of the irreversible damage caused on an electronic circuit through combined power of 02x 1 kW magnetrons is being planned. The setup has been tested at SPF with high power termination.\r\n\r\n(2)   Suitable location has been selected for weapon demonstration at RDS NATHIAGALI AOR. The demonstration will be conducted with adequate safeties in place, for which QC sheets have been prepared. Field demonstration layout has also been finalized. Work Order 2 of Phase I is currently awaited, for demonstration to be conducted.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Power Amplifier. Biasing circuit PCB has been redesigned with adequate track width suitable for high drain current. The Matching networks of the 100 Watt amplifier have been redesigned employing Simplified Real Frequency Technique (SRFT) for output MN and Bounded Performance Technique (BPT) for input MN. Layout design and EM co-simulation of the amplifier is also completed. Procurement of the components and adequate heat sink is in progress.\r\n\r\n2.   Following procurement actions are in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement Completed. Experimental components including 1 kW magnetrons, coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs, FPGA boards, Spectrum Analyzer, Switch Mode Power Supplies, 1 kW waveguide terminations, N52 magnets, Oscilloscope, 2.5 kW waveguide terminations, E-field probe, Signal Generator, DC power supply, refractory material for waveguide termination, 5 kW generator, and Automatic Voltage Regulator for RF lab have been completed. \r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in Progress. Lumped components for in-house designed RFPA, PCB fabrication services and adequate heatsink for the RFPA are in progress.\r\n\r\n3.   Following studies are being conducted to formulate research plans for combination of X-band magnetrons in ensuing years: \r\n\r\na.   A pulsed power supply based on Pulsed Forming Networks (PFN) required to drive pulsed magnetrons is currently being designed.\r\n\r\nb.   Preliminary design of RF devices including circulators and directional couplers at X-band (9 GHz) has been finalized.\r\n\r\n4.   Technical proposal amounting PKR 260M for Phase II pertaining to power combination of multiple J-band pulsed magnetrons of redundant AM-39 has been submitted to NHQ for approval. An anechoic RF chamber will also be designed and fabricated to enable shielded high-power testing of the magnetron combination experiment with adequate safety measures.	DSensors	Edited	2021-12-31 09:43:31	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
