350013	575	2021-11-01 19:45:20	\r\n1.   VTS qualification in vicinity of ESM Detectors onboard PN ATR. M/s RAS highlighted that the high power density and E-Field of LoS VTS transmission will effect the performance of onboard ESM system. It is recommended that both systems should not be operated simultaneously to ensure smooth operation. The same recommendation has been forwarded to NHQ vide letter PN/DGNRDI/RANDDWING/03110878134 dated 15 Oct 21.\r\n\r\n2.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI. The civil work required for installation of GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI is being undertaken by M/s FAST team. Tower construction for radome base has been completed. The radome is also mounted on the tower. GT&RS equipment installation is in progress by NRDI INTELL in collaboration with M/s FAST. Integration of Directional Antenna Director (DAD) system in radome and testing will be completed by end Nov 21.\r\n\r\n3.   Batch-II. Development of Batch-II against Milestone-7 has been completed and successfully tested in recent LWF held in Oct 21. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n4.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at PN Sites. The radomes have been manufactured and will be installed in due course of time subject to approvals by NHQ vide letter PN/NCW (TECH)/03/3249069 dated 08 Oct 21.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-02 11:35:28	25	Oct 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	250	2020-11-09 14:57:53	1.   Lab Development. Lab Development has been completed with installation of ESD mats, earthing point and power sockets. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Magnetron Injection Locking Simulation. Modelling and simulation studies to evaluate injection locking principles have been completed, and the observations have chalked out the requirements to develop sophisticated control loops, in order to enable frequency-injection and phase locking of free running magnetrons and furnish bandwidth reduction for efficient power combining of multiple frequency-injection-phase locked magnetrons. Work is in progress to design and implement the above mentioned control loops; details are provided in ensuing para. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Control System Designing for Frequency Pushing.\r\n\r\n   a.   Multiple simulation studies have been undertaken on MATLAB© Simulink to model frequency pushing of a Voltage Controlled Oscillator (VCO), using Phase Locked Loop (PLL) techniques. The VCO was successfully locked at a fixed frequency, as ripples in the biasing voltage were gradually reduced.\r\n\r\n   b.   Simulations are currently being undertaken on PSpice© to develop pertinent control circuitry, which will be implemented experimentally on a VCO.\r\n\r\n4.   RF Devices. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks, and waveguide directional couplers, are required in project experimentation. As limited funds have been released, inhouse design and development of RF devices is in progress.\r\n\r\n   a.   The fabrication of waveguide circulator and directional coupler has been started. Raw material has been procured and pertinent machining is in progress.\r\n\r\n   b.   A constant current power supply required for biasing the electromagnets and tuning the circulator response, is also being designed.\r\n\r\n5.   RF Power Amplifier.\r\n\r\n   a.   In-house design and optimization of 100W power amplifier has been completed. PCB manufacturing is also completed.\r\n\r\n   b.   RLC meter has been procured. This device has enabled correct selection of lumped components prior soldering and fine tuning of matching circuits used in power amplifiers.\r\n\r\n6.   Hardware Procurement. Project experimentation based on injection locking experimentation of a single magnetron will first be carried out to validate simulated results.\r\n\r\n   a.   Procurement of experimental components including coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, waveguide transitions, waveguide terminations, waveguide adapters, programmable switch mode power supplies and FPGA boards is in process. \r\n\r\n   b.   Electronics systems required for injection locking of single magnetron including Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs and Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) ICs are also being procured.\r\n\r\n7.   Anechoic Chamber. Feasibility study on in-house development of anechoic chamber is completed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n?	DSensors	Edited	2020-11-11 10:30:29	25	Oct 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350002	251	2020-11-09 14:58:09	1.   GPS Spoofing Hardware Development.\r\n\r\n   a.   Hardware Assembly. Ruggedized housing and assembly of spoofing PoC equipment is completed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n   b.   Development of End user GUI. The GUI has been updated to make it more user friendly. Alpha testing on the software is complete and associated recommendations have been implemented.  Beta testing is under progress and will be completed in first week of Nov 20.\r\n\r\n   c.   Laboratory Trials. Using the newly assembled ruggedized housing and spoofing PoC assembly, successful in-house trials have been conducted.\r\n\r\n   d.   Product Manuals. The technical and operator manuals for the product have been developed and are in the review phase.\r\n\r\n   e.   Acceptance Trials. Acceptance trials are planned for the second week of November, 2020.\r\n\r\n2.   Force Majeure has been invoked by DITD due COVID pandemic. The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR is also delayed due to export permit processing delays caused by COVID 19 pandemic. Once 3D X-band RADAR will be received, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of Eagle Hunt -3C version (autonomous GPS spoofing using X-band RADAR).\r\n\r\n3.   Housing of reactive jamming equipment in the marinized container is in progress. The INTELL team visited the M/s RIMS facility and finalized the contours of equipment installation. The said activity will be completed by Nov 20.\r\n\r\n4.   Miscellaneous Studies Supporting PN Fleet and Repair Agencies undertaken during reporting period\r\n\r\n   a.   PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) training. Development of training modules for Omniscan MX2 PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) equipment is completed. OJT of 07 Dockyard Lab staff is initialed at INTEL Lab. Theory classes and demonstration labs are being conducted for the same.\r\n\r\n   b.   Ultrasonic Testing (UT) of Besconds used in the cable hull passage onboard S/Ms. UT of a Balezona based locally developed besconds was undertaken. No flaws / defects were found and the bescond is accepted.\r\n\r\n   c.   500W High Power Antenna for PAF. One antenna has been fabricated and tested in anechoic chamber for radiation pattern, at M/s RIMS facility at NUST H-12 Islamabad. The radiation pattern results were found to be satisfactory and match well with simulation.	DSensors	Edited	2020-11-11 10:27:39	25	Oct 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
250002	649	2022-02-11 12:18:48	1.   Competent Authority has approved Establishment of Virtual Reality Centre at\r\nNRDI with cost effect of Rs.159.9 M. PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/2461806 dated 28 Aug 2020 refers.\r\n\r\n2.   Meeting of Director ET with MTSS team was held to brief them about the scope and modalities of the project. Accordingly, draft Work Order and Technical Proposal of VRC was shared with MTSS. Subsequently, draft work order has been sent to NHQ vide letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing /03/6789893 dated 01 Oct 20 in line with approved funds.\r\n\r\n3.    Recoupment of funds amounting to Rs 22M for CFY has been completed. \r\n\r\n4.   T? yet to be established. Development work will be initiated upon availability of allocated funds.\r\n\r\n5. Meeting chaired by VCNS was held on 14 Sep 21 and subsequently Minutes of Meeting have been received vide reference PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3240447 dated 05 Oct 2021.\r\n\r\n6.     As per Para 12-C of MoM of above mentioned meeting, Development of STLT may be considered after development of Virtual Reality (VR) Center.\r\n\r\n7.    RDW has initiated a letter w.r.t processing of VRC and STLT cases separately. RDW letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/11015633 dated 27 Oct 21 is relevant in this regard. Salient of the letter are provided below:\r\na.   VR based STLT is an ops requirement raised by STC and supported by COMPAK Command being the end user. \r\nb.   Current basic VR facility at R&D Wing (i.e an extension of VA Lab at PG Block of PNS JAUHAR) is ready to develop STLT simulator. Therefore, STLT and VRC may be processed as separate projects, independent of each other. \r\nc.   Budgetary proposal of VRC mainly includes hardware infrastructure. Whereas, VR based projects like STLT mostly covers processing and delivery equipment along-with HR requirement with an aim to enhance capacity and capability. \r\nd.   DSMO, being Sponsoring Dte, may be approached for processing and issuance of STLT Work Order as per procedure in vogue. \r\ne.   In parallel, relevant sponsoring directorate may be approached for processing of funds and work order issuance for VRC Project.  In this regard, draft PPF and URD have also been shared with Dir R&D.\r\n8.       A letter pertaining to queries as raised by DCNS(M) regarding sources of funding for VRC, HR requirements, infrastructure development etc was received from D R&D on         13 Jan 22 vide PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3456015. Accordingly a reply addressing all the queries has been forwarded to  D R&D. RDW Letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12114404 dated 17 Jan 22 refers in this regard.	DEnab	Finalized	2022-02-24 09:47:35	25	Jan 22	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350005	402	2021-04-28 15:35:37	1.   Design / Development Activities.\r\n\r\na.   Design and mold / pattern manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01 have been completed. Manufacturing of airframe skin has also been completed. Machining / assembly of structural components and metallic mounts is under progress.\r\n\r\nb.   Design of MARLIN-02 (full scaled HSTD) is being revised based on the learnings from design / manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01. Detailed design of airframe is completed. Design integration of avionics, launch, recovery systems and fastening of assemblies are under progress.\r\n\r\nc.   Jet Engine Testing. Manufacturing and assembly of test bench for P-1000 and P-220 turbo jet engine has been completed. Detailed safety guidelines & SOP for engine testing are also prepared. \r\n\r\nd.   P220 Turbo jet engine testing (for MARLIN-01) has been successfully completed on the inhouse designed and developed testbench. \r\n\r\ne.   UAV Launcher. Design and analysis activities of MARLIN-01 Launcher / pneumatic circuit testing bench are complete. Rail beams, beam hinges, actuator mounts are manufactured. Also, real beams are assembled, and beam hinges are installed. Assembly of pneumatic circuit components, actuator mounts and manufacturing of beam latches, carriage assembly & beams seats are under progress.\r\n\r\nf.   MARLIN-02 launcher. Design of MARLIN-02 launcher is being upgraded based on the knowledge from design / development of MARLIN-01 Launcher. In this regard, imperative consideration is given to weight reduction, ease of assembly and transportation. Local industry is engaged for the manufacturing of pneumatic actuator in lines with the INTELL design.\r\n\r\ng.   Construction of separate shaded floors for composite layup and launcher manufacturing at Serial Production Facility (SPF) are completed. Two temporary shades are also procured to facilitate launcher assembly process. \r\n\r\nh.   Material Testing. Destructive Testing (DT) of composite material samples have been carried out using PNEC and PCSIR equipment. Tensile tests are completed, bending tests are under progress. Design is being consolidated and manufacturing process is being improved based on the testing data. \r\n\r\ni.   Wind Tunnel Testing. Computer Aided Design (CAD) model, for development of testing model, has been shared as per the requirements of DESTO. The case is under processing at DESTO for timeline / quotation of model development & subsequent testing.\r\n\r\n2.   Hardware Procurement Status.\r\n\r\na.   Order is placed for procurement of JetCat P-1000 (Germany based 1100N) turbo jet engine. The procurement is under progress.\r\n\r\nb.   Order is placed for procurement of Veronte Flight controller of M/s Embention. The procurement is under progress.\r\n\r\nc.   Material for manufacturing of MARLIN-01 UAV and Launcher are being purchased / procured as per the requirement of manufacturing under progress.	DSensors	Edited	2021-05-05 09:38:13	25	Apr 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
