350005	548	2021-09-29 17:13:26	1.   Design / Development Activities.\r\n\r\na.   MARLIN-01 UAV.  Airframe manufacturing, assembly, avionics / control / data link integration and testing activates are completed.  Ground tests of airframe, propulsion, data link and control system are also completed.\r\nb.   MARLIN-01 Backup. Manufacturing of Marlin-01 backup is initiated. Machining of structural parts and curing of airframe skin are completed. Assembly of airframe and integration of avionics and control system assembly is also completed. Finishing/ painting activities are under process. Maiden testing of backup P220 engine (MARLIN-01 backup) is also successfully completed.\r\n\r\nc.   UAV Launcher. Design and manufacturing of MARLIN-01 Launcher/ pneumatic circuit testing bench are complete. Improvements for speed enhancement are under progress.\r\n\r\nd.   Jet Engine Testing. Bench testing P220 Turbo jet engine (for MARLIN-01) is carried out. The tests indicated requirement of improvement intake duct design. Pertinent design improvement and manufacturing of modified intake are completed. Bench testing of engine with upgraded intake duct is also completed. The bench test results indicated performance within acceptable margins.\r\n\r\ne.   UAV Launcher Testing.   Initial testing of launcher with integrated control system and pneumatic circuit at low and medium pressure are successfully completed. Field testing for dead weight and dummy UAV launcher are also planned at PN GHARO facility. Co-ordination for relevant permission is under progress.\r\n \r\nf.   Design of MARLIN-02 (full scaled HSTD). The design is being revised based on the learnings from design/ manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01. Detailed design of airframe components and integration with launch/ recovery systems are also completed. Integration of avionics systems, data link, control mechanism and modifications pertaining to propulsion system is under progress.\r\n\r\ng.   MARLIN-02 launcher. Design of MARLIN-02 launcher is being redesigned based on the learning from design / development of MARLIN-01 Launcher. In this regard, imperative consideration is being given to weight reduction, ease of assembly and transportation. Market surveys for COTs items, pneumatic / control system components and manufacturing progress planning activates are also initialed for subsequent manufacturing. Design of launcher angle positioning mechanism is being revised for cost reduction.\r\n\r\nh.   Material Testing. Destructive Testing (DT) of composite material samples is being carried out using PNEC and PCSIR equipment. Tensile tests and first phase of bending tests are completed. Manufacturing process is improved in lines with the test results. Bending tests of improved samples are under progress. Also, testing of different composite coring materials is planned and sample are being prepared. Shear Testing Jig in accordance with ASTM D7078 is also design and manufactured for the pertinent testing.\r\n\r\nj.   Wind Tunnel Testing. Computer Aided Design (CAD) model, for development of testing model, has been shared as per the requirements of DESTO.  Estimated of quotation & timeline of 190 working days is received from DESTO. DESTO has been requested to reduce the timeline. Foreign WTT facilitates are also being explored for the pertinent testing.\r\n\r\n2.   Hardware Procurement Status.\r\n\r\na.   Order is placed for procurement of JetCat P-1000 (Germany based 1100N) turbo jet engine. The procurement is under progress; EDD Oct 21.\r\n\r\nb.   Veronte flight controller from M/s Embention has been procured. The equipment has been tested in lab and found to be in working order. OEM is engaged for technical support regarding development of flight control and mission planning setup based on requirement. Order for an amplifier for air trials has also been initiated. \r\n\r\nc.   Material for finishing of MARLIN-01 UAV and Launcher are being purchased/ procured as per the requirement of manufacturing under progress.\r\n\r\nd.   Orders are placed for raw material & COTs items for MARLIN-02 UAV and Launcher. The procurement is under progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-10-28 11:18:19	25	Sep 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	216	2020-10-07 12:10:48	Lab Development: Lab development is partially completed. \r\na.   Table top required to carry out project experimentation of power combining of two magnetrons has been procured and installed.\r\nb.   Installation of ESD mats, earthing points and power sockets is in progress.\r\n\r\n2.   Magnetron Injection Locking Modeling and Simulation\r\na.   Preliminary injection locking numerical scheme as designed has been investigated using computational modeling. Promising results are achieved in lines with the design.\r\nb.   Various combinations of gain and bandwidth of the injection signal were tested in simulation. The trend was observed to follow the classical Adler’s Equation and theory. This analysis has furnished the requirement to develop additional feedback loop to control the characteristics of injection locking signal’s spectral bandwidth and gain, through FPGA based control circuitry. \r\nc.   Noisy excitation signal to the magnetron was also simulated to investigate the effect on magnetron jittering. Magnetron output was observed to be highly non-stationary (the frequency is varying with respect to time). As mentioned above, this analysis has furnished the requirement to develop additional feedback loops for a stabilized fully controllable power supply through Spartan Xilinx based COTs FPGA.\r\n\r\n3.   RF Devices: Indigenous design and fabrication of following high frequency RF devices are being undertaken to accomplish project experimentation in the given funds. Circulators and couplers required for the experimentation has been modeled and simulated successfully. The production drawings have also been generated. Procurement of raw material is in progress. It is pertinent to mention that limited funds (Rs. 80M) have been allocated against the approved amount (Rs. 146M). The in-house design and development of RF devices will enable completion of project in available funds. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n4.   RF Power Amplifier:\r\n\r\na.   8Wa PA. In-house design and manufacturing of Heat Sink along with packaging of amplifier has been completed. The assembly has been successfully tested on VNA and spectrum analyzer. The thermal performance of PA with the developed sink is also satisfactory.\r\n\r\nb.   100 Watt PA.\r\n1)   In-house design of 100W power amplifier has been completed. Optimization of results through different simulations is in progress.\r\n2)   The raw material for 100W amplifier has been procured. \r\n3)   RLC meter procurement for measurement of RLC components is being undertaken. This will enable optimization and fine tuning of matching circuits used in power amplifiers.\r\n\r\n6.   Control System Designing: As mentioned above, injection locking simulation studies have revealed that sophisticated control loops are required to furnish stable phase and frequency at magnetron output port. Therefore, following control loops are being studied and under development:\r\na.   Feedback loop to furnish control power supply voltage through magnetron pushing characteristics. \r\nb.   Feedback loop to furnish efficient magnetron locking bandwidth by adjusting the bandwidth and gain of the injection signal. \r\nc.   The abovementioned feedback loops will be programmed in above mentioned FPGA. The HR is being trained in the area of control implementation on board FPGAs. \r\n\r\n7.   Hardware Procurement: Project experimentation based on injection locking experimentation of a single magnetron will first be carried out to validate simulated results.\r\na.   Procurement of experimental components including coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, waveguide transitions, waveguide adapters, power supplies and FPGA boards is in process. \r\nb.   Electronics systems required for injection locking of single magnetron including Phase Locked Loop (PLL) based ICs and Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) ICs are also being procured.\r\n\r\n8.   Anechoic Chamber. Preliminary study on in-house development of anechoic chamber is being pursued at INTELL.	DSensors	Edited	2020-10-12 11:35:53	38	Sep 20	-20-25-30-38-	\N	f	\N
350013	218	2020-10-07 12:11:08	1.   International Procurement. All required raw material from foreign OEMs has already been acquired except Profi tracker used in Directional Antenna Director (DAD). Profi tracker delivery is delayed due to export licensing issues from Germany. Consequently team is working on an alternate solution including re-routing to Pakistan or customization of substitute product from China. All out efforts are in place to meet the deadlines.\r\n\r\n2.   Radome for housing GT&RS Antenna. Radome composite lay-up for 1st batch is under progress at Serial Production Facility (SPF) and will be completed in early Oct 20.\r\n\r\n3.   Installation of GTRS.\r\nInstallation of LoS VTS antenna Radome on rooftop of ELINT station as RDS NATHIAGALI has been proposed in lines with NRDI INTELL design. The proposed design report for Radome installation and hardware configuration is also submitted. NHQ engaged DW and CE for ensuring existing load bearing capacity vide letter PN/NCW/03/2490723 dated 16 Sep 20.\r\n\r\n\r\n4.   Vans modification to house VTS receiving station for ISR Operations. The van modification in lines with INTELL design is completed. Installed equipment and van modification are tested by INTELL team. The modified van will be delivered by end Sep 20. The installation of equipment in the modified van will be finished by mid Oct 20.\r\n\r\n5.   LoS VTS airborne unit installation onboard MPA ATR. \r\na. In-house designed transmitter rack and GPS Radome has been manufactured by AED workshops. INTELL team qualified the development of same. NHQ(NAM Dte) was requested to approach M/s RAS to render qualification of EMS detectors on board marinized ATRs against VTS transmission vide letter PN/AED DEP/GM ILM AND OLS/03/ 6519269 dated 07 Sep 20. The reminder was again sent to DNAM Dte by HQ COMPAK to provide an update on qualification of EMS detectors vide letter PN/HQ COMPAK/03/6522890 dated 08 Sep 20.\r\n\r\n\r\n6.   GPS Parser development. GPS Parser PCBs for first batch have been developed from the local industry in lines with INTELL designs. Order is placed for development of in-house designed casing, EDD is early Oct 20. \r\n\r\n7.   NATHIAGALI visit. INTELL team visited RDS NATHIAGALI on 3 Sep 20 with shortlisted local industry personnel for the civil works involved in GT&RS installation	DSensors	Edited	2020-10-12 11:30:05	38	Sep 20	-20-25-30-38-	\N	f	\N
350005	665	2022-03-03 15:09:02	\r\n1.   Submission of Hardware Purchase Order. Hardware purchase order for experimental components for Magnetron Combination against Milestone M2 has been submitted. <Point recommended to be dropped.>\r\n\r\n2.   Design / Development Activities.\r\n\r\na.   MARLIN-01 UAV.  Airframe manufacturing, assembly, avionics/ control / data link integration is completed.  Operational tests of airframe, propulsion, data link and control system are also completed. Point recommended to be dropped \r\n\r\nb.   MARLIN-01 Backup. Manufacturing of an additional MARLIN-01 (as backup), is in the final stages. Machining of structural parts and curing of airframe skin are completed. Assembly of airframe and avionics / control integration and painting work are also completed. In lines with the avionics system testing, a dedicated cooling system has been designed and installed. Moreover, in-house Ingress Protection (IP) testing of avionics box is successfully completed.\r\n \r\nc.   UAV Launcher. Design and manufacturing of MARLIN-01 Launcher / pneumatic circuit testing bench are complete. Design and assembly of carriage deceleration / braking system is also completed. The designed system has been successfully tested as well. To further improve speed performance, the pneumatic actuator has been replaced with a larger stroke actuator, the pulley ratio has been reduced and one more inlet is added to the accumulator vessel. \r\n\r\nd.   UAV Launcher Testing.   Initial testing of launcher with integrated control system and pneumatic circuit at low, medium pressure is completed. In-house testing of launcher at SPF are also completed successfully.  Field testing for dead weight and dummy UAV launches are successfully conducted at PN GHARO facility.  The criteria of projectile launch speed, aerial time and ground range are successfully met.\r\n\r\ne.   Jet Engine Testing. Bench testing of P220 Turbo jet engine (for MARLIN-01) has been conducted. Intake duct design has been improved and manufactured. Bench testing of engine with improved intake is also conducted and results are within acceptable margins. \r\n\r\nf.   Backup P220 Engine. Maiden testing of backup P220 engine (MARLIN-01 backup) is also successfully completed.\r\n\r\ng.   Ground Testing of Marlin-01 UAVs. Extensive ground testing activities of Marlin-01 UAVs are considered essential prior to the flight trials. In this regard: airframe load tests, pitch/roll performance testing of propulsion system, avionics endurance testing, data-link range tests, parachute release mechanism tests, control surface load tests, carriage-lock thrust testing are planned. Airframe load tests, pitch/roll performance testing of propulsion system and avionics endurance tests are successfully completed. Data link range tests and parachute release mechanism tests are partly completed. During control surface load testing, problem related to deformation of control linkages and servo failure is observed. Control linkage mechanism has been upgraded to increase stiffness and rigidity. Root cause analysis of servo failure is being carried out and results will be used to further ruggedize avionics systems. Carriage-lock thrust testing of the UAV will be conducted at PN GHARO facility in Mar 22.\r\n\r\nh.   Field Testing of Marlin-01 UAVs. Field testing / launch trials of Marlin-01 UAV has been planned at PN GHARO facility in Mar 22. For this purpose, leakage testing of launcher, site survey and coordination meeting between NRDI and NSTOC reps regarding recovery of HSTD from creek area was held on 24-25 Feb 22, vide reference PN/NRDI/ R AND D Wing/03/12462317 dated 18 Feb 22. \r\n\r\nj.   Design of MARLIN-02 (full-scale HSTD). The design has been revised based on the learnings from design / manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01. Detailed design of airframe components and integration with launch / recovery systems are completed. CAD integration of avionics systems, data link, control mechanism and modifications pertaining to propulsion system are under progress. Pattern machining activities have been initiated for the completed airframe components. Pattern finishing activities and mold fabrication are also completed. Test fabrication of airframe parts in the finished molds is under progress for quality assessment and assembly tests. Subsequently, final airframe parts are being manufactured.\r\n\r\nk.   MARLIN-02 Launcher. MARLIN-02 launcher is being re-designed based on the learning from design / development of MARLIN-01 Launcher. In this regard, considerations are being given to weight reduction, ease of assembly and transportation. In order to keep the development, cost effective and reduce develop time imperative consideration is given to re-use of parts / sub-assemblies manufactured for the MARLIN-01 launcher. Export of manufacturing drawings and market surveys for COTs items are under progress. \r\n\r\nl.   Material Testing. Destructive Testing (DT) of composite material samples is being carried out using PNEC and PCSIR equipment. Tensile tests and first phase of bending tests are completed. Manufacturing process is improved in lines with the test results. Bending tests of improved samples are also completed. Testing of different composite coring materials are tested and coring scheme for MARLIN-02 has been finalized. \r\n\r\nm.   Wind Tunnel Testing. Computer Aided Design (CAD) model for development of testing model has been shared, as required by M/s DESTO.  Estimated of quotation & timeline of 190 working days is received from the firm. M/s DESTO has been requested to reduce timeline. Foreign WTT facilities are also being explored for the pertinent testing. \r\n\r\n3.   Hardware Procurement Status.\r\n\r\na.   Order is already placed for procurement of JetCat P-1000 (Germany based 1100N) turbo jet engine. Engine is ready at OEM facility while export license is being processed for shipment to Pakistan. EDD for the engine is Feb 22.\r\n\r\nb.   Veronte flight controller (of M/s Embention) excluding air antenna is received at INTELL NRDI. Individual components have been tested and radio link is established. Firmware update has also been received for tracker. Currently, development of controls for HSTD are being studied and range testing activates are being planned.\r\n\r\nc.   Material for fabrication of MARLIN-02 UAV and Launcher are being purchased/ procured as per manufacturing requirements.\r\n\r\nd.   Orders are placed for raw material & COTs items for MARLIN-02 UAV and Launcher. The procurement is under progress.\r\n?	DSensors	Finalized	2022-03-30 08:52:03	25	Feb 22	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
