350005	476	2021-06-29 04:17:36	1.   Design/ Development Activities.\r\n\r\na.   Design and mold / pattern manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01 are completed. Manufacturing of airframe skin and machining of structural members, assembly and integration of engine, control system, data links are also complete. Finishing activities are under progress. \r\n\r\nb.   Design of MARLIN-02 (full scaled HSTD) is being revised based on the learnings from design / manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01. Detailed design of airframe and integration with launch / recovery systems are also completed. Modifications pertaining to feasibility of manufacturing of molds / patterns are under progress. \r\n\r\nc.   Jet Engine Testing. Manufacturing and assembly of test bench for P-1000 and P-220 turbo jet engine is completed. P220 Turbo jet engine testing has been successfully completed. Engine will be further tested after mounting with the finished airframe. \r\n\r\nd.   UAV Launcher. Design and analysis activities of MARLIN-01 Launcher / pneumatic circuit testing bench are complete. Manufacturing/ assembly of rail structure and pneumatic control circuit is also completed.\r\n\r\ne.   UAV Launcher Testing.   Initial testing of launcher with integrated control system and pneumatic circuit is also successfully completed. The control system is being refined based on the test results. Field testing of dummy launches with dead weight are being planned at PN GHARO facility in Jul 21. \r\n\r\nf.   MARLIN-02 launcher. Design of MARLIN-02 launcher is being redesigned based on the learning from design / development of MARLIN-01 launcher. In this regard, imperative consideration is being given to weight reduction, ease of assembly and transportation. Manufacturing of customized high pneumatic actuator through local industry is also completed. \r\n\r\ng.   Construction of separate shaded floors for composite layup and launcher manufacturing at Serial Production Facility (SPF) are completed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nj.   Material Testing. Destructive Testing (DT) of composite material samples is being carried out using PNEC and PCSIR equipment. Tensile tests and first phase of bending tests are completed. Manufacturing process is improved in lines with the test results. Bending tests of improved samples are under progress. Also, testing of different composite coring materials is being planned.\r\n\r\nk.   Wind Tunnel Testing. Computer Aided Design (CAD) model, for development of testing model, has been shared as per the requirements of DESTO.  Estimated of quotation & timeline of 190 working days is received from DESTO. DESTO has been requested to reduce the timeline.\r\n\r\nl.   Recovery method testing. Test setup is developed for the testing of MARLIN-01 parachute recovery system. Relevant section of the fuselage (nose section) and hard points for parachute mounting are manufactured and finishing activities are under progress. Step wise trial sheets are also being developed for subsequent field testing of system.\r\n\r\n\r\n2.   Hardware Procurement Status. Order is placed for the procurement of the following items:\r\n\r\na.   JetCat P-1000 (Germany based 1100N) turbo jet engine\r\nb.   Veronte Flight controller of M/s Embention\r\nc.   Raw material for MARLIN-02 UAV and launcher\r\nd.   Material for finishing of MARLIN-01 UAV and launcher (as per manufacturing requirements)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n?	DSensors	Finalized	2021-07-16 14:04:11	25	Jun 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
