350004	477	2021-06-29 04:17:41	1.   Critical Design of UCAV. Design of propulsion system of UCAV has been initiated. Integration of selected engine from ROTAX is being carried out in design. Design of control system electronics for engine is also underway. Design of landing gear retraction mechanism has been initiated. Furthermore, design study for control surface actuation mechanism has also started. \r\n\r\n2.   Design of test bench for ROTAX 914 engine is underway. Detailed CAD design of test stand and provisions for mounting of ancillary equipment such as radiators, oil pump etc. are being considered in this design. Control electronics for this test bench are also being designed. A detailed study of integrated sensors and electronics is being carried out for the development of test bench.\r\n\r\n3.   TUALCOM ELINT module has been procured and is awaiting shipment from OEM. Delivery is expected in first week of Jul 21.\r\n\r\n4.   Mission Computer Test Bench. Study on mission computer algorithms for integration with flight controller and other avionics is in progress. \r\n\r\n5.   Scaled Down UCAV Model (GANNET). Flight trials for Gannet are being planned once suitable runway has been selected. Tuning of Proportional, Integral and Derivative (PID) gains will be carried out and flight controller will be calibrated for autonomous operations. Presently, hop-test is being planned at Faisal air field. \r\n\r\n6.   Machine Shop. End User Certificate (EUC) for M/s Doosan CNC was turned down by the South Korean authorities. An alternate 4-axis machining center of equal specification has already been selected from Taiwan (M/s Hartford). OEM has been engaged for the procurement. Two machines (table grinder and drill press) have also been sourced locally. Lathe machine delivery is expected in Jul 21. Construction work on machine shop is under progress. Thermal insulation and electrical works are underway and will be completed soon. \r\n\r\n7.   Team development. Hiring of undergraduate students as EAs is being planned for HR development. \r\n?	DSensors	Finalized	2021-07-16 14:04:07	25	Jun 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
