350015	684	2022-04-27 21:30:52	1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Small Scale Weapon Field Testing. Preliminary Field testing was of 2.5 KW setup was conducted at RDS NATHIAGALI vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12427313 dated 16 Feb 22. The interference was observed with drone as target. Multiple targets such as Low Noise Amplifiers (LNAs) and Phase Frequency Detectors (PFDs) are being evaluated for disruptive demonstration. \r\n\r\nb.   Horn Antenna Improvement. Horn antenna has been redesigned and fabricated resulting in better efficiency.  A testing was carried out at SPF with one horn antenna used for transmission, and another used for reception. A 47 dBm signal was transmitted at 2.45 GHz, and 13 dBm was received at reception antenna at 10 m, resulting in propagation loss of 34 dB. The exercise was aimed to simulate the in-band damage effect on a missile seeker. The 13 dBm signal is disruptive for LNAs and PFDs used in RADAR systems of missile seekers.\r\n\r\nc.   X-Band Experiment. RF devices are being designed and fabricated at X-band for use in power combination of pulsed M1475A 25 kW magnetrons. Power supplies and pulse modulators have been procured and are undergoing extensive testing before use in experimentation.\r\n\r\n2.   RF Power Amplifier. Biasing circuit PCB has been redesigned with adequate track width suitable for high drain current. The Matching networks of the 100 Watt amplifier have been redesigned employing Simplified Real Frequency Technique (SRFT) for output MN and Bounded Performance Technique (BPT) for input MN. PCB fabrication has been completed; PCB component population is in progress and will available for testing in Apr 22.\r\n\r\n3.   Submission of Hardware Purchase Order. Hardware purchase order for experimental components for Magnetron Combination against Milestone M2 has been submitted. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n \r\n4.   Procurement in Progress. Lumped components for in-house designed RFPA, PCB fabrication services and adequate heatsink for the RFPA have been completed. Point recommended to be dropped. \r\n\r\n5.   Following studies are being conducted to formulate research plans for combination of X-band magnetrons for more effective DEW design: \r\n\r\na.   A pulsed power supply based on Pulsed Forming Networks (PFN) required to drive pulsed magnetrons is currently being designed.\r\n\r\nb.   Preliminary design of RF devices including circulators and directional couplers at X-band (9 GHz) has been finalized. \r\n\r\n6.   Technical proposal amounting PKR 232M for Phase II pertaining to power combination of multiple J-band pulsed magnetrons of redundant AM-39 has been submitted to NHQ for approval. An anechoic RF chamber will also be designed and fabricated to enable shielded high-power testing of the magnetron combination experiment with adequate safety measures. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n7.   The proposal for future plan was also submitted vide Ref no PN/DGNRDI/RNDWING/03/11409776 dated 21ST Nov 21 in which Power Combination of multiple 25Kw pulsed J-band magnetrons, to achieve 150 kW combined power, is to be undertaken. Following are the salient highlights of the approach. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\na.   Pulsed operation philosophy will yield lower operational cost, lesser cooling requirement, higher lethality compared to CW.\r\n\r\nb.   J-band RF devices will be smaller in size and can be efficiently tailored for installation onboard naval platform.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-05-10 03:02:26	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350012	690	2022-04-27 04:03:08	\r\n1.   Coordination meeting with PN FMG for NDT data acquisition. A meeting was held at NRDI INTELL on 13 Dec 21 vide reference PN/DG NRDI/At PNS JAUHAR/03/11802413 dated 17 Dec 21. The NDT data acquisition methodology for the project was finalized in the meeting. The NDT data comprising of thermal and ultrasonic data will be periodically acquired by FMG team depending upon the availability of Ship/vessel. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Acquisition of Environmental data. The NRDI team acquires the environmental data from PN Ship/vessel on monthly basis. The data was retrieved from the deployed data loggers. Moreover, the team also replaced the battery packs of the data loggers during their visit. The data will be acquired by NRDI team upon availability of the PN Ship/vessel vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12124832 dated 18 Jan 2022. \r\n\r\n3.   Historical Database Development. A historical database is being developed to record the acquired environmental and NDT data from PN ships/vessels. The database is being analyzed at NRDI. Subsequently, data analytics is being performed on the database for estimation of degradation parameter. Data provided by FMG was not suitable; the same has been communicated to the PoC for rectification, vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12119861 dated 18 Jan 2022. The availability of PN platforms to perform data acquisition activity by NRDI team in the presence of FMG reps is requested vide reference PN/NRDI/ R AND D WING/03/12449213 dated 21 Feb 22.\r\n\r\n4.   Implementation of RUL Prediction Algorithms on Historical Database (MS-5). A detailed report on “Implementation of RUL Prediction Algorithms on historical database” has been submitted on 10 Jan 22 according to milestone 5 of the project. A presentation on the same was requested vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12240914 dated 01 Feb 22. Subsequently, a detailed presentation was given in a meeting between NRDI NDT & Reliability Engineering Center, NCMA and FMG teams, held at NRDI INTELL on 21 Feb 22, vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12499265 dated 22 Feb 22.  Queries from NCMA on delivered presentation was received vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12629885 dated 04 Mar 22. Detailed response on raised queries was provided by NRDI vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12737531 dated 11 Mar 22. Further clarification on milestone 5 report was again requested by NCMA vide letter PN/NCMA/03/12744668 dated 14 Mar 22. More detailed response was forwarded vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12766316 dated 15 Mar 22 in which diligent reading of work order is requested. Further clarification was requested by NCMA w.r.t understanding of milestone 5 report vide letter PN/NCMA/03/12816140 dated 18 Mar 22. The itemized response on each point was forwarded vide PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12898610 dated 25 Mar 22. Subsequently, NCMA have forwarded the response to FMG ME, FMG WE and GM RD and TA for feedback vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12958496 dated 31 Mar 22. The acceptance of milestone 5 is still under deliberation at NCMA.\r\n\r\n5.   Non-Availability of PN platforms for Data Acquisition. During the conduct of said project, sufficient historical data could not be collected by FMG team due non availability of PN platforms. Following references are relevant is this regard\r\n\r\na.   PN/HQ COMPAK/03/12879578 dated 24 Mar 22\r\nb.   PN/NCMA/03/12878153 dated 24 Mar 22\r\nc.   PN/DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11285138 dated 12 Nov 21\r\nd.   PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12008222 dated 06 Jan 22\r\n\r\n6.   Extension in Project Timeline. A case for extension of the project for 06 months is suggested after acceptance of milestone 5 and subject to availability of PN platform vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12655448 dated 21 Mar 22 . The same has not acceded to vide NHQ letter PN/ILS Dte /03/3616326 dated 25 Mar 22. Same will be again pursued in upcoming field project meeting.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-05-10 03:03:02	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
