350014	658	2022-03-03 15:08:09	\r\n1.   Design. A detailed study on engineering design of ship-based gyro stabilized platform has been carried out. It is being optimized for PN ships. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Modelling and Simulation. A detailed CAD model of GSP has been developed based on URD. Forward kinematics equations have been generated for the platform. A study on inverse kinematics is underway. Sim-scape® simulations have been carried out. The obtained model has been used to generate a control loop in Matlab and Simulink. Hardware integration of the controller with the Matlab environment has been carried out. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Design Engineering Study. Design engineering study has been submitted according to milestone 3. The same will be processed by acceptance committee, upon its formulation, as per the requirement of work order. NHQ comments on DES vide reference letter no. NCW/WO/LOS VTS/II/664 are adequately responded and updated DES has been submitted. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n4.   Development of Scaled Down Model of GSP. A scaled down model of GSP has been developed in-house to validate the calculated range of motion and forces for the platform and linkages. The scaled down model has been designed to retain the full range of motion in roll (± 25?) and pitch (± 15?) as outlined in the URD, along with a capability to carry upto 1kg of payload. Electronic components for scaled down model have been procured along with raw materials for structure and frame and construction has been completed. The range of motion in roll and pitch for the system, acquired using kinematics models have been validated using the scaled down model. Development of scaled down model will provide confidence in full scale GSP development. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n5.   Algorithm Development. The control algorithm for GSP has been extensively studied and different approaches have been implemented in Matlab. The most optimized approach in terms of system response time was observed using the inverse kinematics model along with PID. Fine tuning of parameters for PID has been carried out. Additionally, an optimized, lightweight version of algorithm to run it on industrial mini pc in the field has been developed. \r\n\r\n6.   PN Ship Visit. INTELL team visit PNS MOAWIN to ascertain the final placement of full scale GSP. Ship’s bridge top was selected as the ideal location due to ample space, proximity to electrical systems and bridge where LOS VTS receiver can be placed. INTELL team will carry out detailed designs of deck space and a rugged base platform for the full-scale model to be mounted. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n7.   Assembly of Full-Scale Model. Design of full-scale model was completed, and QC was carried out on the design. Parts were manufactured according to design and assembly has been carried out. QC of assembled parts has also been carried out. Integration of electronics in full scale model is completed. Developed algorithms have also been used to verify movement and stabilization capabilities of full scale GSP model. Integration of MOTUS IMU has been carried out in full scale model. \r\n\r\n8.   Development of Test Bench. A test bench is being developed to verify the range of motion of full-scale model of GSP. Updated parameters for this design have been used in forward kinematics equations to verify the range of motion. CAD design of the model has been developed based on the calculated values. QC of design and simulation of stress and forces has also been carried out. Manufacturing of metal linkages and parts has been initiated. Design and development of GUI and algorithms for test bench and implementation of testing protocols is underway.\r\n\r\n9.   Installation of GSP onboard PNS MOAWIN. INRDI INTELL recommends installation of the GSP and LoS VTS antenna on PNS MOAWIN Bridge top while keeping the receiver assembly on Ships Bridge. Two options were proposed for placement of antenna mounted on GSP vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/12114815 dated 19 Jan 22. Letter PN/NDRI/ R AND D Wing/03/12492965 dated 21 Feb 22 is again forwarded for early directions in this regard.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-03-30 08:53:24	25	Feb 22	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
