350012	566	2021-11-01 19:43:59	1.   Workorder Issuance. The T0 is established as 10 Jun 21 vide letter ILS/0620/INVENTORY MODEL dated 03 Aug 21. Formulation of the acceptance committee as per the requirement of work order is in progress. \r\n\r\n2.   Finalized Case Study. A detailed study of Machining Control System (MCS) of YARMOOK class ship and SR-60 RADAR has been carried out. The case study was reviewed by NCMA and INTELL NRDI team incorporated the recommendations. Finalized Case Study report submitted Oct against Milestone-3 for release of funds has been evaluated and supported vide PN/NCMA/03/10738145 dated 06 Oct 21. \r\n\r\n\r\n3.   SR-60 RADAR. A detailed study on SR-60 RADAR has been carried out. Technical documentation and defect history of the RADAR has been received. A visit was carried out by the project team to identify potential data acquisition points for periodic NDT data collection and shortlist data-loggers deployment locations inside the RADAR cabinet. The team visited SR-60 RADAR onboard PNS ASLAT on 29th October 2021 to analyze actual operational and environmental conditions of a functional RADAR system. The team performed thermal, magnetic and ultrasonic non-destructive testing at accessible data acquisition points. The shortlisted data acquisition points and NDT data collection methodology was also briefed to the accompanied FMG staff. The recorded NDT data is maintained in a historical database for analytics.\r\n\r\n4.   Procurement and development of Dataloggers. Magnetic flux leakage and environmental monitoring sensors have been procured and are being tested. Printed circuit board (PCB) based data-loggers are being developed for recording equipment environmental conditions and magnetic non-destructive testing (NDT) data. The developed dataloggers will subsequently be installed on SR-60 RADAR and MCS onboard PN Ship.\r\n\r\n5.   Survey Visit. INTELL NRDI team embarked PNS TABUK for sea trip to analyze actual operational and environmental conditions of onboard Machinery Control System (MCS). Thermal and ultrasonic emission data of different MCS sensors installed on running engines (ME-1 & ME-4) as well as the ambient signals were recorded. The acquired data will be analyzed to identify potential data acquisition points that embed health information of the MCS. The list of MCS sensors used for data acquisition for each running engine is provided below. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\na.   Main Engine Exhaust Temperature Sensor\r\nb.   Main Engine Jacket Water Temperature Sensor\r\nc.   Main Engine Oil-Mist Detection Sensor\r\nd.   Main Engine PORT-side Cylinders 1-8\r\ne.   Main Engine STBD-side Cylinders 1-8\r\nf.   Main Engine Turbo Chargers 1- 2\r\ng.   I/O Module 1\r\nh.   I/O Module 2\r\nj.         Display Module 1\r\nk.        Display Module 2	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-02 11:35:54	25	Oct 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350010	567	2021-11-01 19:44:06	1.   Procurement. 24 VFDs and Keypads have been received from Taiwan. Testing of received items has been carried out and all items are operational.\r\n\r\n2.   Test Bench Design. In house developed test bench has been completed. Testing has been carried out using returned 11T and 150T VFDs. Functionality of test bench has been verified.  \r\n\r\n3.   FATs of 50T VFD from S/M for Air Compressor (HPAC) and Water Regulation Pump (DM). The design and execution of 50T VFD for HPAC and DM are completed while FATs and QA/QC testing by DY personnel are being carried out. All the FATs comments have been addressed vide letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11057564 dated 28 Oct 21.\r\n\r\n4.   Design of VFDs. Following design activities have been carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Mechanical design of VFDs for 03 VFDs for Hydraulic Pumps (DT) has been initiated. The CAD of VFD cabinet is completed to accommodate new VFDs procured from Taiwan. Moreover, the casings have been sent for powder coating from local vendors. \r\n\r\nb.   Electrical design for 03 VFDs of Hydraulic Pumps (DT) is initiated. Queries in this regard have been shared with DY rep and logic designing have been initiated based on their feedback.   \r\n\r\nc.   Electrical and Mechanical design of VFDs for Battery Fans has been initiated.\r\n5.   Appreciation Letter. Timely delivery of 150T VFD for DA pump after successful modification of PN S/M KHALID is highly appreciated by PND vide letter PN/PN DOCKYARD/ S/M WING/GM (ME S/M WING)/03/10930706 dated 21 Oct 21.\r\n\r\n6.   Provision of Three Speeds on DA-Pump VFD. Activity to enable third speed on DA pump VFD will be carried out by NRDI INTELL team. Team will visit installed VFD onboard AGOSTA 90B and will carry out on-site modifications. This activity will bring the installed VFD in-line with provided URD.\r\n\r\n7.   Correspondence. Following correspondence has been carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Queries regarding electrical panel design along with the preliminary panel for Hydraulic pump have been forwarded to DY team. Once approved and accepted by DY team, the electrical panel will be implemented by NRDI INTELL.\r\n\r\nb.   FATs for HPACs were carried out and subsequently, feedback and queries were shared by PN DY team. Response to each of the raised points was attached and shared with DY representatives.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-02 11:36:03	25	Oct 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
