350006	733	2022-06-04 05:46:25	1.   Submission of Test Benches for HSTD avionics and aerospace components. "Development of Test Benches for HSTD avionics and aerospace components" has been successfully completed and submitted against Milestone M3. \r\n\r\n2.   Design / Development Activities.\r\n   \r\na.   MARLIN-01 UAV.  Airframe manufacturing, assembly, avionics/ control / data link integration is completed.  Operational tests of airframe, propulsion, data link and control system are also completed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nb.   MARLIN-01 Backup. Manufacturing of an additional MARLIN-01 (as backup) including structural parts, skin sections, propulsion assembly, avionics assembly, avionics, and cooling system are completed. Ground testing is also successfully completed.\r\n\r\nc.   UAV Launcher. Design and manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01 Launcher / pneumatic circuit testing bench have been completed. Design and assembly of carriage deceleration / braking system has also been completed. The designed system has been successfully tested as well. To further improve speed performance, the pneumatic actuator has been replaced with a larger stroke actuator, the pulley ratio has been reduced and one more inlet is added to the accumulator vessel. \r\n\r\nd.   UAV Launcher Testing.   Initial testing of launcher with integrated control system and pneumatic circuit at low and medium pressures is completed. In-house testing of launcher at SPF is also completed successfully.  Field testing for dead weight and dummy UAV launches are successfully conducted at PN GHARO facility.  The criteria of projectile launch speed, aerial time and ground range are successfully met.\r\n\r\ne.   P220 Jet Engine Testing. Bench testing of P220 Turbo jet engine (for MARLIN-01) has been conducted. Intake duct design has been improved and manufactured. Bench testing of engine with improved intake is also conducted and results are within acceptable margins. \r\n\r\nf.   Backup P220 Jet Engine Testing. Maiden testing of backup P220 engine (MARLIN-01 backup) is also successfully completed.\r\n\r\ng.   P1000 Jet Engine Testing. Bench testing of P1000 Turbo jet engine (for MARLIN-02) has been conducted. Engine successfully started and thrust / temperature measurements are taken for design-adjustment of propulsion system assembly with airframe. \r\n\r\nh.   Ground Testing of Marlin-01 UAVs. Extensive ground testing activities of Marlin-01 UAVs are considered essential prior to the flight trials. In this regard, airframe load tests, pitch/roll performance testing of propulsion system, avionics endurance testing, data-link range tests, parachute release mechanism tests, control surface load tests, carriage-lock thrust testing are planned. Airframe load tests, pitch/roll performance testing of propulsion system and avionics endurance tests are successfully completed. Data link range tests and parachute release mechanism tests are partly completed. During control surface load testing, problem related to deformation of control linkages and servo failure was observed. Control linkage mechanism has been upgraded to increase stiffness and rigidity. Avionics system has been ruggedized based on root cause analysis of servo failure. Carriage-lock thrust testing of UAV has been successfully conducted at PN GHARO facility on 8 Mar 22.\r\n\r\nj.   Field / Flight Testing of Marlin-01 UAV. Field testing / launch trials of Marlin-01 UAV were planned at PN GHARO facility in Mar 22. For this purpose, leakage testing of launcher, site survey and coordination meeting between NRDI and NSTOC reps regarding recovery of HSTD from creek area was held on 24-25 Feb 22 vide reference PN/NRDI/ R AND D Wing/03/12462317 dated 18 Feb 22. The planned field trials of UAV were successfully conducted on 28 Mar 22. During launch phase Marlin-01 endured axial load of 13g, attained the height of ~2400 ft. (735 m) and reached speed of 336 kmph (93.4 m/s). Then during ~4.5 min flight, Marlin-01 completed two rounds of 4km radius and successfully pulled multiple 5g maneuvers. Post-flight data analysis is under progress for further improvement / consolidation of HSTD system. Another field test of MARLIN-01 is being planned to test improved flight parameters.\r\n\r\nk.   Design of MARLIN-02 (full-scale HSTD). The design has been revised based on the learning from design / manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01. Detailed design of airframe components and integration with launch / recovery systems are completed. CAD integration of avionics systems, data link, control mechanism and modifications pertaining to propulsion system are under progress. Pattern machining activities have been initiated for the completed airframe components. Pattern finishing activities and mold fabrication are also completed. Airframe manufacturing and control circuits assembly is also completed. MARLIN-02 is ready for ground testing. \r\n\r\nl.   Ground Testing of MARLIN-02 UAV. MTSS has requested NHQ for nomination inspection/ acceptance committee for conduct of ground test of MARLIN-02 UAV against milestone M4, vide reference MTSS/20/NRDI/HSTD-II/02 dated 13 Apr 22. Moreover, draft ATPs have also been forwarded for perusal vide Letter no. PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13317845 dated 21 May 22. \r\n\r\nm.   MARLIN-02 Launcher. MARLIN-02 launcher is re-designed based on the learning from design / development of MARLIN-01 Launcher. In this regard, considerations are given to weight reduction, ease of assembly and transportation. In order to keep the development cost and time efficient, imperative consideration is given to re-use of parts / sub-assemblies manufactured for the MARLIN-01 launcher. Export of manufacturing drawings, market surveys for COTS items and Bill of Material (BOM) compilation are completed. Sheet metal cutting and machining of metal parts is under progress. Subsequently, assembly of beam section and pressure testing will be undertaken. This will be followed by pressure testing of accumulator vessel and dead weight launch to validate the operating parameters.\r\n\r\nn.   Material Testing. Destructive Testing (DT) of composite material samples is being carried out using PNEC and PCSIR equipment. Tensile tests and first phase of bending tests are completed. Manufacturing process is improved in lines with the test results. Bending tests of improved samples are also completed. Testing of different composite coring materials are tested and coring scheme for MARLIN-02 is finalized. \r\n\r\np.   Wind Tunnel Testing. Computer Aided Design (CAD) model for development of testing model has been shared, as required by M/s DESTO.  Estimated quotation & timeline of 190 working days is received from the firm. M/s DESTO has been requested to reduce timeline. Foreign WTT facilities are also being explored for the pertinent testing. \r\n\r\n3.   Hardware Procurement & Testing Status.\r\n\r\na.   The ordered JetCat P-1000 (Germany based 1100N) turbo jet engine is successful procured. \r\n\r\nb.   Veronte flight controller (of M/s Embention) excluding air antenna is received at INTELL NRDI. Individual components have been tested and radio link is established. Firmware update has also been received for tracker. Currently, development of controls for HSTD are being studied and range testing activates are being planned.\r\n\r\nc.   Material & COTS items for fabrication of MARLIN-02 UAV and Launcher are being purchased in lines with manufacturing requirements.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-08-02 23:18:33	25	May 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350015	738	2022-06-04 05:59:24	1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Small Scale Weapon Field Testing. Preliminary Field testing was of 2.5 KW setup was conducted at RDS NATHIAGALI vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12427313 dated 16 Feb 22. The interference was observed with drone as target. Multiple targets such as Low Noise Amplifiers (LNAs), Phase Frequency Detectors (PFDs), RF rectifiers and RF Power Meters are being evaluated for disruptive demonstration. Field testing is scheduled to be conducted in early June 2022.\r\n\r\nb.   Horn Antenna Improvement. Horn antenna has been redesigned and fabricated resulting in better efficiency.  A testing was carried out at SPF with one horn antenna used for transmission, and another used for reception. A 47 dBm signal was transmitted at 2.45 GHz, and 13 dBm was received at reception antenna at 10 m, resulting in propagation loss of 34 dB. The exercise was aimed to simulate the in-band damage effect on a missile seeker. The 13 dBm signal is disruptive for LNAs and PFDs used in RADAR systems of missile seekers. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nc.   X-Band Experiment. RF devices are being designed and fabricated at X-band for use in power combination of pulsed M1475A 25 kW magnetrons. Power supplies and pulse modulators were procured and have undergone preliminary testing to ensure desired voltages are achieved at pertinent test points. The modulators will now be tested with X-band magnetrons. Waveguide adapters have also been fabricated and will be used for subsequent testing of other waveguide devices.\r\n\r\n2.   RF devices required for experimentation are being manufactured in-house. Details are appended in the table below:\r\n\r\na.   2.45 GHz Horn Antenna. \r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 01.\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. The device modeling was completed on 30 Mar 22, manufacturing completed on 07 April 22. \r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Device tested.\r\n\r\nb.   9.45GHz Horn Antenna. \r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 01.\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. The device modeling was completed on 17 Mar 22, manufacturing completed on 13 April 22. \r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Testing of device is pending till the availability of VNA.\r\n\r\nc.   9GHz Termination. \r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 04.\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. 01 Termination modeling was completed on 20 April 22, manufacturing completed on 26 April 22. \r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Testing of device is complete.\r\n\r\nd.   Directional Coupler (71 dB).\r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 02\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. 01 Directional coupler modeling was completed on 18 March 22. Manufacturing was completed on 07 April 22.\r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Testing of device is pending till the availability of VNA.\r\n\r\ne.   Adapters.\r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 10\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. 04 adapters modeling was completed on 18 March 22. Manufacturing was completed on 25 April 22. Devices were re-manufactured with improved designed 23 May 22.\r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Testing of device is pending till the availability of VNA.\r\n\r\nf.   Directional Couplers (51dB).\r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 02\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. 01 Directional coupler modeling was completed on 06 April 22. Manufacturing was completed on 28 April 22.\r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Testing of device is pending till the availability of VNA.\r\n\r\ng.   Circulator.\r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 04\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. 01 circulator modeling was completed on 06 April 22. Manufacturing was completed on 23 May 22.\r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Testing of device is pending till the manufacturing f flange.\r\n\r\nh.   Waveguide Termination.\r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 04\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. Modeling and manufacturing is pending.\r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Device Manufacturing is pending.\r\n\r\nj.   Microstrip Circulator.\r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 02\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. Modeling and manufacturing is pending.\r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Device Manufacturing is pending.\r\n\r\nk.   Casegrain Antenna.\r\n(1)   Quantity. Total required = 01\r\n(2)   Timeline/Expected Completion Date. Modeling and manufacturing is pending.\r\n(3)   Status/Remarks. Device Manufacturing is pending.\r\n\r\n3.   RF Power Amplifier. Biasing circuit PCB has been redesigned with adequate track width suitable for high drain current. The matching networks of the 100 Watt amplifier have also been redesigned employing Simplified Real Frequency Technique (SRFT) for output MN and Bounded Performance Technique (BPT) for input MN. PCB fabrication has been completed; PCB component population is in progress and will be available for testing in early Jun 22. Initial testing of the biasing circuit is being conducted with a 15 W GaN transistor to ensure correct operation, prior testing with expensive 100 W transistors.\r\n\r\n4.   Following studies are being conducted to formulate research plans for combination of X-band magnetrons for more effective DEW design: \r\n\r\na.   A pulsed power supply based on Pulsed Forming Networks (PFN) required to drive pulsed magnetrons is currently being designed in-house.\r\n\r\nb.   Preliminary design of RF devices including circulators and directional couplers at X-band (9 GHz) has been finalized. RF devices are under fabrication and testing stages.\r\n\r\n5.   Technical proposal amounting PKR 232M for Phase II pertaining to power combination of multiple J-band pulsed magnetrons of redundant AM-39 has been submitted to NHQ for approval. An anechoic RF chamber will also be designed and fabricated to enable shielded high-power testing of the magnetron combination experiment with adequate safety measures. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n6.   The proposal for future plan was also submitted vide Ref no PN/DGNRDI/RNDWING/03/11409776 dated 21 Nov 21 in which Power Combination of multiple 25Kw pulsed J-band magnetrons, to achieve 150 kW combined power, is to be undertaken. Following are the salient highlights of the approach. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\na.   Pulsed operation philosophy will yield lower operational cost, lesser cooling requirement, higher lethality compared to CW.\r\n\r\nb.   J-band RF devices will be smaller in size and can be efficiently tailored for installation onboard naval platform.\r\n\r\n7.   Scan Eagle. INTELL NRDI RF team visited PNS MAKRAN to conduct defect diagnosis in the RF end of Scan Eagle GCS AIM and Directional Antenna. \r\n\r\na.   Antenna was found to be mechanically deformed and mismatched at S-band.    Defect rectification was attempted on-site and antenna VSWR parameters were significantly improved. INTELL was also approached to design a new antenna based on solid dish, for which the team took all design measurements on-site. The design study for the antenna is currently in progress. PPF forms are awaited from NHQ, which once received will help ensure proper utilization of developed HR and computational resources at INTELL. \r\n\r\nb.   RF paths of three of the AIMs were also tested at INTELL on VNA. The mechanical filters of two of the systems were found degraded. PPF form for development of these filters is awaited from NHQ.\r\n\r\n8.   GPS Band stop Filter. PN DY approached NRDI INTELL for GPS deactivation of INMARSAT TT3020-C. INTELL proposed development of an absorptive reflection-less GPS band stop filter to ensure protection of low power elements such as LNAs and MUX in the transceiver circuitry from high power reflection signals. A 3rd order band stop microstrip absorptive filter is designed and is currently under final fabrication stages. Subsequent testing will be conducted on VNA.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-08-02 23:18:48	25	May 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350009	568	2021-11-01 19:44:12	1.   Testing Exercises. EH-01 testing exercises were executed to test efficacy of all deployed EH-01 systems vide NHQ Letter PN/SECURITY OPS DTE/03/3143226 dated 28 Aug 21. Following observations were reported vide Letter PN/HQ COASTAL COMMAND/03/I0724465 dated 05 Oct 21:\r\na.   GPS jamming was found satisfactory. \r\nb.   Tele-command jamming was found intermittent.\r\n\r\n2.   EH-01 Trial Scenario. Trials were conducted without considering threat scenario. The tests were conducted while operator and UAV were in close range. Typically, operators don’t jam beyond 1 km due to following:\r\na.   RTH function is not available due to jamming.\r\nb.   Operators’ concerns with supply chain of DJI Mavic.\r\n\r\n3.   Presentation on Threat Scenarios. Dir. Sensors presented threat scenario details to DCNS(M) and DCNS(O) dated 22nd Oct 21. Alternate test/ exercise methodology is also proposed to all concerned units.\r\n\r\n4.   EH-01 Warranty. All deliverables and technical milestones of EH-01 have been successfully completed. The project is under warranty period, ending in May 22. NRDI INTELL teams have been readily available and active in maintenance/ troubleshooting activities during warranty period. Unit/site-wise details of received Opdef and defect mitigation strategy by NRDI team are given below:\r\n\r\na.   LSS-14. \r\n(1)   Reported Defect. GPS jamming was reported to be in-effective.\r\n(2)   Rectification. The GPS jamming antenna was found to be broken. Subsequently, new GPS jamming antenna was provided.\r\n(3)   Status. EH-01 System operational.\r\n\r\nb.   3rd FP, GWADAR. \r\n(1)   Reported Defect. Tele-command Jamming was reported to be intermittent.\r\n(2)   Rectification. RF cable from PA to Front panel was found defective. Subsequently, the RF cable replaced.\r\n(3)   Current Status. EH-01 System operational.\r\n\r\nc.   6th FP, ORMARA. \r\n(1)   Reported Defect. Tele-command Jamming was reported to be intermittent.\r\n(2)   Rectification. No physical defect was observed. The defect was mitigated through Software Patch update.\r\n(3)   Current Status. EH-01 System operational.\r\nd.   PNAD, PNS AATISH. \r\n(1)   Reported Defect. Tele-command Jamming was reported to be intermittent.\r\n(2)   Rectification. No physical defect was observed. The defect was mitigated through software Patch update.\r\n(3)   Current Status. EH-01 System operational.\r\n\r\ne.   LSS LIAQUAT. \r\n(1)   Reported Defect. GPS & Tele-command jamming was reported to be non-operational.\r\n(2)   Rectification. GPS and Tele-command PA were found to be defective. Moreover, Tele-command and GPS jamming antenna were also found to be broken. Subsequently, the GPS and Tele-command PA were replaced along with the GPS and Tele-command jamming antenna.\r\n(3)   Current Status. EH-01 system operational.\r\n\r\nf.   1st FP, NRC ISB. \r\n(1)   Reported Defect. GPS jamming is reported to be non-operational\r\n(2)   Rectification. GPS PA is reported to be not working. Subsequently, rectification team along with spare GPS PA will be sent to ISB in early Nov 21.\r\n(3)   Current Status. Rectification is in-process.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-02 11:35:14	25	Oct 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
