350004	572	2021-11-01 19:44:43	\r\n1.   Change in The Scope of Project. The project scope has been revised in VCNS IHD meeting, vide reference PN/ NDR DIV/ R AND D DTE/03/3240447 dated 05 Oct 21. Operating range of UCAV is limited to 200 km and BLOS operation requirements are eliminated. In this regard, SATCOM and EOIR systems are also removed from the scope. The timeline is also revised to 18 months. Project plan, itemized cost and pertinent details finalization are under progress at NRDI INTELL. Same will be reported by mid of Nov 21.\r\n\r\n2.   Critical Design of UCAV. Study on selection of actuators for control surfaces and landing gear is being undertaken. Design of fuel supply circuit and linkage for retraction mechanism of landing gear are in progress. Actuators for control surfaces and landing gear will be selected after design studies are completed. \r\n\r\n3.   Test Bench for ROTEX Engine. Design of test bench for ROTAX 914 engine has been completed. Manufacturing drawings have been handed over to vendor and manufacturing is in process. Final QC of mechanical design will be conducted once received. Procurement of components for electrical panel has been completed, including a custom designed casing. Integration of electrical components are in progress.\r\n\r\n4.   ELINT Module. TUALCOM ELINT module has been tested against different generated signals across specified range. The module was able to detect signals of different frequencies generated from a software defined radio (SDR) in lab environment. \r\n\r\n5.   Mission Computer Test Bench. Study on algorithms for mission computer is ongoing and development of algorithm will follow the conclusion of study.\r\n\r\n6.   Machine Shop. Machine tools for Hartford 4-axis CNC have been shortlisted for procurement. Lathe machine has been procured and commissioned. Additional tools for lathe machine have been ordered and the machine is being used in part manufacturing. Backup power requirements for additional equipment (PCs, Desktop CNC, 3D Printer) have been calculated and suitable models are being shortlisted.\r\n\r\n7.   Team development. In-house interviews for hardware design engineers are being conducted.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-02 11:35:51	25	Oct 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	275	2020-11-30 11:55:56	1.   Lab Development. Lab Development has been completed with installation of ESD mats, earthing point and power sockets. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Magnetron Injection Locking Simulation. Modelling and simulation studies to evaluate injection locking principles have been completed. The observations have chalked out the requirements to develop sophisticated control loops, in order to enable frequency-injection and phase locking of free running magnetrons. This will furnish bandwidth reduction for efficient power combining of multiple frequency-injection-phase locked magnetrons. Work is in progress to design and implement the above mentioned control loops; details are provided in ensuing para. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Control System Designing for Frequency Pushing.\r\n\r\na.   Design of control circuit PCB based on PLL IC, required for frequency locking has been completed, and development has been started. Pertinent components required are being procured.\r\nb.   Design of control circuitry required for phase matching of magnetron response with the phase of injection signal is in progress.\r\n\r\n4.   RF Devices. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks, and waveguide directional couplers, are required in project experimentation. As limited funds have been released, in-house design and development of RF devices is in progress.\r\n\r\na.   The fabrication of waveguide circulator and directional coupler has been completed. \r\nb.   A constant current power supply required for biasing the electromagnets and tuning the circulator response has been designed and fabricated.\r\nc.   Testing of fabricated RF devices is in progress. Pertinent test equipment Gauss Meter has been procured.\r\nd.   Design of phase shifter required for phase matching of two magnetrons, in order to accomplish efficient power combining, has been completed. Procurement of the required components is in progress.\r\n\r\n5.   RF Power Amplifier.\r\n\r\na.   In-house design and optimization of 100W power amplifier (PA) has been completed. PCB manufacturing is also completed. Heat sink design has been completed and is being fabricated. Soldering of components on manufactured PCB is in progress. QC sheets for safe testing of the designed and developed RF PA are also being prepared.\r\nb.   Preamplifier required for requisite RF power input is being designed. IC procurement of the same is in progress. \r\n\r\n6.   Hardware Procurement. Project experimentation based on injection locking experimentation of a single magnetron will first be carried out to validate simulated results.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement of experimental components including coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, waveguide transitions, waveguide terminations, waveguide adapters, programmable switch mode power supplies and FPGA boards is in process. \r\nb.   Electronics systems required for injection locking of single magnetron including Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs and Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) ICs are also being procured.\r\nc.   IT equipment required for computational modelling and multiphysics simulations of RF devices have been procured.\r\n\r\n7.   Anechoic Chamber. Feasibility study on in-house development of anechoic chamber is completed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n8.   Other Projects. SATCOM Antenna of PNS/M HASHMAT, TT-3005M was tested onboard VNA. Specialized set up was also made at INTELL to power up the active antenna. The malfunctioned LNA (low noise Amplifier)/ HPA (High Power Amplifier) PCB was identified.	DSensors	Edited	2020-12-28 11:33:21	25	Nov 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350002	276	2020-11-30 11:56:06	1.   GPS Spoofing Hardware Development.\r\n\r\na.   Hardware Assembly. Ruggedized housing and assembly of spoofing PoC equipment is completed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\nb.   Development of End user GUI. The GUI has been updated to make it more user friendly. Beta testing on the software is completed and subsequently associated recommendations have been implemented. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nc.   Laboratory Trials. Using the newly assembled ruggedized housing and spoofing PoC assembly, successful in-house trials have been conducted. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nd.   Product Manuals. The technical and operator manuals for the product have been developed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\ne.   Acceptance Trials. Acceptance trials have been conducted successfully in the field on 13 Nov 20, at PN GHARO site. Acceptance by the committee has been reported vide letter PN/HQ PAK MARINES/2ND FP BN/03/7405148 dated 25 Nov 20. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Serial Production. Deployment of Drone Jammers and Spoofing systems while considering FP and GBAD setups vis-à-vis functionality of Project Eagle Hunt deliverables was presented to COMCOAST on 16 Nov 20 vide letter PN/ HQ COSTAL COMMAND/03/7250666.\r\n\r\n3.   Force Majeure has been invoked by DITD due COVID pandemic. The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR is also delayed due to export permit processing delays caused by COVID 19 pandemic. Once 3D X-band RADAR will be received, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of Eagle Hunt -3C version (autonomous GPS spoofing using X-band RADAR). 3D RADARs from other OEMs are also being explored.\r\n\r\n4.   Housing of reactive jamming equipment in the marinized container is in progress. The INTELL team visited the M/s RIMS facility and finalized the contours of equipment installation. The said activity will be completed by end Dec 20.\r\n\r\n5.   Miscellaneous Studies Supporting PN Fleet and Repair Agencies undertaken during reporting period\r\n\r\na.   PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) training. OJT of 07 Dockyard Lab staff comprising of theory classes and demonstration labs on Omniscan MX2 PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) equipment is completed.\r\n\r\nb.   Ultrasonic Testing (UT) of Besconds used in the cable hull passage onboard S/Ms. UT of a locally developed Balezona & Neoprene based besconds, along with NG besconds was undertaken. No flaws / defects were found in NG bescond, while locally developed besconds were found defected. \r\n\r\nc.   500W High Power Antenna for PAF. Two more antennas have been fabricated, one of which was handed over to PAF for high power testing. High power antenna testing was conducted at PAF 606 Workshop Badaber, which revealed satisfactory results. Range testing and in-situ thermal testing of the antenna are in progress.	DSensors	Edited	2020-12-28 11:31:52	25	Nov 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
