350010	582	2021-12-03 09:10:00	\r\n1.   Procurement. 24 VFDs and Keypads have been received from Taiwan. Testing of received items has been carried out and all items are operational. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Test Bench Design. In house developed test bench has been completed. Testing has been carried out using returned 11T and 150T VFDs. Functionality of test bench has been verified.  Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   FATs of Completed VFDs. The design and execution of VFD for Fats for Battery Fans (FC-V), Hydraulic pumps (DT), Water Regulation pump (DM), have been carried out and sent to dockyard for further testing with DY team.\r\n\r\n4.   Design of VFDs. Mechanical and electrical design of cooling pump VFDs DK1 and DK 2 are near finalization and will be completed till end Nov 21.\r\n\r\n5.   Appreciation Letter. Timely delivery of 150T VFD for DA pump after successful modification of PN S/M KHALID is highly appreciated by PND vide letter PN/PN DOCKYARD/ S/M WING/GM (ME S/M WING)/03/10930706 dated 21 Oct 21. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n6.   Provision of Three Speeds on DA-Pump VFD. Activity to enable third speed on DA pump VFD has been carried out by NRDI INTELL team. Team visited dockyard and carried out replacement activity of the installed VFD on board S/M. Testing of the same has been carried out by DY team as well and performance was found to be in-line with requested URD.\r\n\r\n7.   Correspondence. Following correspondence has been carried out. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\na.   Queries regarding electrical panel design along with the preliminary panel for Hydraulic pump have been forwarded to DY team. Once approved and accepted by DY team, the electrical panel will be implemented by NRDI INTELL.\r\n\r\nb.   FATs for HPAC VFDs are successfully completed. HPAC VFDs will be handed over to PND on 7 Dec 21 for workshop trials.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-31 10:00:10	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350004	587	2021-12-03 09:10:32	1.   Change in The Scope of Project. The project scope has been revised in VCNS IHD meeting, vide reference PN/ NDR DIV/ R AND D DTE/03/3240447 dated 05 Oct 21. Operating range of UCAV is limited to 200 km and BLOS operation requirements are eliminated. In this regard, SATCOM and EOIR systems are also removed from the scope. The timeline is also revised to 18 months. Itemized cost estimates for procurement plan and pertinent details are submitted vide reference PN/DG NRDI/ At PNS JAUHAR/03/11526644 dated 29 Nov 21. \r\n\r\n2.   Critical Design of UCAV. Study on selection of actuators for control surfaces and landing gear is being undertaken. Electrohydraulic servo valve systems are being considered to implement a fully redundant control system for control surfaces. Upon conclusion of study, quotations will be requested from vendors for relevant components/systems. Circuit design of fuel supply system is completed. Design of linkage for retraction mechanism of landing gear is in progress. Actuators for control surfaces and landing gear will be selected after design studies are completed. \r\n\r\n3.   Test Bench for ROTAX Engine. Test bench for ROTAX 914 engine has been manufactured and detailed QC of manufactured frame has been carried out. Integration of electrical components in control panel has been completed. Mounting of engine onto the test bench is completed and integration of fuel and cooling circuits along with some peripherals is in progress. Overall mounting of mechanical and electrical components will be completed in Nov ‘21 and engine will be ready for ignition and testing in early Dec 21.\r\n\r\n4.   ELINT Module. TUALCOM ELINT module has been tested against different generated signals across specified range. The module was able to detect signals of different frequencies generated from a software defined radio (SDR) in lab environment. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n5.   Mission Computer Test Bench. Study on algorithms for mission computer is ongoing and development of algorithm will follow the conclusion of study. Integration of sensors with available flight controller will be carried out and different interfaces available (CAN, RS232, RS485, GPIO) will be used to integrate sensors.\r\n\r\n6.   Machine Shop. The Hartford 4-axis CNC Milling Machine is ready at OEM facility. Inspection trial has been conducted and accuracy report is received for acceptance. Machine tools have also been ordered. Backup power requirements for additional equipment (PCs, Desktop CNC, 3D Printer) have been calculated and suitable models are being shortlisted. Moreover, a curing oven for undertaking manufacturing of large parts has been designed in-house. Design specifications have been forwarded to vendor and the oven is currently under fabrication. \r\n\r\n7.   Team development. In-house interviews for hardware design engineers have been conducted and suitable candidates for hiring have been shortlisted.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-31 09:52:08	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350014	577	2021-12-02 18:58:00	\r\n1.   Design. A detail study on engineering design of ship-based gyro stabilized platform has been carried out. It is being optimized for PN ships.\r\n\r\n2.   Modelling and Simulation. Detailed CAD model of GSP has been developed based on URD. Forward kinematics equations have been generated for the platform. Study on inverse kinematics is underway. Sim-scape® simulations have been carried out. The obtained model will be used to generate control loop in Matlab and Simulink. Hardware integration of controller with Matlab environment will be undertaken.\r\n\r\n3.   Design Engineering Study. Design Engineering study has been submitted according to Milestone 3. The same will be processed by acceptance committee, upon its formulation, as per the requirement of work order. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n4.   Procurement. Electronics components for scaled down model have been procured. Raw materials for structure will be procured and frame manufacturing will be started accordingly.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-31 09:58:51	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
