350003	603	2021-12-31 09:43:31	\r\n1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Small Scale Weapon Demonstration. \r\n\r\n(1)   Demonstration of the irreversible damage caused on an electronic circuit through combined power of 02x 1 kW magnetrons is being planned. The setup has been tested at SPF with high power termination.\r\n\r\n(2)   Suitable location has been selected for weapon demonstration at RDS NATHIAGALI AOR. The demonstration will be conducted with adequate safeties in place, for which QC sheets have been prepared. Field demonstration layout has also been finalized. Work Order 2 of Phase I is currently awaited, for demonstration to be conducted.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Power Amplifier. Biasing circuit PCB has been redesigned with adequate track width suitable for high drain current. The Matching networks of the 100 Watt amplifier have been redesigned employing Simplified Real Frequency Technique (SRFT) for output MN and Bounded Performance Technique (BPT) for input MN. Layout design and EM co-simulation of the amplifier is also completed. Procurement of the components and adequate heat sink is in progress.\r\n\r\n2.   Following procurement actions are in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement Completed. Experimental components including 1 kW magnetrons, coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs, FPGA boards, Spectrum Analyzer, Switch Mode Power Supplies, 1 kW waveguide terminations, N52 magnets, Oscilloscope, 2.5 kW waveguide terminations, E-field probe, Signal Generator, DC power supply, refractory material for waveguide termination, 5 kW generator, and Automatic Voltage Regulator for RF lab have been completed. \r\n\r\nb.   Procurement in Progress. Lumped components for in-house designed RFPA, PCB fabrication services and adequate heatsink for the RFPA are in progress.\r\n\r\n3.   Following studies are being conducted to formulate research plans for combination of X-band magnetrons in ensuing years: \r\n\r\na.   A pulsed power supply based on Pulsed Forming Networks (PFN) required to drive pulsed magnetrons is currently being designed.\r\n\r\nb.   Preliminary design of RF devices including circulators and directional couplers at X-band (9 GHz) has been finalized.\r\n\r\n4.   Technical proposal amounting PKR 260M for Phase II pertaining to power combination of multiple J-band pulsed magnetrons of redundant AM-39 has been submitted to NHQ for approval. An anechoic RF chamber will also be designed and fabricated to enable shielded high-power testing of the magnetron combination experiment with adequate safety measures.\r\n\r\n5.   WO-II amounting Rs 30M has been issued on 30 Nov 21.	DR&D	Finalized	2021-12-31 09:44:15	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
