350014	629	2022-01-02 15:47:41	\r\n1.   Design. A detailed study on engineering design of ship-based gyro stabilized platform has been carried out. It is being optimized for PN ships. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Modelling and Simulation. A detailed CAD model of GSP has been developed based on URD. Forward kinematics equations have been generated for the platform. A study on inverse kinematics is underway. Sim-scape® simulations have been carried out. The obtained model has been used to generate a control loop in Matlab and Simulink. Hardware integration of the controller with the Matlab environment has been carried out.\r\n3.   Design Engineering Study. Design engineering study has been submitted according to milestone 3. The same will be processed by acceptance committee, upon its formulation, as per the requirement of work order. NHQ comments on DES vide reference letter no. NCW/WO/LOS VTS/II/664 are adequately responded and updated DES has been submitted. \r\n\r\n4.   Development of Scaled Down Model of GSP. A scaled down model of GSP has been developed in-house to validate the calculated range of motion and forces for the platform and linkages. The scaled down model has been designed to retain the full range of motion in roll (± 25?) and pitch (± 15?) as outlined in the URD, along with a capability to carry upto 1kg of payload. Electronic components for scaled down model have been procured along with raw materials for structure and frame and construction has been completed. The range of motion in roll and pitch for the system, acquired using kinematics models have been validated using the scaled down model. Development of scaled down model will provide confidence in full scale GSP development. Point recommended to be dropped\r\n\r\n5.   Algorithm Development. The control algorithm for GSP has been extensively studied and different approaches have been implemented in Matlab. The most optimized approach in terms of system response time was observed using the inverse kinematics model along with PID. A study is underway to fine-tune different parameters and achieve desired rates and positions, minimizing errors.\r\n\r\n6.   PN Ship Visit. INTELL team visit PNS MOAWIN to ascertain the final placement of full scale GSP. Ship’s bridge top was selected as the ideal location due to ample space, proximity to electrical systems and bridge where LOS VTS receiver can be placed. INTELL team will carry out detailed designs of deck space and a rugged base platform for the full scale model to be mounted.\r\n\r\n7.   Procurement. Electronics components for the scaled-down model have been procured along with raw materials for structure and frame. Shortlisted stepper motors and drivers for full-scale models as well as the universal joints have also been procured. The manufacturing of the full-scale model is currently in progress. Fabrication and assembly will be completed in early Jan’ 21 and manufacturing QC will be initiated.\r\n\r\n?	DSensors	Finalized	2022-01-04 14:44:58	25	Dec 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350012	631	2022-01-02 15:48:12	\r\n1.   Work Order Issuance. The T0 is established as 10 Jun 21 vide letter ILS/0620/INVENTORY MODEL dated 03 Aug 21. Formulation of the acceptance committee as per the requirement of work order is in progress. Point Recommended to be dropped. \r\n\r\n2.   Finalized Case Study. A detailed case study of Machining Control System (MCS) of YARMOOK class ship and SR-60 RADAR has been carried out. The case study was reviewed by NCMA and INTELL NRDI team incorporated the recommendations. Finalized Case Study report submitted against Milestone-3 for release of funds has been evaluated and supported vide PN/NCMA/03/10738145 dated 06 Oct 21. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   SR-60 RADAR. A detailed study on SR-60 RADAR has been carried out. Technical documentation and defect history of the RADAR has been received. A visit was carried out by the project team to identify potential data acquisition points for periodic NDT data collection and shortlist data-loggers deployment locations inside the RADAR cabinet. The team visited SR-60 RADAR onboard PNS ASLAT on 29th October 2021 to analyze actual operational and environmental conditions of a functional RADAR system. The team performed thermal, magnetic and ultrasonic non-destructive testing at accessible data acquisition points. The shortlisted data acquisition points and NDT data collection methodology was also briefed to the accompanied FMG staff. The recorded NDT data is maintained in a historical database for analytics. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n4.   Deployment of Dataloggers. Magnetic flux leakage and environmental monitoring sensors have been developed and tested for recording environmental and magnetic data. The developed dataloggers have been installed on SR-60 RADAR and MCS onboard PN Ships. Point recommended to be dropped. \r\n\r\n5.   Coordination meeting with PN FMG for NDT data acquisition. A meeting was held at NRDI INTELL on 13 Dec 21 vide reference PN/DG NRDI/At PNS JAUHAR/03/11802413 dated 17 Dec 21. The NDT data acquisition methodology for the project was finalized in the meeting. The NDT data comprising of thermal and ultrasonic data will be periodically acquired by FMG team depending upon the availability of Ship/vessel. \r\n\r\n6.   Acquisition of Environmental data. The NRDI team acquires the environmental data from PN Ship/vessel on monthly basis. The data was retrieved from the deployed data loggers. Moreover, the team also replaces the battery packs of the data loggers during their visit. The data was acquired by NRDI team vide PN/NCMA/03/11884712 dated 27 Dec 21 for the month of Dec 21. \r\n\r\n7.   Historical Database Development. A historical database is being developed to record the acquired environmental and NDT data from PN ships/vessels. The database is being analyzed at NRDI. Subsequently, data analytics is being performed on the database for estimation of degradation parameter.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-01-04 14:45:20	25	Dec 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350010	632	2022-01-02 15:48:18	\r\n1.   Procurement. 24 VFDs and Keypads have been received from Taiwan. Testing of received items has been carried out and all items are operational. \r\n\r\n2.   Test Bench Design. In house developed test bench has been completed. Testing has been carried out using returned 11T and 150T VFDs. Functionality of test bench has been verified.  \r\n\r\n3.   Factory Acceptance Trials.  Factory Acceptance Trials of 02 Air Conditioner VFDs, 02 Fresh Water VFDs and 02 Sea Water VFDs were carried out in the presence of PNDY representatives on 20th December 2021 at NRDI and after complete functionality testing all the 06 VFDs were handed over to PNDY representatives. This concluded the FATs of all 19 VFDs to be developed under this work order.\r\n\r\n4.   Workshop Acceptance Trials. Workshop Acceptance Trials of the 06 VFDs were carried out on 21st December 2021 at PNDY workshop. The safety checks for all 06 VFDs were carried out successfully in the presence of ship staff, PNDY and NRDI representatives. This concluded the Workshop Acceptance Trials of all 19 VFDs to be developed under this work order.   \r\n\r\n5.   VFDs Handing Over. As of 21st December 2021, 19 VFDs for 09 different applications were handed over to PNDY with satisfactory Factory & Workshop Acceptance Trials   \r\n\r\n6.   Appreciation Letter. Timely delivery of 150T VFD for DA pump after successful modification of PN S/M KHALID is highly appreciated by PND vide letter PN/PN DOCKYARD/ S/M WING/GM (ME S/M WING)/03/10930706 dated 21 Oct 21. Point recommended to be dropped\r\n\r\n7.   Provision of Three Speeds on DA-Pump VFD. Activity to enable third speed on DA pump VFD has been carried out by NRDI INTELL team. Team visited dockyard and carried out replacement activity of the installed VFD on board S/M. Testing of the same has been carried out by DY team as well and performance was found to be in-line with requested URD. Point recommended to be dropped\r\n\r\n8.   Correspondence. Following correspondence has been carried out. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\na.   Queries regarding electrical panel design along with the preliminary panel for Hydraulic pump have been forwarded to DY team. Once approved and accepted by DY team, the electrical panel will be implemented by NRDI INTELL.\r\n\r\nb.   FATs for HPAC VFDs are successfully completed. HPAC VFDs will be handed over to PND on 7 Dec 21 for workshop trials.\r\n\r\n9.   Documentation Finalization Meeting. The meeting was held at NRDI INTELL on 28 Dec 21 to consolidate document format of already delivered VFDs. Reps from PND and NCMA were attended the said meeting.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-01-04 14:45:41	25	Dec 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
