350002	327	2021-02-01 10:55:00	1.   Force Majeure has been invoked by DITD due COVID pandemic. The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR was delayed due to export permit processing delays caused by COVID 19 pandemic. However, due to persisting export permit issues, two other 3D RADARS (Chinese origin) have been shortlisted. Procurement of the same is in progress. Once 3D X-band RADARs are received, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of Eagle Hunt -3C version (autonomous GPS spoofing using X-band RADAR).\r\n\r\n2.   Housing of reactive jamming equipment in the marinized container is in progress.  Equipment installation activity will be completed by end-Feb 21.\r\n\r\n3.   Miscellaneous Studies Supporting PN Fleet and Repair Agencies undertaken during reporting period.\r\n\r\na.   500 Watt High Power Antenna for PAF. PAF 606 Workshop conducted thermal testing of the antenna during high power operation, which revealed satisfactory results. Measurement of radiation pattern in anechoic chamber, and high power range testing also revealed satisfactory results. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Testing of SATCOM Systems onboard PNS/Ms. INTELL team visited PNS/M HASHMAT and PNS/M HURMAT for RF path testing of SATCOM systems, with coaxial terminations replacing antennas. Two antennas from these S/Ms were also tested in INTELL Lab on VNA and a detailed report was submitted to GM W & S for facilitation in defect rectification. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nc.   Air Drop Logistics Container (ADLC). Study assigned by NHQ is undertaken to determine drop trajectory, descent rate / terminal velocity and selection of optimal parachute system for ADLCs. Detailed analysis is carried out to compute these characteristics. In this regards, detailed structural analysis has been done to evaluate of the stress concentration and to determine related failure modes. Subsequently, design modifications are suggested to prevent failure and increase fatigue life of the structure. Finally, serial production plan, manufacturing drawing of mold / patterns and Quality Assurance (QA) methods are specified.\r\n\r\nd.   Computational Modeling of SARDOM Radome on-board PNS S/Ms. INTELL was approached to undertake computational study on the S/M SATCOM Radome and suggest design improvements to prevent structural failure and improve fatigue life. A broken sample of S/M Radome and OEM drawings have been received. Method of Finite Element Analysis (FEA) is implemented for stress analysis to determine the stress concentration and fatigue life of structure. Electro-Magnetic (EM) analysis is also performed to determine attenuation characteristics of the structure. Design modification is being done to reduce stress concentration and increase fatigue life of the structure with minimal changes in the EM attenuation characteristics. Finally, manufacturing drawings have been given and manufacturing process is specified. NHQ vide letter  PN/SMM Dte/03/2728197 promulgated that the Radomes be manufactured in lines with newer design proposed by INTELL and submarine Radomes be replaced progressively.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-02-17 09:25:12	25	Jan 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
