350003	638	2022-01-02 15:48:53	\r\n1.   Following activities pertaining to in-house development and experimentation were carried out:\r\n\r\na.   Small Scale Weapon Demonstration. \r\n\r\n(1)   Demonstration of the irreversible damage caused on an electronic circuit through combined power of 02x 1 kW magnetrons is being planned. The setup has been tested at SPF with high power termination.\r\n\r\n(2)   Suitable location has been selected for weapon demonstration at RDS NATHIAGALI AOR. The demonstration will be conducted with adequate safeties in place, for which QC sheets have been prepared. Field demonstration layout has also been finalized. Safety procedures and target finalization is in progress.\r\n\r\nb.   RF Power Amplifier. Biasing circuit PCB has been redesigned with adequate track width suitable for high drain current. The Matching networks of the 100 Watt amplifier have been redesigned employing Simplified Real Frequency Technique (SRFT) for output MN and Bounded Performance Technique (BPT) for input MN. Layout design and EM co-simulation of the amplifier is also completed. Response has also been simulated with practical components using manufacturer provided s2p files. Procurement of the components and adequate heat sink is in progress.\r\n\r\n2.   Following procurement actions are in progress to undertake the required experimentation.\r\n\r\na.   Procurement in Progress. Lumped components for in-house designed RFPA, PCB fabrication services and adequate heatsink for the RFPA are in progress.\r\n\r\n3.   Following studies are being conducted to formulate research plans for combination of X-band magnetrons in ensuing years: \r\n\r\na.   A pulsed power supply based on Pulsed Forming Networks (PFN) required to drive pulsed magnetrons is currently being designed.\r\n\r\nb.   Preliminary design of RF devices including circulators and directional couplers at X-band (9 GHz) has been finalized. \r\n\r\n4.   Technical proposal amounting PKR 232M for Phase II pertaining to power combination of multiple J-band pulsed magnetrons of redundant AM-39 has been submitted to NHQ for approval. An anechoic RF chamber will also be designed and fabricated to enable shielded high-power testing of the magnetron combination experiment with adequate safety measures. \r\n\r\n5.   The proposal for future plan was also submitted vide Ref no PN/DGNRDI/RNDWING/03/11409776 dated 21ST Nov 21 in which Power Combination of multiple 25Kw pulsed J-band magnetrons, to achieve 150 kW combined power, is to be undertaken. Following are the salient highlights of the approach.\r\n\r\n\r\na.   It is envisaged that 150 kW power will be lethal to electronics placed at a distance of 10Km when connected with highly directional & high power rated antenna.\r\n\r\nb.   Pulsed operation philosophy will yield lower operational cost, lesser cooling requirement, higher lethality compared to CW.\r\n\r\nc.   J-band RF devices will be smaller in size and can be efficiently tailored for installation onboard naval platform.\r\n\r\nd.   Subsequently, the 150 kW DEW Poc will be advanced to higher powers as well as will be tailored for installation onboard naval platforms.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-01-04 14:45:25	25	Dec 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
