350002	87	2020-04-02 00:00:00	1.   Ruggedized UAV Jammer (Eagle Hunt-01)\r\n\r\n   a.   Serial production and through life supportability (TLS) of 10 jammers at NRDI is approved. The facility for serial production is also allocated at PNS KARSAZ.\r\n\r\n   b.   The detailed upgradation/requirement plan along with case for re-appropriation of the allocated facility is also forwarded to HQ COMKAR for approval. Work order issuance is under process at NHQ.\r\n\r\n2.   Reactive Jamming. \r\n\r\n   a.   In order to undertake long range field testing of reactive jamming system; Software Defined Radios (SDRs) and Power Amplifier (PAs) are required. Procurement orders for the same have also been placed through MTSS. EDD is end April 2020\r\n\r\n   b.   In-house modelling and simulation of pyramidal HORN antenna for 1-6 GHz has been finalized. Procurement orders for the same have also been placed through MTSS. EDD is end April 2020\r\n\r\n3.   GPS Spoofing. \r\n\r\n   a.   Field testing of the counterfeit signal generated from the BRDC (Broadcast Ephemeris) files have been successfully conducted.\r\n\r\n   b.   Successful field trials were also conducted to vary the altitude of the GPS signal while the UAV is in autonomous mode.\r\n\r\n   c.   X-Band RADAR is required for continuous feedback of UAV’s position. Procurement order of X-Band RADAR has been placed. EDD is Apr 20. 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of GPS spoofing milestone upon receipt of requisite equipment.\r\n\r\n4.   Scaled-Down UCAV Model. Manufacturing of Scaled-Down UCAV Model has commenced in UAV Lab. Mold layup of various parts (bottom-tail, upper v-tail and both wings) have been completed. CAD model of engine test bench and electronic components has been finalized. These electronic components are required to determine RPM, temperature, thrust and fuel consumption of the procured engine. Testing and trials will be undertaken after receipt of the engine\r\n\r\n5.   Marinized Container to house Project Eagle Hunt equipment. \r\nDesign of field deployable ruggedized container to house Reactive Jamming and GPS Spoofing equipment is finalized. The ruggedized container with EM shielding has arrived Karachi Port. The custom clearance by EHQ (N) is in progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2020-04-03 00:00:00	30	Mar 20	-20-35-30-	\N	f	\N
350002	91	2020-05-20 11:06:53	1.   Ruggedized UAV Jammer (Eagle Hunt-01).\r\n\r\n  a.   Work order for serial production of 10 jammers is still awaited.\r\n\r\n  b.   The proposed costing is based on project raw material. Therefore, the availability of funds prior three months before delivery of jammers is the requirement.\r\n\r\n  c.   The facility for serial production has been taken over by INTELL. Maintenance and renovation of labs for serial production will be undertaken upon availability of requisite material presently not available due to COVID-19 Pandemic.\r\n\r\n2.   Reactive Jamming.\r\n\r\n  a.   Field trials are in progress to consolidate the performance of Direction Finding algorithm by placing the UAVs at different ranges and different altitudes.\r\n\r\n  b.   Software Defined Radios (SDRs) were received in the last week of April 2020.\r\n\r\n  c.   The EDD of Power Amplifier (PAs) and pyramidal HORN antenna is mid May 2020.\r\n\r\n  d.   Long range field trials will be carried out after reception of PAs and antenna.\r\n\r\n3.   GPS SPOOFING\r\n\r\n  a.   The algorithm for prediction of ephemeris data using historical data is finalized. This predicted data helps in generating the counterfeit GPS signal which allows glitch free and rapid switching.\r\n\r\n  b.   The dynamic spoofing trials were also carried out at different power levels so that the UAV can switch promptly (without generating error) from actual GPS signals to counterfeit GPS signals. This activity ensures smooth implementation of the Carry-Off Attack.\r\n\r\n  c.   The delivery of X-Band RADAR is still awaited due to COVID 19 pandemic. The revised EDD is end May 20. Thereafter, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of GPS spoofing milestone upon receipt of requisite equipment.\r\n\r\n4.   Scaled-Down UCAV Model.\r\n\r\n  a.   In the scaled-down UCAV model, avionics testing and surface finishing of various parts are in progress.\r\n\r\n  b.   For avionics testing, a skeletal version of sub-systems has been established to test the integration of servo motors (of wings, tails, payloads and engine throttle control) with auto-pilot via radio link.\r\n\r\n  c.   Surface finishing of various parts such as bottom-tail, upper v-tail and both wings have been undertaken.\r\n\r\n  d.   The controller for manual pilot input (i.e. HOTAS) has also been ordered.\r\n\r\n5.   Marinized Container to house Project Eagle Hunt equipment.: Equipment for Reactive Jamming and GPS Spoofing will be integrated on container upon the availability of container.	DSensors	Finalized	2020-05-20 12:07:58	30	Apr 20	-20-25-30-	\N	f	\N
