350004	163	2020-09-02 13:18:58	1.   Milestone is submitted for release of funds.\r\n\r\n2.   Skeleton team for project kickoff is recruited.\r\n\r\n3.   Comparative study was carried out between M/s IMSAR NSP-7 and CH4 JY-200 SAR by NRDI INTELL team. It was recommended that the American made NSP-7 be the priority consideration for this project since Chinese made RF devices and electrical circuits have been known to age rapidly with use.\r\n\r\n4.   Scaled-Down UCAV Model.\r\na.   Manufacturing.\r\n\r\n1)   Engine Fine Tuning: Initial fine tuning of engine has been performed using RPM and thrust data. \r\n\r\n2)   Static load testing has been undertaken to ensure structural integrity of UAV. \r\n\r\n3)   Avionics system installation and engine integration has been performed. QA/QC has been completed to validate the propulsion and avionics components and system integration within the airframe. \r\n\r\n4)   Wings, tails, landing gears and retraction mechanism have been completed and installed onboard fuselage structure.\r\n\r\n5)   The airframe is also painted.\r\n\r\nb.   Way Forward.\r\n\r\n1)   Engine break-in will be completed by running the engine for the recommended time period. Final fine tuning of engine will be carried out once break-in is completed.\r\n\r\n2)    Ground trials will be undertaken with IC engine and avionics onboard the UAV for operational testing and assessment of propulsion, control surfaces and telemetry system.  \r\n\r\n3)   Following successful ground trials, flight trials will be planned for the UAV.\r\n\r\n4)   The learning acquired during the development of Scaled down UCAV will immensely be used in the design and development of UCAV PoC.\r\n\r\n5.   Machine Shop. Layout plan for machine shop is being finalized. The majority of equipment has been finalized and quotations from vendors have been acquired. Quotations are under review and procurement of equipment is being planned. Following equipment is finalized: \r\n\r\na.   Lathe machine\r\nb.   Engine Hoist/Engine Crane\r\nc.   Drill press\r\nd.   Bandsaw\r\ne.   Angled grinder with stand\r\nf.   Vertical belt sander\r\ng.   CNC milling machine\r\nh.   CNC router\r\ni.   PCB CNC	DSensors	Finalized	2020-09-07 12:28:58	30	Aug 20	-20-25-30-	\N	f	\N
350003	164	2020-09-02 13:19:14	1.   Milestone is submitted for the release of  funds\r\n\r\n2.   Skeleton team for project kickoff is recruited.\r\n\r\n3.   Lab Development. A Lab is being developed for carrying out power combination experiment of 02 magnetrons, each rated 1KW output power. Below is the progress\r\n\r\na.   Lab Layout has been finalized.\r\nb.   Design of metallic box for EM shielding of experimental setup has been finalized.\r\nc.   Procurement of Lab equipment is being undertaken.\r\n\r\n4.   Magnetron Injection Locking Study. \r\na.   A free running magnetron at 2.45 GHz with 10MHz bandwidth has unstable phase and varying frequency.\r\n\r\nb.   Therefore, a preliminary computation scheme has been designed to simulate injection locking of free running magnetron.\r\n\r\nc.   The scheme includes a 3 port WR340 waveguide circulator with injection locking signal fed at port 1, magnetron placed at port 2, and injection locked response measured at port 3.\r\n\r\nd.   The simulation code includes multi physics PIC-EM ferrite coupling equations, and will be tested to investigate magnetron injection locking efficiency.\r\n\r\ne.   High computational machine is being procured to undertake this study.\r\n\r\n5.   RF devices. \r\n\r\na.   Indigenous design and fabrication of following high frequency RF devices are being undertaken to accomplish project experimentation: \r\n\r\n1)   3 Port Waveguide ferrite circulators\r\n2)   4 Port Waveguide ferrite circulators\r\n3)   Directional couplers \r\n4)   Phase shifters\r\n\r\nb.   The simulation results are as expected. The hardware is being procured to implement the design. If the RF devices are developed successfully in-house. This will lead towards substantial saving and less dependence on foreign items.\r\n\r\nc.   Ferrite substrate disks required for fabrication of waveguide circulators have been shortlisted and procurement is in process.\r\n\r\n6.   Power Amplifier. \r\n\r\na.   8Watt PA. \r\n1)   In-house development of 8W power amplifier is completed.\r\n\r\n2)   EM simulations for finding S-parameters are completed and desired results are achieved.\r\n\r\n3)   Components along with PCB for 8W amplifier procured, assembled and tested. Results are being optimized.  \r\n\r\n4)   In-house design of Heat Sink along with packaging of amplifier has been completed. Manufacturing is being undertaken.\r\n\r\nb.   100Watt PA.\r\n\r\n1)   In-house design and development of 100W power amplifier has been completed. Optimization of results is being undertaken on simulations.\r\n\r\n2)   IC transistor for 100W amplifier has been procured. \r\n\r\n3)   RLC meter procurement for measurement of RLC components is being undertaken. This will enable optimization and fine tuning of matching circuits used in power amplifiers. \r\n\r\n7.   Anechoic Chamber. Preliminary study on in-house development of anechoic chamber is being pursued.	DSensors	Finalized	2020-09-07 12:32:52	30	Aug 20	-20-25-30-	\N	f	\N
