350003	230	2020-10-12 11:35:53	1.   Lab Development\r\n\r\n   a.   Table top required to carry out project experimentation of power combining of two magnetrons has been procured and installed.\r\n\r\n   b.   Installation of ESD mats, earthing points and power sockets is in progress.\r\n\r\n2.   Magnetron Injection Locking Modeling and Simulation\r\n\r\na.   Preliminary injection locking numerical scheme has been investigated using computational modeling. Promising results are achieved in lines with the design.\r\n\r\n   b.   Various combinations of gain and bandwidth of the injection signal were tested in simulation. The trend was observed to follow the classical Adler’s Equation and theory. This analysis has furnished.\r\n\r\n   c.   Noisy excitation signal to the magnetron was also simulated to investigate the effect on magnetron jittering. Magnetron output was observed to be highly non-stationary (the frequency is varying with respect to time).\r\n\r\n   d.   As the above analysis indicate requirement to develop additional feedback loops for a stabilized fully controllable power supply through Spartan Xilinx based COTs FPGA.\r\n\r\n3.   RF Devices. Indigenous design and fabrication of following high frequency RF devices are being undertaken to accomplish project experimentation in the given funds. Circulators and couplers required for the experimentation has been modeled and simulated successfully. The production drawings have also been generated. Procurement of raw material is in progress. It is pertinent to mention that limited funds (Rs. 80M) have been allocated against the approved amount (Rs. 146M). The in-house design and development of RF devices will enable completion of project in available funds. \r\n\r\n4.   RF Power Amplifier:\r\n\r\n   a.   8Watt PA. In-house design and manufacturing of Heat Sink along with packaging of amplifier has been completed. The assembly has been successfully tested on VNA and spectrum analyzer. The thermal performance of PA 