350003	262	2020-11-11 10:30:29	1.   Lab Development has been completed with installation of ESD mats, earthing point and power sockets. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Magnetron Injection Locking Simulation. Modelling and simulation studies indicate requirements of control loops, to enable frequency-injection and phase locking of free running magnetrons for bandwidth reduction for efficient power combining. Work is in progress to design and implement the control loops.\r\n\r\nPoint recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Control System Designing for Frequency Pushing.\r\n\r\n      a.   Multiple simulation studies have been undertaken on MATLAB© Simulink to model frequency pushing of a Voltage Controlled Oscillator (VCO), using Phase Locked Loop (PLL) techniques. The VCO was successfully locked at a fixed frequency.\r\n\r\n      b.   Simulations are currently being undertaken on PSpice© to develop control circuitry, which will be implemented experimentally on a VCO.\r\n\r\n4.   RF Devices. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks, and waveguide directional couplers, are required in project experimentation. As limited funds have been released, inhouse design and development of RF devices is in progress.\r\n\r\n        a.   The fabrication of waveguide circulator and directional coupler has been started. \r\n\r\n      b.   A constant current power supply required for biasing the electromagnets and tuning the circulator response, is also being designed.\r\n\r\n5.   RF Power Amplifier. In-house design and optimization of 100W power amplifier has been completed. \r\n\r\n6.   Hardware Procurement.  Procurement of coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, waveguide transitions, waveguide terminations, waveguide adapters, programmable switch mode power supplies and FPGA boards is in process. Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs and Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) ICs are also being procured.\r\n\r\n7.   Feasibility study on in-house development of anechoic chamber is completed.	DR&D	Finalized	2020-11-11 10:31:00	25	Oct 20	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
