350013	277	2020-11-30 11:56:20	1.   The pending export license from Germany for Profi tracker to be used in Directional Antenna Director (DAD) has been recently issued. The item has been shipped and EDD is early Dec 20.\r\n\r\n2.   Radome assembly of individual slices has been tested at Serial Production facility (SPF). Paint job will be completed in early Dec 20.\r\n\r\n3.   Following activities were undertaken in the development of tower at RDS NATHIAGALI for mounting Ground Tracking and Receiving Station (GT&RS).\r\n\r\na.   Quotes have been received from local vendor for Radome tower base construction at RDS NATHIAGALI in lines with NRDI INTELL design.  \r\n\r\nb.   Finalized design of tower in lines with INTELL NRDI has been sent vide letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND Wing/03/7319558 dated 18 Nov 20 for approval for construction of tower according to the proposed design. The proposed drawing and location of tower in vicinity of ELINT station are also enclosed with letter. The construction will kick off shortly after receiving concurrence from NHQ.\r\n\r\n4.   Vans modification to house VTS receiving station for ISR Operations. The INTELL team has successfully tested the modifications and functionality of the equipment installed in the van. The field trials of the van are planned in near future.\r\n\r\n5.   LoS VTS airborne unit installation onboard MPA ATR. The response from DNAM Dte is still awaited for the qualification of VTS transmission in the vicinity of installed ESM detectors on board marinized ATRs as requested vide PN/HQ COMPAK/03/6522890 dated 08 Sep 20. A meeting was conducted on 19th and 20th Nov 20 at NHQ between NRDI INTELL and M/s RAS to discuss the safety of onboard ESM system in conjunction to radiating LoS VTS antenna. NRDI prepared report for installation of LoS VTS onboard ATR was also shared with M/s RAS for validation and vetting.\r\n\r\n6.   GPS Parser development. GPS Parser PCBs and casing fabrication for the modified van in lines with INTELL design is completed. The system is installed in vehicle and has been tested successfully. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n\r\n7.   Video Streaming Server (VSS) casing development. In-house designed casing has been developed to house Video Streaming Server (VSS). The NRDI INTELL developed VSS casing is handed over to C4I department at Dockyard on 21 Oct 20. The VSS casing was tested successfully during recent LWF coverage in Oct 20. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n8.   Live Weapon Firing (LWF). The INTELL team successfully provided coverage during LWF on 27 Oct 20 at RDS MIANWALI. Point recommended to be dropped.	DSensors	Finalized	2020-12-28 11:38:49	25	Nov 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350002	284	2020-12-28 11:31:52	1.   GPS Spoofing Hardware Development.\r\n\r\na.   Development of End user GUI. The GUI has been updated to make it more user friendly. Beta testing on the software is completed and subsequently associated recommendations have been implemented. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nb.   Laboratory Trials. Using the newly assembled ruggedized housing and spoofing PoC assembly, successful in-house trials have been conducted. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nc.   Product Manuals. The technical and operator manuals for the product have been developed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\nd.   Acceptance Trials. Acceptance trials have been conducted successfully in the field on 13 Nov 20, at PN GHARO site. Acceptance by the committee has been reported vide letter PN/HQ PAK MARINES/2ND FP BN/03/7405148 dated 25 Nov 20. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Serial Production. Deployment of Drone Jammers and Spoofing systems while considering FP and GBAD setups vis-à-vis functionality of Project Eagle Hunt deliverables was presented to COMCOAST on 16 Nov 20 vide letter PN/ HQ COSTAL COMMAND/03/7250666.\r\n\r\n3.   Force Majeure has been invoked by DITD due COVID pandemic. The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR is also delayed due to export permit processing delays caused by COVID 19 pandemic. Once 3D X-band RADAR will be received, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of Eagle Hunt -3C version (autonomous GPS spoofing using X-band RADAR). 3D RADARs from other OEMs are also being explored.\r\n\r\n4.   Housing of reactive jamming equipment in the marinized container through M/s RIMS facility will be completed by end Dec 20.\r\n\r\n5.   Miscellaneous Studies Supporting PN Fleet and Repair Agencies undertaken during reporting period:\r\n\r\na.   PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) training. OJT of 07 Dockyard Lab staff comprising of theory classes and demonstration labs on Omniscan MX2 PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) equipment is completed.\r\n\r\nb.   Ultrasonic Testing (UT) of Besconds used in the cable hull passage onboard S/Ms. UT of a locally developed Balezona & Neoprene based besconds, along with NG besconds was undertaken. No flaws / defects were found in NG bescond, while locally developed besconds were found defected. \r\n\r\nc.   500W High Power Antenna for PAF. Two more antennas have been fabricated, one of which was handed over to PAF for high power testing. High power antenna testing was conducted at PAF 606 Workshop Badaber, which revealed satisfactory results. Range testing and in-situ thermal testing of the antenna are in progress.	DR&D	Finalized	2020-12-28 11:32:44	25	Nov 20	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
350013	687	2022-04-27 03:59:22	1.   VTS qualification in vicinity of ESM Detectors onboard PN ATR. M/s RAS highlighted that the high-power density and E-Field of LoS VTS transmission will affect the performance of onboard ESM system. It is recommended that both systems should not be operated simultaneously to ensure smooth operation. The same recommendation has been forwarded to NHQ vide letter PN/DGNRDI/RANDDWING/03110878134 dated 15 Oct 21. Point recommended to be dropped. \r\n\r\n2.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI. The civil work required for installation of GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI, undertaken by M/s FAST team, has been completed successfully. Tower construction, Radome mounting on tower, GT&RS equipment installation, integration of Directional Antenna Director (DAD) system and testing activities have been successfully completed. The GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI is made fully operational as reported vide reference PN/ NRDI/ R AND D WING/ 03/12348866 dated 11 Feb 22. Trial was conducted with P3C MPA on 10 Feb 22 and smooth video received with a range over 100NM. Subsequently, the same is being used in ongoing ISR missions. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS MIANWALI. Nominated reps of NRDI INTELL and CDR JNB conducted joint trials of RDS MIANWALI for site finalization of permanent installation of Ground Terminal and Receiver Station (GT&RS) on 10 Mar 22. The trials of LoS VTS system with P3C indicates normal operation of GT&RS station without any system glitches (Video & GPS data) while positioning aircraft at different locations. The mission route of P3C for undertaking the trials covered TURBAT, ORMARA, TP1 (At Sea), TP2 (At Sea), TP3 (At Sea), NATHIAGALI, MAKRAN, TURBAT. The maximum range for the trials were 112 NM. There is adequate power supply and availability of network at the proposed site. Also, no interference is observed with nearby installations or equipment. In this regard, site between CDR JNB HUT & DEFCOM building (25.1903 N, 64.6008E) has been finalized for installation of said system. The same location is confirmed by HQ COMCOAST vide Letter no PN/HQ COASTAL COMMAND/03/12810179 dated 21 Mar 22.\r\n\r\n\r\n4.   GT&RS Location Finalization for NAS TURBAT. Identification of suitable site (Roof top of Admin Block) for installation of GT&RS at NAS TURBAT under Project Raven-I has been forwarded vide letter PN/HQ COMNAV/03/12508931 dated 24 Feb 22. CMES(N) COMPAK has asked DW&CE (NHQ) for suitability of proposed permanent installation site w.r.t existing load bearing capacity vide letter no PN/HQ COMPAK/CMES (N) COMPAK/03/12771728 dated 16 Mar 22. The same has been reported by HQ COMNAV for information vide letter no PN/HQ COMNAV/03/12799310 dated 18 Mar 22.\r\n\r\n5.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at GWADAR. All construction works at GWADAR Hammerhead have been halted due to some cracks being observed, as informed vide letter PN / HQ COASTAL COMMAND /03/11311292 dated 16 Nov 21. NRDI INTELL has requested HQ COMCOAST to share the report pertaining to Geo Hazard study of the area, if available, to evaluate the alternate suitable location vide reference PN/ DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11409842 dated 30 Nov 21. NHQs has been requested to pursue approval vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12557270 dated 25 Feb 22.\r\n\r\n6.   Milestones Timeline Amendment. Pertaining to delays in case file approvals, NHQs has been requested to expedite amendment of milestones timeline by M/s MTSS vide letter MTSS/20/42 dated 09 Feb 22. A request to expedite approval for smooth execution of the project was also sent by NRDI INTELL vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12551993 dated 25 Feb 22. The milestone timeline amendment is still pending. The milestone (M7) is already completed but the corresponding payment can not be filed due to pending amendment case.\r\n\r\n7.   ISR Mission Activity. Owing to volatile security situation in Baluchistan, NRDI INTELL team as directed vide NHQ letter No PN/ NCW (TECH)/ 03/ 3506199 dated 04 Feb 22 established Ty GT&RS setup at PNS MAKRAN and PNS SIDDIQ for live video relay from P3C to COCs, with effect from 5 Feb 22. NRDI INTELL team has successfully installed temporary setups of GT&RS at both sites, however the teams engaged for the said purpose mainly comprises of project contractual civilian research officers (ROs) and research technicians (RTs), along with PN officers. NRDI INTELL requested DA and PNCA for nomination of service personnel for on job training of the LOS VTS system vide letter PN/ NRDI/ R AND D WING/ 03/ 12424979 dated 17 Feb 22, to facilitate subsequent takeover of the system. The nomination of service personnel was received from DA vide letter PN/ Drafting Authority/03/12500297 dated 22 Feb 22. The OJT is currently in progress at PNS SIDDIQ and PNS MAKRAN. In addition, LOS VTS transmitter system was installed by NRDI ITNELL team on PC86 MPA (3rd aircraft) for the subject activity, vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/03/ 12267923 dated 5 Feb 22. . Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n8.   Video Relay from A/C to GT&RS Station for coverage of Live Weapon Firing (LWF). NRDI INTELL team as directed vide NHQ Letter No PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3574695 dated 07 Mar 22 established Ty GT&RS setup at RDS MIANWALI for live video relay, of the LWF, from P3C to COCs and VIP Ship. The LWF activity was carried out from 11 Mar 22 (Full Dress Rehearsal) to 12 Mar 22.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-05-10 02:59:57	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
