350010	682	2022-04-27 02:44:49	\r\n1.   Harbor Acceptance Trials. Harbor Acceptance Trials of all 19 VFDs has been carried out and cleared by DY team.\r\n \r\n2.   Factory Acceptance Trials. Factory Acceptance Trials of 02 Air Conditioner VFDs, 02 Fresh Water VFDs and 02 Sea Water VFDs were carried out in the presence of PNDY representatives on 20th December 2021 at NRDI and after complete functionality testing all the 06 VFDs were handed over to PNDY representatives. This concluded the FATs of all 19 VFDs to be developed under this work order. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Workshop Acceptance Trials. Workshop Acceptance Trials of the 06 VFDs were carried out on 21st December 2021 at PNDY workshop. The safety checks for all 06 VFDs were carried out successfully in the presence of ship staff, PNDY and NRDI representatives. This concluded the Workshop Acceptance Trials of all 19 VFDs to be developed under this work order.  Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n4.   Provision of Three Speeds on DA-Pump VFD. Activity to enable third speed on DA pump VFD has been carried out by NRDI INTELL team. Team visited dockyard and carried out replacement activity of the installed VFD on board S/M. Testing of the same has been carried out by DY team as well and performance was found to be in-line with requested URD. Point recommended to be dropped\r\n\r\n5.   Correspondence. Following correspondence has been carried out. \r\n\r\na.   NRDI INTELL team has critically analyzed the phenomena of insulation drop onboard PNS KHALID. The insulation drop occurs while connecting MO with NRDI develop VFDs. The deployment of insulation barrier in between them has rectified the insulation issue and improved the protection of VFD from external surges/ground faults.  \r\nb.   4 to 20 mA signal provision design also revised. Opto-coupler based solid state relays coupled with insulation barrier are used for higher insulation and better protection of VFDs. \r\n\r\n6.   Documentation Finalization Meeting. The meeting was held at NRDI INTELL on 28 Dec 21 to consolidate document format of already delivered VFDs. Reps from PND and NCMA were attended the said meeting. INTELL NRDI team has developed documentation including technical and operating manuals, based on provided feedback from DY team. Documentation for Drain Pump was handed over to DY team. Incorporation of feedback and comments of DY team has been integrated into documentation and final version has been shared with DY team.\r\n\r\n7.   Patternization of VFDs. Detailed part list for all 10 applications of NRDI developed VFDs have been forwarded to NCMA vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12841118 dated 24 Mar 22 for initialization of patternization process.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-05-10 02:59:09	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
400002	703	2022-05-10 23:01:59	Third quarterly inspection of the system has been conducted on 21 April 2022. All aspects of the system were inspected and found correct. System is working properly and no any malfunctioning is reported till date. Moreover, fourth and last quarterly inspection according to the contract will be carried out in the month of July 2022 depending upon availability of the ship.	DSOS	Finalized	2022-06-03 02:19:43	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350006	707	2022-05-11 23:02:27	1.   Submission of Test Benches for HSTD avionics and aerospace components. "Development of Test Benches for HSTD avionics and aerospace components" has been successfully completed and submitted against Milestone M3. \r\n\r\n2.   Design / Development Activities.\r\n   \r\na.   MARLIN-01 UAV.  Airframe manufacturing, assembly, avionics/ control / data link integration is completed.  Operational tests of airframe, propulsion, data link and control system are also completed. Point recommended to be dropped \r\n\r\nb.   MARLIN-01 Backup. Manufacturing of an additional MARLIN-01 (as backup), including structural parts, skin sections, propulsion assembly, avionics assembly, avionics cooling system are completed. Ground testing is also successfully completed.\r\n\r\nc.   UAV Launcher. Design and manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01 Launcher / pneumatic circuit testing bench have been completed. Design and assembly of carriage deceleration / braking system has also been completed. The designed system has been successfully tested as well. To further improve speed performance, the pneumatic actuator has been replaced with a larger stroke actuator, the pulley ratio has been reduced and one more inlet is added to the accumulator vessel. \r\n\r\nd.   UAV Launcher Testing.   Initial testing of launcher with integrated control system and pneumatic circuit at low, medium pressure is completed. In-house testing of launcher at SPF are also completed successfully.  Field testing for dead weight and dummy UAV launches are successfully conducted at PN GHARO facility.  The criteria of projectile launch speed, aerial time and ground range are successfully met.\r\n\r\ne.   P220 Jet Engine Testing. Bench testing of P220 Turbo jet engine (for MARLIN-01) has been conducted. Intake duct design has been improved and manufactured. Bench testing of engine with improved intake is also conducted and results are within acceptable margins. \r\n\r\nf.   Backup P220 Jet Engine Testing. Maiden testing of backup P220 engine (MARLIN-01 backup) is also successfully completed.\r\n\r\ng.   P1000 Jet Engine Testing. Bench testing of P1000 Turbo jet engine (for MARLIN-02) has been conducted. Engine successfully started and thrust / temperature measurements are taken for design-adjustment of propulsion system assembly with airframe. \r\n\r\n\r\nh.   Ground Testing of Marlin-01 UAVs. Extensive ground testing activities of Marlin-01 UAVs are considered essential prior to the flight trials. In this regard: airframe load tests, pitch/roll performance testing of propulsion system, avionics endurance testing, data-link range tests, parachute release mechanism tests, control surface load tests, carriage-lock thrust testing are planned. Airframe load tests, pitch/roll performance testing of propulsion system and avionics endurance tests are successfully completed. Data link range tests and parachute release mechanism tests are partly completed. During control surface load testing, problem related to deformation of control linkages and servo failure is observed. Control linkage mechanism has been upgraded to increase stiffness and rigidity. Avionics system has been ruggedized based on root cause analysis of servo failure. Carriage-lock thrust testing of UAV has been successfully conducted at PN GHARO facility on 8th Mar 22.\r\n\r\nj.   Field / Flight Testing of Marlin-01 UAV. Field testing / launch trials of Marlin-01 UAV has been planned at PN GHARO facility in Mar 22. For this purpose, leakage testing of launcher, site survey and coordination meeting between NRDI and NSTOC reps regarding recovery of HSTD from creek area was held on 24-25 Feb 22, vide reference PN/NRDI/ R AND D Wing/03/12462317 dated 18 Feb 22. The planned field trials of UAV is successfully conducted on 28th Mar 22. During launch phase Marlin-01 endured axial load of 13g, attained the height of ~2400 ft. (735 m) and reached speed of 336 kmph (93.4 m/s). Then during ~4.5 min flight, Marlin-01 completed two rounds of 4km radius and successfully pulled multiple 5g maneuvers. Post-flight data analysis is under progress for further improvement / consolidation of HSTD system. Another field test of MARLIN-01 is being planned to test improved flight parameters.\r\n\r\nk.   Design of MARLIN-02 (full-scale HSTD). The design has been revised based on the learnings from design / manufacturing activities of MARLIN-01. Detailed design of airframe components and integration with launch / recovery systems are completed. CAD integration of avionics systems, data link, control mechanism and modifications pertaining to propulsion system are under progress. Pattern machining activities have been initiated for the completed airframe components. Pattern finishing activities and mold fabrication are also completed. Airframe manufacturing and control circuits assembly is completed. MARLIN-02 is ready for ground testing. \r\n\r\nl.   Ground Testing of MARLIN-02 UAV. MTSS has requested NHQ for nomination inspection/ acceptance committee for conduct of ground test of MARLIN-02 UAV against milestone M4, vide reference MTSS/20/NRDI/HSTD-II/02 dated 13 Apr 22. Moreover, draft ATPs have also been forwarded for perusal. \r\n\r\nm.   MARLIN-02 Launcher. MARLIN-02 launcher is re-designed based on the learning from design / development of MARLIN-01 Launcher. In this regard, considerations are given to weight reduction, ease of assembly and transportation. In order to keep the development, cost effective and reduce develop time imperative consideration is given to re-use of parts / sub-assemblies manufactured for the MARLIN-01 launcher. Export of manufacturing drawings, market surveys for COTs items and Bill of Material (BOM) compilation are completed.\r\n\r\nn.   Material Testing. Destructive Testing (DT) of composite material samples is being carried out using PNEC and PCSIR equipment. Tensile tests and first phase of bending tests are completed. Manufacturing process is improved in lines with the test results. Bending tests of improved samples are also completed. Testing of different composite coring materials are tested and coring scheme for MARLIN-02 has been finalized. \r\n\r\np.   Wind Tunnel Testing. Computer Aided Design (CAD) model for development of testing model has been shared, as required by M/s DESTO.  Estimated of quotation & timeline of 190 working days is received from the firm. M/s DESTO has been requested to reduce timeline. Foreign WTT facilities are also being explored for the pertinent testing. \r\n\r\n3.   Hardware Procurement & Testing Status.\r\n\r\na.   The ordered JetCat P-1000 (Germany based 1100N) turbo jet engine is successful procured. \r\n\r\nb.   Veronte flight controller (of M/s Embention) excluding air antenna is received at INTELL NRDI. Individual components have been tested and radio link is established. Firmware update has also been received for tracker. Currently, development of controls for HSTD are being studied and range testing activates are being planned.\r\n\r\nc.   Material & COTs items for fabrication of MARLIN-02 UAV and Launcher are being purchased/ procured as per manufacturing requirements.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-06-04 04:39:55	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350018	698	2022-05-11 23:00:10	1.   Issuance of Work Order. The Work order for the project “Fabrication of Antenna Units long With Associated Accessories of SUR-17 RADAR onboard F-22P Frigates” has been received vide reference SMR-WE/NRDI/SUR-17/598 dated 15 Mar 22. The acceptance of work order is achieved, To established is 01 Apr 22. \r\n2.   Submission of Project Plan. "Project Plan" has been submitted against Milestone M2. Electromagnetic modelling of class A and class B antenna units will first be undertaken. Once the RF design of individual antenna types is finalized, design and RF analysis of the complete array will be performed. Finally, mechanical modelling will be undertaken to ensure reliable operation at high drag and wind speeds.\r\n\r\n3.   Full Wave EM Simulation. Computational Electromagnetics Modelling of individual class A and class B antenna units as well as complete array has been performed and preliminary design is finalized. Radiation patterns have been analyzed with weighted power assignment to each antenna in the array.\r\n\r\n4.   Weighted Power Divider Design. Preliminary design of weighted power divider is finalized. \r\n\r\n5.   Fabrication. Fabrication of single class A and class B antennas will first be undertaken, based on preliminary finalized design. Fabrication and testing of weighted power divider is also planned and pertinent procurement is in progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-06-04 04:40:22	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350012	704	2022-05-11 22:46:52	\r\n1.   Coordination meeting with PN FMG for NDT data acquisition. A meeting was held at NRDI INTELL on 13 Dec 21 vide reference PN/DG NRDI/At PNS JAUHAR/03/11802413 dated 17 Dec 21. The NDT data acquisition methodology for the project was finalized in the meeting. The NDT data comprising of thermal and ultrasonic data will be periodically acquired by FMG team depending upon the availability of Ship/vessel. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Acquisition of Environmental data. The NRDI team acquires the environmental data from PN Ship/vessel on monthly basis. The data was retrieved from the deployed data loggers. Moreover, the team also replaced the battery packs of the data loggers during their visit. The data will be acquired by NRDI team upon availability of the PN Ship/vessel vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12124832 dated 18 Jan 2022. \r\n\r\n3.   Historical Database Development. A historical database is being developed to record the acquired environmental and NDT data from PN ships/vessels. The database is being analyzed at NRDI. Subsequently, data analytics is being performed on the database for estimation of degradation parameter. Data provided by FMG was not suitable; the same has been communicated to the PoC for rectification, vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12119861 dated 18 Jan 2022. The availability of PN platforms to perform data acquisition activity by NRDI team in the presence of FMG reps is requested vide reference PN/NRDI/ R AND D WING/03/12449213 dated 21 Feb 22.\r\n\r\n4.   Implementation of RUL Prediction Algorithms on Historical Database (MS-5). A detailed report on “Implementation of RUL Prediction Algorithms on historical database” has been submitted on 10 Jan 22 according to milestone 5 of the project. A presentation on the same was requested vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12240914 dated 01 Feb 22. Subsequently, a detailed presentation was given in a meeting between NRDI NDT & Reliability Engineering Center, NCMA and FMG teams, held at NRDI INTELL on 21 Feb 22, vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12499265 dated 22 Feb 22.  Queries from NCMA on delivered presentation was received vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12629885 dated 04 Mar 22. Detailed response on raised queries was provided by NRDI vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12737531 dated 11 Mar 22. Further clarification on milestone 5 report was again requested by NCMA vide letter PN/NCMA/03/12744668 dated 14 Mar 22. More detailed response was forwarded vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12766316 dated 15 Mar 22 in which diligent reading of work order is requested. Further clarification was requested by NCMA w.r.t understanding of milestone 5 report vide letter PN/NCMA/03/12816140 dated 18 Mar 22. The itemized response on each point was forwarded vide PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12898610 dated 25 Mar 22. Subsequently, NCMA have forwarded the response to FMG ME, FMG WE and GM RD and TA for feedback vide reference PN/NCMA/03/12958496 dated 31 Mar 22. The acceptance of milestone 5 is still under deliberation at NCMA.\r\n\r\n5.   Non-Availability of PN platforms for Data Acquisition. During the conduct of said project, sufficient historical data could not be collected by FMG team due non availability of PN platforms. Following references are relevant is this regard\r\n\r\na.   PN/HQ COMPAK/03/12879578 dated 24 Mar 22\r\nb.   PN/NCMA/03/12878153 dated 24 Mar 22\r\nc.   PN/DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11285138 dated 12 Nov 21\r\nd.   PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12008222 dated 06 Jan 22\r\n\r\n6.   Extension in Project Timeline. A case for extension of the project for 06 months is suggested after acceptance of milestone 5 and subject to availability of PN platform vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/12655448 dated 21 Mar 22. The same has not acceded to vide NHQ letter PN/ILS Dte /03/3616326 dated 25 Mar 22. Recently, it has been informed that the PN platforms are not available for data acquisition activity till end May 22 due Ops dictates. It is therefore requested to revisit the decision pertaining to six-month timeline extension vide reference PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13038794 dated 09 Apr 22.	DSensors	Finalized	2022-06-04 04:42:04	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
