350018	939	2023-05-08 11:16:01.765	HATs/SATs Finalization. An initial testing of the SUR 17 antenna was undertaken on 2-3 Feb 23. A range of 159 Km was successfully achieved during trials with NRDI developed antenna. NRDI INTELL visited PND for further antenna inspection, RF tuning and retuning of cables length and report is forwarded vide letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/3469111 dated 16 Mar 23. The team has performed the below mentioned tasks. Subsequent SATs are to be undertaken to verify results. \r\n\r\n       a.   RF path tuning of the SUR 17 antenna units.\r\n\r\n       b.   Design and development of customized adapters for testing of 1:4 power splitters and antenna mast unit. \r\n\r\n       c.   VNA testing of the complete antenna unit along with mast was undertaken and found to be within allowable limits. \r\n\r\n       d.   Finally, all the antenna components were re-installed at weapon complex PND.\r\n\r\n       e.   SATs of SUR 17 were conducted again vide letter PN/HQ COMPAK/OPERATIONS/3810181 dated 07 Apr 23. During trials increased clutter was observed. Upon inspection, NRDI INTELL team diagnosed that the grazing angle of the antenna was towards the sea. Therefore, antenna unit was brought back to the manufacturing facility and is under process for further alignment. In this regard, mitigation measures are under progress to improve the antenna structure through introduction of additional Kevlar ropes and support columns.	DSensors	Finalized	2023-05-12 09:06:18.639	25	Apr 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
