350025	1028	2023-08-08 12:06:51.156	1.   Project Plan Submission. The "Global Project Plan" (GPP) has been submitted against Milestone M2. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n2.   HPO Submission. The "Hardware Purchase Order" (HPO) has been submitted against Milestone M3. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n3.   Procurement. Sintering furnace is being procured which will be utilized for the development of cathode.\r\n\r\n4.   Design Activities. Reverse engineering for dimensional analysis and material characterization using XRF analyzer held with NRDI is in progress. Moreover, heater design, electron gun and slow wave structure design are in progress. The power supply of existing TWT of LR66 radar is received at NRDI INTELL which will be utilized in this project. \r\n\r\n5.   Development of ARRC. Advance Radar Research Center (ARRC) is being developed at manufacturing facility Karsaz. The design of ARRC has been completed whereas, and development is in progress. \r\n\r\n6.   Study for Recovery of LR66 Radar. The study for the recovery of complete LR 66 tracking radar is in progress. In this regard, a visit of F22P ship is being planned in Aug 23.	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jul 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350019	1020	2023-08-07 16:40:59.841	1.   Part-level Disassembly. Custom tools have been developed to carry out part-level disassembly of the propulsion unit. The propeller assembly, pulley drive, radiator, starter, intake & exhaust assemblies have been disassembled. The disassembly of the core engine clock is in progress. \r\n\r\n2.   Degradation Study. The disassembled components are being studied for signs of wear & degradation. Based on the observations, the degradation report is compiled and submitted. Subsequently, the defects are being studied for sourcing of COTS, in-house manufacturing, and development of rectification methods.\r\n\r\n3.   Literature Review. Review of open-source literature pertaining to rotary engine defects, their rectification methods, seals materials and manufacturing processes is being carried out. Subsequently, the maintenance methodology will be developed, and in-house manufacturing and sourcing of COTS will be undertaken. \r\n\r\n4.   Maintenance Study. Detailed maintenance report encompassing the description of disassembly tools, part/ component inspection checks, qualification criteria, and rectification procedures is being compiled. \r\n\r\n5.   Reverse Engineering. 3D scanning of OEM parts is under progress for geometric feature extraction and development of CAD model. The extracted geometry will then be used for development of manufacturing ready CAD model of parts/ components. Subsequently, dimensional QCs and tolerance analysis of designed parts will be carried out with reference to original OEM parts. Moreover, XRF based material testing is being carried out for the identification of materials for subsequent procurement.	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jul 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350021	1021	2023-08-07 16:43:10.283	1.   Team Visit. The video output from LUNA payload can only be seen within the GCS placed at PN GHARO site. Team from NRDI INTELL visited PN GHARO site to observe the operational condition of existing data link of LUNA. Team inspected the bird, payload and GCS in detail in order to undertake modifications for installation of digital video link. \r\n\r\n2.   Payload Requirement. LUNA payload (EO/IR) required for execution of this project. In this regard, INTELL NRDI requested payload and relevant documentation of payload from SSO Air ENGG COMPAK in Para 2 vide reference PN/R AND WING/GENERAL/3705733 dated 01 April 2023. The payload was handed over to NRDI in mid-June for tapping the video feed. \r\n\r\n3.   Video Feed from Payload. The team has successfully tapped the video feed from the Payload through detailed reverse engineering process. The tapped video is tested successfully by turning ON the payload. Moreover, the video was also tested successfully using the video splitter on two different display screens.  One feed is given to PMR (Payload manager) and the second feed is used to display the video on LCD. The second feed has been successfully transmitted from AV to GCS (NRDI developed) for proof of concept. Data link ruggedization and position/ location finalization of the antenna for installation onboard AV is currently under progress.\r\n\r\n4.   Design Digital Video Link. The design and development of digital video link have been completed. Furthermore, the integration of RF power amplifier has also developed.	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jul 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350024	1025	2023-08-07 16:49:10.891	1.   Submission of Project Plan and List of Deliverables. The "Project Plan and List of Deliverables" has been submitted against Milestone M2. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n2.   Submission of Design Report & Drawings. Design of Radome assembly has been completed. Structural analysis for verification of design is also completed. A report encompassing the design details is submitted, against Milestone M4. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n3.   Manufacturing of Radome and Base. Manufacturing of these parts in line with already developed detailed drawings has been completed. The developed parts have been sent to PND for acceptance testing, against Milestone M6. Structural integrity is tested successfully at 45bar. Minor water leakage observed suspected chamber seal and radome seal was accordingly replaced by NRDI. New chamber connector has also been designed and developed by NRDI. Testing is awaited due to non-ops chamber and RF equipment.	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jul 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350020	1022	2023-08-07 16:44:13.946	1.   Documentation Review. A detailed review of LUNA NG documentation including the system operators’ manual, and available ATRs from OEM visit, has been conducted for development of DES. Testing protocols for relevant components are under development based on detailed inspection of individual components, and their interfaces. BOM for in-house developed tools, custom cables, and breakout boards will also be finalized sequentially, as the study progresses. \r\n\r\n2.   Testing & Analysis. Testing of RF component, cable and connectors of AV & GCS with detailed analysis is in progress. Moreover, testing criteria and protocol as well as development of breakout box for HF data cable testing is in progress. RF connectors, bias Tee, and passive components are being procured to test remaining part of RF front end of GCS and AV. ATRs and ATPs are being formulated.	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jul 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350022	1023	2023-08-07 16:45:44.13	1.   Antenna Design. Dish antenna has been designed and developed at NRDI INTELL. Patch feeder is also developed. Complete assembly of first prototype is in progress.\r\n\r\n2.   ATP Finalization. The trial procedure has been forwarded to NHQ. HQ COMPAK requested COMNAV for evaluation and finalization of ATPs in consultation with NRDI INTELL by 12 Jun 23, vide letter PN/HQ COMPAK/TRAINING/4706893 dated 06 Jun 23. Furthermore, it is solicited to schedule and finalize the venue for the conduct of acceptance trials. FATs are planned in Jul 23.     \r\n\r\n3.   Delivery of 03 DA. Three Dish Antennas are ready to deliver. The same has been informed to MTSS for onward communication to NHQ.\r\n\r\n4.   Final Testing & Field Trials of 1st prototype. FATs were conducted with NRDI developed dish antenna and were found satisfactory. Further field testing was conducted at Pasni from 17-21 Jul 23. The developed dish antenna demonstrated a range of 54NM with OEM Patch feeder and a range of 25NM with NRDI developed Patch feeder. \r\n\r\n5.   RF tuning of Patch Feeder. Reverse engineering of OEM developed patch feeder was conducted using XRF analyzer for material characterization and dimensional analysis using Vernier caliper. Redeveloped patch feeder is providing similar results compared to the OEM feeder. The same feeder is being anodized and will be ready for field trials in 2nd week of Aug 23. ?	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jul 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350023	1024	2023-08-07 16:47:39.36	1.   Filter Design. Cavity based filters for L1 (1.3-1.5 GHz), L2 (1.7-1.8 GHz), and S-band (2.2-2.5 GHz) have been designed and fabricated. Design is further consolidated through reverse engineering of the original OEM filter using XRF analyzer for material characterization and 3D Scanner for dimensional analysis.\r\n\r\n2.   Lab Testing Report. Filters have been tested in lab and performance is found satisfactory. Lab Testing Report has been sent to MTSS for onward submission to NHQ, against Milestone M5. \r\n\r\n3.   Field Testing. Ruggedized casing and assembly of filters is in progress after which field testing will be planned.	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jul 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
