450002	1044	2023-10-04 12:31:40.301	• Work Order for upgradation of 25 mm gun received vide letter PN/HQs COASTAL COMMAND/GENERAL/273704 dated 13 Feb 23.\r\n\r\n• Project start date (To) was established from 03 Jul 23. Subsequently, milestone-1 (Global Project Plan) was completed on 18 Jul 23. \r\n\r\n• Consequently, milestone-3 (Submission of Preliminary Design Review) completed on 08 Sep 23. \r\n\r\n• Milestone-4 (Critical Design Review and List of Deliverables) is under process.\r\n\r\nActivity Summary\r\n\r\n       a.   System Preliminary Design. The preliminary system has been designed. Details of the system is elaborated in Preliminary Design Review (PDR) report. \r\n\r\n       b.   Testing/Trials of Hydraulic Pump. Hydro Pack (Turkish brand) was shortlisted for tests/trials. The Hydraulic pump was integrated with 25mm gun (at R&D Wing) and tested. Functioning of Training, elevation, cocking and firing mechanism was found satisfactory. \r\n\r\n       c.   Camera Mount and Real-Time Video Transmission Setup. A removable camera mount has been fabricated and installed on Gun mount for test/ trials. A video transmission setup based on embedded board is being implemented for test/ trials.\r\n\r\n       d.   Remote Monitoring & Control Console. Design of control console has been finalized. Procurement of console equipment is in process. \r\n\r\n       e.   Hiring of HR. Case for hiring of 03 x engineers and 01 x Lab assistant has been approved from DG NRDI.  HR induction is in process. \r\n\r\nPlanned Activities \r\n\r\n       a.   Camera Alignment. The procedure/ setup for camera center alignment with Gun Bore is planned to be developed.\r\n\r\n       b.   Variable Hydraulic Control. The hydraulic system design is currently limited to single speed movement in training and elevation. Also, the current design is limited to 01 x degree of movement at a time. Variable training and elevation control sub-system is to be developed for smooth acquisition and tracking (manual) of the target using joystick as well 02 x degree of movement (simultaneously).	DSystems	Finalized	2023-10-30 11:49:16.776	25	Sep 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
250002	1046	2023-10-05 14:58:05.473	1.   The project was again presented in 3rd R& D Board meeting held on 15 Nov 22. With the revised cost of Rs 232.97 M. As per the decisions DNT Inland was nominated as sponsoring directorate.\r\n\r\n2.   A presentation was held on 13 Apr 2023 at R&D Wing, chaired by COS. Proposed VRC setup and related aspects were well appreciated by COS.\r\n\r\n3.   HQ COMKAR was directed by COS to constitute a committee to study the need for VR based training simulators in consultation with NRDI for newly acquired platforms (054-A, MILGEM, OPVs)\r\n\r\n4.   Series of meetings held at PNS BAHADUR to discuss VR based training simulators. Subsequently, following 03 x systems shortlisted for development:\r\n\r\n       a.   VR based Simulator for LY 80 (N) Missile\r\n\r\n       b.   VR based Simulator for Missile System and Maintenance\r\n\r\n       c.   VR based Simulator for Fixed Drenching Systems onboard Type-54A/ F-22P Ships\r\n\r\n5.   Draft URDs of the above mentioned systems were received for views and comments. Same have been forwarded after review vide letter: PN/ R AND D WING/GENERAL/5313709 dated 21 July 23.\r\n\r\n6.   The project presented in 4th R&D Board meeting. MoMs are awaited.	DEnab	Cancelled	2023-10-05 15:07:45.38	19	Sep 23	-19-	\N	f	\N
