350021	1061	2023-10-06 12:15:36.254	1.   Video Feed from Payload. Video feed was tested successfully using the video splitter on two different display screens.  One feed is given to PMR (Payload manager) and the second feed is used to display the video on LCD. The second feed has been successfully transmitted from AV to GCS (NRDI developed) for proof of concept.\r\n\r\n2.   Data Link Design Report: Detailed design report of digital video link containing data link parameters such as dimensions’ weight and position for installation onboard AV has been submitted. Data link ruggedization and position/ location finalization of the antenna for installation onboard AV are also proposed in the design report. The development/ modification will be started after approval from 47 Sqn. A detailed meeting was held between INTELL, 47 Sqn and AED reps vide reference PN/ILM AND OLS WING/MAINTAINANCE/1145156 dated 07 Sep 23. In the meeting design report was explained in detail. The response from AED/47 Sqn reps is awaited to carry out the proposed modifications onboard AV.\r\n\r\n3.   Custom Hatch Development for Antenna Installation. The lower bottom hatch of AV is designed for installation of DVL antenna. This hatch will be developed with similar specifications to the original hatch and thus will not introduce any CG variations. This hatch can be easily replaceable with the original hatch, whenever required.\r\n\r\n4.   Antenna Drag Calculations. Drag study was also conducted for installation of DVL antenna on the hatch of AV and it is reported safe in contrast to LUNA AV altitude and speed.\r\n\r\n5.   EMI/ EMC Study. EMI/EMI study of DVL and the antenna is also carried out for position finalization. The proposed installation position is safe and does not interfere with any other electrical and RF device as per the study.	DSensors	Finalized	2023-10-30 11:48:57.614	25	Sep 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
