350027	1067	2023-10-06 12:21:08.074	1.   Development of ASGSI Control Unit. Development of ASGSI Control Unit is under progress for which NRDI INTELL has requested for the provision of Faulty Control Unit and Motor Controllers from HQ COMPAK to perform in depth technical analysis of the system, vide reference letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/584774 dated 01 Aug 23. Thorough study of internal components including wiring, pinouts and interfaces has been carried out by INTELL. Furthermore, signal tapping of installed motors was carried out and motors were made operational by INTELL team using custom developed test benches and setup. Based on results of study, suitable hardware was shortlisted and procurement has been initiated. Custom control algorithm is currently under development.\r\n\r\n2.   Handing Over of ASGSI Control Unit to PND. The handing over of ASGSI unit held by INTELL was requested by PND for the recovery of the system through spares vide reference letter PN/PNS MOAWIN/MAINTENANCE/914834 dated 22 Aug 23. In this regard NRDI INTELL requested that the ASGSI unit will be required multiple times for the smooth conduct of project activities vide reference letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/937124 dated 24 Aug 23. Subsequently, the ASGSI unit was handed over to the PND, while the defective controller and motor driver PCBs were handed over to NRDI INTELL vide reference letter PN/COMAUXMIN 9/MAINTENANCE/1005488 dated 29 Aug 23. ASGSI unit retrieved back from ship staff on 4th Oct 23. Development of control algorithm for servo motors is in progress which will be tested on ASGSI unit for further validation.  \r\n\r\n3.   Milestones Completion. The “Design Engineering Study” (DES) has been submitted against Milestone M4. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.	DSensors	Finalized	2023-10-30 11:47:56.431	25	Sep 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350020	1062	2023-10-06 12:16:21.103	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Documentation Review. A detailed review of LUNA NG documentation including the system operators’ manual, and available ATRs from OEM visit, has been conducted for development of DES. Testing protocols for relevant components are under development based on detailed inspection of individual components, and their interfaces. BOM for in-house developed tools, custom cables, and breakout boards will also be finalized sequentially, as the study progresses. ATRs for the following components have been designed based on lab testing:\r\n\r\n       a.   Cooling System\r\n\r\n       b.   Board Battery\r\n\r\n       c.   Lid Integrated Pilot View\r\n\r\n       d.   LDS Electronics\r\n\r\n       e.   Servo Units\r\n\r\n       f.   Pump Unit\r\n\r\n2.   Design of breakout boards and test cables is underway based on findings of study. Components and connectors required for testing are being shortlisted and procurement of relevant components is in progress. \r\n\r\n3.   Data tapping and acquisition of communication protocols and signals is underway for different AV components. Different subsystems of the AV are being powered up and tapping of signals at relevant interfaces is being carried out using digital multimeter, oscilloscope and interface converters (USB to 485, CANBus, etc). Items under test are:\r\n\r\n       a.   Flight Controller\r\n\r\n       b.   Flight Data Recorder\r\n\r\n       c.   Servo Measurement Unit\r\n\r\n4.   Hardware Purchase Order Submission. The Hardware purchase order has been completed and sent to MTSS for onward submission to NHQ, against Milestone M4.	DSensors	Finalized	2023-10-30 11:48:04.683	25	Sep 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
