350022	1083	2023-11-11 10:03:49.339	1.   Antenna Design. Dish antenna has been designed and developed at NRDI INTELL. Patch feeder is also developed.    \r\n\r\n2.   Final Testing & Field Trials of 1st Prototype. FATs and aerial trials were successfully conducted with 01 x NRDI developed dish antenna and were found satisfactory with a range of 54 NM vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/PROJECTS/1038701 dated 01 Sep 23.\r\n\r\n3.   Delivery of 03 DA. 03 x Dish Antennas with all associated accessories handed over to rep of 47 Sqn vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/PROJECTS/1326593 dated 18 Sep 23. Successful HATs and aerial trials of 03 x Dish Antenna have also been conducted.\r\n\r\n4.   Delivery of Support Structure. 03 x Support structure for BSE Dish were handed over to 47 Sqn vide reference PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1419950 dated 11 Oct 23.	DSensors	Finalized	2023-11-29 15:22:17.332	25	Oct 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350020	1082	2023-11-11 10:03:20.939	1.   Documentation Review. A detailed review of LUNA NG documentation including the system operators’ manual, and available ATRs from OEM visit, has been conducted. Testing protocols for relevant components are under development based on detailed inspection of individual components, and their interfaces. BOM for in-house developed tools, custom cables, and breakout boards will also be finalized sequentially, as the study progresses. ATRs for the following components have been designed based on lab testing:\r\n\r\n       a.   Cooling System\r\n\r\n       b.   Board Battery\r\n\r\n       c.   Lid Integrated Pilot View\r\n\r\n       d.   LDS Electronics\r\n\r\n       e.   Servo Units\r\n\r\n       f.   Pump Unit\r\n\r\n2.   Design of breakout boards and test cables is underway based on findings of study. Components and connectors required for testing are being shortlisted and procurement of relevant components is in progress. \r\n\r\n3.   Data tapping and acquisition of communication protocols and signals is underway for different AV components. Different subsystems of the AV are being powered up and tapping of signals at relevant interfaces is being carried out using digital multimeter, oscilloscope and interface converters (USB to 485, CANBus, etc). Items under test are:\r\n\r\n       a.   Flight Controller\r\n\r\n       b.   Flight Data Recorder\r\n\r\n       c.   Servo Measurement Unit\r\n\r\n       d.   Engine Electronics Box\r\n\r\n       e.   Secondary Data Link Terminal\r\n\r\n4.   Testing wiring harness and OEM provided diagnostic laptop held with PN 47 SQN has been requested by INTELL for access to software and configurations (data rates, encoding, header files) of Engine Electronics Box (EEB) and Flight Data Recorder (FDR). Held information is critical in the development of ATPs of mentioned components. \r\n\r\n5.   Hardware Purchase Order Submission. The Hardware purchase order has been completed and sent to MTSS for onward submission to NHQ, against Milestone M4.	DSensors	Finalized	2023-11-29 15:22:43.76	25	Oct 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
