350018	1144	2024-01-15 16:12:24.063	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   SUR 17 antenna CAD Modelling, EM Design & Drag Analysis of Individual Class A & Class B Yagi Antenna Arrays has been completed along with the development and assembly of complete antenna array. Accordingly, FATs of antenna were successfully conducted on 30 Sep 22. Afterwards, HATs of antenna were successfully conducted on 2 Feb 23. Post FATs and HATs, 04 x sea trials were conducted:\r\n\r\n       a.   1st sea trial onboard PNS ZULFIQUAR on 3 Feb 23: 159 km max range\r\n\r\n       b.   2nd sea trial onboard PNS ZULFIQUAR on 13 Apr 23: Only Clutter observed.\r\n\r\n       c.   3rd sea trial onboard PNS ASLAT on 24-25 Jul 23: 326 km max range\r\n\r\n       d.   4th sea trials conducted on 05 Sep 23 for 03 hours onboard PNS ASLAT with PNS SHAMSHEER available for comparison, vide reference letters PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1179170 dated 07 Sep 23 & PN/PNS ASLAT/MAINTENANCE/1179128 dated 07 Sep 23. Following was observed.\r\n\r\n              (1)   PNS ASLAT successfully tracked PC-89 during 02 x RUNS\r\n\r\n              (2)   Performance of the antenna is considered SAT\r\n\r\n              (3)   Ship’s head line and true azimuth markers on the radar display were static and misaligned, due to the non-conduct of MOP017\r\n\r\n              (4)   RADAR system crashed 04 times during the operation\r\n\r\n2.   Maintenance Work. Necessary maintenance work to enhance and improve antenna structural health has been completed by NRDI INTELL team. Afterwards antenna was installed onboard PNS ZULFIQUAR on 19 Oct 23 for onward sea trials, vide reference PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1144156 dated 02 Nov 23.\r\n\r\n3.   Sea Trials. Sea trials of NRDI INTELL fabricated SUR 17 antenna are tentatively planned in Jan 24. In this regard, a coordination meeting was held onboard PNS ZULFIQUAR with all stakeholders in attendance. It was decided that trials will be conducted as per finalized trial sheet formulated with mutual consent, vide reference letter, PN/COMDESRON 18/MAINTENANCE/6758737 dated 28 Dec 23.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-02-01 12:44:11.638	25	Dec 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350028	1154	2024-01-15 16:22:14.911	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Project Plan Submission. The "Global Project Plan" (GPP) has been submitted against Milestone M2. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n2.   HPO Submission. The "Hardware Purchase Order" (HPO) has been submitted against Milestone M3. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n3.   Detailed Design Report. Milestone M4 (Submission of Detailed Design Report) has been submitted.\r\n\r\n4.   Sourcing of Heat Sink. Required 5 kW Heat Sink was received and tested with 02 kW magnetron. Same heat sink will be utilized as load for effective power combination of 4 x S band 1KW magnetrons.\r\n\r\n5.   Study for Next Phase. Study for development of high power electromagnetic sources for enhance lethality and extended ranges is in progress.\r\n\r\n6.   Design Activities. \r\n\r\n       a.   Design of antenna mode converter for enhanced gain from TE10 to TE11 is completed along with conical antenna. Fabrication has been initiated.\r\n\r\n       b.   Study and design mechanism of circularly polarized conical horn antenna is in progress.\r\n\r\n7.   Lab Testing. Lab testing with 04 x Magnetrons is completed.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-02-01 12:46:23.169	25	Dec 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
