350025	1151	2024-01-15 16:19:19.611	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   DES Submission. The "Design Engineering Study" (DES) has been submitted against Milestone M4. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n2.   Procurement. Sintering furnace is being procured which will be utilized for development of cathode.\r\n\r\n3.   Design Activities. Reverse engineering for dimensional analysis and material characterization using XRF analyzer held with NRDI is in progress. Moreover, heater design, Electron Gun and slow wave structure designing is in progress. Power supply of existing TWT of LR66 radar is received at NRDI INTELL which will be utilized in this project. \r\n\r\n       a.   Design of Waveguide to Coaxial Adapter for cold testing of existing TWT on VNA.\r\n\r\n       b.   Heater Design: Sample heater coil has been successfully designed and manufactured. The manufacturing process has been established. The final design of heater coil will be developed based on calculation of cathode temperature and work function. \r\n\r\n       c.   Pierce Electron Gun: Simulation of Pierce electron Gun has been completed. Design will be revised after finalization of SWS.\r\n\r\n       d.   Slow Wave Structure: Preliminary Eigen mode analysis has been completed to compute initial dimensions. Hot test simulations are in progress under which backward wave suppression techniques and pitch tapering are being implemented to improve TWT Gain. Time Frequency Energy analysis is being undertaken to correlate frequency response with electron flow in TWT\r\n\r\n       e.   Collector Design:  Collector preliminary design simulation jas been completed. Design will be revised after finalization of SWS.\r\n\r\n4.   Development of ARRC. Advance radar research center (ARRC) is being developed at manufacturing facility PNS KARSAZ. Design of ARRC has been completed whereas, development of Clean room is in progress. Procurement of Molecular Vacuum Pump is in progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-02-01 12:45:41.252	25	Dec 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
