350012	1167	2024-02-06 16:26:04.314	Progress \r\n\r\n1.   Training of Personnel: 14 x Personnel (from NCMA, FMG (WE), FMG (ME), RD & TA, W&S, S & S, SW and ITRF) were earmarked and trained for Operation/ Installation and Maintenance, from 04 Sep 23 to 15 Sep 23.\r\n\r\n2.   GUI Development. The Graphical User Interface (GUI) pertaining to the developed framework has been updated based on the received feedback during training and vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/1036919 dated 31 Aug 23. \r\n\r\n3.   Documentation. The documentation of the project has been updated based on the received feedback vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/1036919 dated 31 Aug 23. The documentation of the project has been forwarded to MTSS as well as NCMA vide PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1320116 Dated 28 Sep 23. The document (4-NRDI-RULMANUAL-08100-001-000-0) saliently covers theoretical concepts, Operation of the RUL framework, data acquisition, uploading, diagnosis, prognosis and RUL estimation.  \r\n\r\n4.   Acceptance. ATPs were conducted on 07 Dec 23, subsequently feedback/observations were received from NCMA against conducted ATPs vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/6499087 dated 13 Dec 23. In response NRDI wrote a detailed response of received observation vide letter PN/ R AND D WING/PROJECTS/6595648 dated 19 Dec 23. A meeting was held on 11 Jan 24 between NCMA, FMG and NRDI for clarification of response sent by NRDI. Moreover, acceptance from NCMA has been received vide PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/7020919 dated 31 Jan 24.	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jan 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350014	1168	2024-02-06 16:27:00.648	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   The complete Raven II system has been successfully deployed onboard PNS MOAWIN for LWF held on 28 - 29 Oct 22. The project has been successfully completed. The project warranty is also completed.\r\n\r\n2.   Complete system was handed over by PNS MOAWIN to NRDI INTELL on 16 Feb 23 for training of PN personnel. 03 x days operator and maintenance training sessions on the developed Raven-II system have been imparted by NRDI INTELL team from 20-22 Jun 23 vide reference PN/ R AND D WING/GENERAL/4996456 dated 24 Jun 23. \r\n\r\n3.   NRDI INTELL successfully tested SSDLS antenna at Suparco SRDC-Lahore using GSP Testbench indigenously developed by NRDI INTELL. Feasibility Report of the tested system has been submitted vide letter (PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/6016051 dated 06 Nov 23).\r\n\r\n4.   Formulation of PMS/MMS routines (Job Information Card (JICs)) requested vide reference letter (PN/COMAUXMIN 9/MAINTANANCE/5444776 dated 26 Sep 23). In response NRDI forwarded PMS/MMS routines (Job Information Card (JICs)) of complete RAVEN II system vide reference letter PN/ R AND D WING/GENERAL/6801319 dated 08 Jan 24. Moreover, installation and ground test of complete system were successfully done onboard PNS MOAWIN on 5 Jan 24 for LWF (SS-24) subsequently system was handed over to WEO MOWAIN. Harbor and sea trials were also held with PC flight on 21 Jan 24 and 23 Jan 24 respectively. \r\n\r\n?	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jan 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350023	1166	2024-02-06 16:32:08.857	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Filter Design. Cavity based filters for L1 (1.3-1.5 GHz), L2 (1.7-1.8 GHz), and S-band (2.2-2.5 GHz) have been designed and fabricated. Design is further consolidated through reverse engineering of the original OEM filter using XRF analyzer for material characterization and 3D Scanner for dimensional analysis.\r\n\r\n2.   Field Testing. 09 x filters have been assembled and are ready to deliver, same has been informed to sponsoring directorate vide reference PN/R AND D WING/PROJECTS/5436562 dated 25 Sep 23. Moreover, draft ATPs have been revised vide letter PN/HQ COMPAK/MAINTENANCE/5714329 dated 13 Oct 23. Furthermore, NHQ was informed vide letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/6485602 Dated 07 Dec 23 that filters are ready for delivery and conduct of ATPs.\r\n\r\n3.   Conduct of FATs. FATs of NRDI INTELL fabricated 09 x filters were successfully conducted on 20 Dec 23 in the presence of 47 Sqn reps at NRDI INTELL. VNA testing along with material characterization was also performed during FATs. All filters were checked and performance was found within acceptable ranges. Afterwards, filters were handed over to 47 sqn reps for conduct of field trials, vide letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/6669049 Dated 21 Dec 23. Preliminary trials were conducted which exhibited range of 62NM. Further trials will be conducted to ascertain filter performance. However, it is pending due to maintenance & operational work at PNS MAKRAN as informed vide reference PN/COMNAV/MAINTENANCE/6963160 Dated 11 Jan 24	DSensors	Under Finalization	\N	25	Jan 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
