350023	1210	2024-03-12 12:28:17.558	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Filter Design. Cavity based filters for L1 (1.3-1.5 GHz), L2 (1.7-1.8 GHz), and S-band (2.2-2.5 GHz) have been designed and fabricated. Design is further consolidated through reverse engineering of the original OEM filter using XRF analyzer for material characterization and 3D Scanner for dimensional analysis.\r\n\r\n2.   Field Testing. 09 x filters have been assembled and are ready to deliver, same has been informed to sponsoring directorate vide reference PN/R AND D WING/PROJECTS/5436562 dated 25 Sep 23. Moreover, draft ATPs have been revised vide letter PN/HQ COMPAK/MAINTENANCE/5714329 dated 13 Oct 23. Furthermore, NHQ was informed vide letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/6485602 Dated 07 Dec 23 that filters are ready for delivery and conduct of ATPs.\r\n\r\n3.   Conduct of FATs. FATs of NRDI INTELL fabricated 09 x filters were successfully conducted on 20 Dec 23 in the presence of 47 Sqn reps at NRDI INTELL. VNA testing along with material characterization was also performed during FATs. All filters were checked and performance was found within acceptable ranges. Afterwards, filters were handed over to 47 sqn reps for conduct of field trials, vide letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/6669049 Dated 21 Dec 23. Preliminary trials were conducted which exhibited range of 62NM. Further trials will be conducted to ascertain filter performance. However, it is pending due to maintenance & operational work at PNS MAKRAN as informed vide reference PN/COMNAV/MAINTENANCE/6963160 Dated 11 Jan 24.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-03-27 09:39:52.429	25	Feb 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350022	1209	2024-03-12 12:27:28.544	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Antenna Design. Dish antenna has been designed and developed at NRDI INTELL. Patch feeder is also developed.    \r\n\r\n2.   Final Testing & Field Trials of 1st Prototype. FATs and aerial trials were successfully conducted with 01 x NRDI developed dish antenna and were found satisfactory with a range of 54 NM vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/PROJECTS/1038701 dated 01 Sep 23.\r\n\r\n3.   Delivery of 03 DA. 03 x Dish Antennas with all associated accessories handed over to rep of 47 Sqn vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/PROJECTS/1326593 dated 18 Sep 23. Successful HATs and aerial trials of 03 x Dish Antenna have also been conducted.\r\n\r\n4.   Delivery of Support Structure. 03 x Support structure for BSE Dish were handed over to 47 Sqn vide reference PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1419950 dated 11 Oct 23.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-03-27 09:39:59.565	25	Feb 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350012	1204	2024-03-12 12:18:21.878	Progress \r\n\r\n1.   Training of Personnel: 14 x Personnel (from NCMA, FMG (WE), FMG (ME), RD & TA, W&S, S & S, SW and ITRF) were earmarked and trained for Operation/ Installation and Maintenance, from 04 Sep 23 to 15 Sep 23.\r\n\r\n2.   GUI Development. The Graphical User Interface (GUI) pertaining to the developed framework has been updated based on the received feedback during training and vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/1036919 dated 31 Aug 23. \r\n\r\n3.   Documentation. The documentation of the project has been updated based on the received feedback vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/1036919 dated 31 Aug 23. The documentation of the project has been forwarded to MTSS as well as NCMA vide PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1320116 dated 28 Sep 23. The document (4-NRDI-RULMANUAL-08100-001-000-0) saliently covers theoretical concepts, Operation of the RUL framework, data acquisition, uploading, diagnosis, prognosis and RUL estimation.  \r\n\r\n4.   Acceptance. ATPs were conducted on 07 Dec 23, subsequently feedback/observations were received from NCMA against conducted ATPs vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/6499087 dated 13 Dec 23. In response NRDI wrote a detailed response of received observation vide letter PN/ R AND D WING/PROJECTS/6595648 dated 19 Dec 23. A meeting was held on 11 Jan 24 between NCMA, FMG and NRDI for clarification of response sent by NRDI. Moreover, acceptance from NCMA had been received vide PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/7020919 dated 31 Jan 24 and case is under process at NHQs. Hardware (02 x PCs, 06 x Data loggers, 01 x DVD) against Milestone-9 also ready for delivery. However, NCMA has requested to hold hardware provision till acceptance of the Milestone-6 by NHQs. NCMA letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/7627804 dated 29 Feb 2024 and NRDI letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/7546684 dated 24 Feb 24 refers.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-03-27 09:41:12.688	25	Feb 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350025	1215	2024-03-12 12:33:35.868	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   CDR Submission. The "Critical Design Report" (CDR) has been submitted against Milestone M6. \r\n\r\n2.   Procurement. Sintering furnace is being procured which will be utilized for development of cathode.\r\n\r\n3.   Design Activities. Reverse engineering for dimensional analysis and material characterization using XRF analyzer held with NRDI is in progress. Moreover, heater design, Electron Gun and slow wave structure designing is in progress. Power supply of existing TWT of LR66 radar is received at NRDI INTELL which will be utilized in this project. \r\n\r\n       a.   Design of Waveguide to Coaxial Adapter for cold testing of existing TWT on VNA.\r\n\r\n       b.   Heater Design: Sample heater coil has been successfully designed and manufactured. The manufacturing process has been established. The final design of heater coil will be developed based on calculation of cathode temperature and work function. \r\n\r\n       c.   Pierce Electron Gun: Simulation of Pierce electron Gun is being revised after finalization of SWS.\r\n\r\n       d.   Slow Wave Structure: Design has been completed. \r\n\r\n       e.   Collector Design:  Collector is being redesigned in accordance with beam spent curve analysis of slow wave structure. \r\n\r\n4.   Development of ARRC. Advance radar research center (ARRC) is being developed at manufacturing facility PNS KARSAZ. Design of ARRC has been completed whereas, development of Clean room is in progress. Procurement of Molecular Vacuum Pump & Bio Safety Cabinet is in progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-03-27 09:40:13.676	25	Feb 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
