350020	1230	2024-04-09 09:41:05.71	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Hardware Lab Assembly. Team visited GHARO on 9 Jan 24 for ground testing of LUNA RF and Avionics components. RF testing of Primary and secondary datalink antennas on GCS along with Remaining GCS side RF components such as attenuator, RF cables and BMR 120 has also been completed along with relevant ATP and ATR. Hardware lab assembly report is submitted. \r\n\r\n2.   Lab & Field Trials. Lab and field trials of the system were successfully carried out.\r\n\r\n3.   Training of AED Personnel. Training plan has been formulated and shared with AED, vide reference. In this regard, AED has nominated reps to attend the said training sessions, vide reference PN/COMNAV/MAINTENANCE/7970758 Dated 29 Mar 24.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-05-02 12:25:07.082	25	Mar 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350025	1228	2024-04-09 09:38:48.394	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   CDR Submission. The "Critical Design Report" (CDR) has been submitted against Milestone M6. \r\n\r\n2.   Procurement. Sintering furnace is being procured which will be utilized for development of cathode.\r\n\r\n3.   Design Activities. Reverse engineering for dimensional analysis and material characterization using XRF analyzer held with NRDI is in progress. Moreover, heater design, Electron Gun and slow wave structure designing is in progress. Power supply of existing TWT of LR66 radar is received at NRDI INTELL which will be utilized in this project. \r\n\r\n       a.   Design of Waveguide to Coaxial Adapter for cold testing of existing TWT on VNA.\r\n\r\n       b.   Heater Design: Sample heater coil has been successfully designed and manufactured. The manufacturing process has been established. The final design of heater coil will be developed based on calculation of cathode temperature and work function. \r\n\r\n       c.   Pierce Electron Gun: Simulation of Pierce electron Gun is also been revised after finalization of SWS.\r\n\r\n       d.   Slow Wave Structure: Design has been completed. \r\n\r\n       e.   Collector Design:  Collector is being redesigned in accordance with beam spent curve analysis of slow wave structure. \r\n\r\n4.   Development of ARRC. Advance radar research center (ARRC) is being developed at manufacturing facility PNS KARSAZ. Design of ARRC has been completed whereas, development of Clean room is in progress. Procurement of Molecular Vacuum Pump & Bio Safety Cabinet is in progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-05-02 12:24:16.343	25	Mar 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
