350023	1236	2024-04-09 09:47:38.373	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Filter Design. Cavity based filters for L1 (1.3-1.5 GHz), L2 (1.7-1.8 GHz), and S-band (2.2-2.5 GHz) have been designed and fabricated. Design is further consolidated through reverse engineering of the original OEM filter using XRF analyzer for material characterization and 3D Scanner for dimensional analysis.\r\n\r\n2.   Conduct of FATs. FATs of NRDI INTELL fabricated 09 x filters were successfully conducted on 20 Dec 23 in the presence of 47 Sqn reps at NRDI INTELL. VNA testing along with material characterization was also performed during FATs. All filters were checked and performance was found within acceptable ranges. Afterwards, filters were handed over to 47 sqn reps for conduct of field trials, vide letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/6669049 Dated 21 Dec 23. Preliminary trials were conducted which exhibited range of 62NM. Further trials will be conducted to ascertain filter performance. However, it is pending due to maintenance & operational work at PNS MAKRAN as informed vide reference PN/COMNAV/MAINTENANCE/6963160 Dated 11 Jan 24.\r\n\r\n3.   Field Testing. During Field testing 47Sqn faced some connectivity issues thus filters are returned to NRDI INTELL on 01 Apr 24. Defect rectification is in process.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-05-02 12:24:07.31	25	Mar 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350004	1237	2024-04-09 09:48:10.474	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Phase-II Work Order. The work order for phase 2 is still awaited. The earliest issuance of WO is requested in order to retain the trained project HR. \r\n\r\n2.   Space Requirement for UCAV Development. Allocation of PNS BAHADUR drill shed for shifting of NRDI M/SPF to undertake UCAV development is awaited. NHQ letter PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3754293 dated 02 Jun 22 refers.\r\n\r\n3.   For earlier issuance of the WO case has been processed with NHQ vide letter PN/NDRI/GENERAL/4586185 dated 01 Jun 23.\r\n\r\n4.   NRDI has successfully developed test bench for the ROTAX engine, the test bench is fully operational and capable of monitoring multiple parameters. Moreover, during the COMPAK Command presentation held on 26 Apr 22, perused by the Chief of the Naval Staff vide reference PN/NO Dte/OPERATIONS /1101791 dated 03 Jul 23, it has been decided that the NRDI is to be engaged to establish I&D level maintenance setup / limited R&D of CH4. PPF and URD have been received. Work on technical and budgetary proposal will be started upon identification of airworthiness certification body from NHQ.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-05-02 12:25:16.114	25	Mar 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
250003	1240	2024-05-20 10:55:03.644	1.   Competent authority approved indigenous development of STLT at a cost of Rs 53.85M in 3rd R&D Board vide NRD/189/R & D Board/158 dated 02 Jan 2023.\r\n\r\n2.   Project has been approved to be undertaken at the cost of 53.85 M. Rs 10 M to be allocated during CFY for Recoupment in BOA with M/S MTSS for subsequent issuance of work order. \r\n\r\n3.   Workorder has been issued w.e.f 22 June 2023.\r\n\r\n4.   Milestone 1 and 2 have been completed. Milestone 3 is in progress.\r\n\r\n5.   Visit of PNSM KHALID was conducted by officers on 21 Dec 2023 for manual acquisition of images/ videos of Torpedo Launching Tube (TLT) section of AGOSTA 90B S/M.\r\n\r\n6.   Initial wire diagram of the overall structure/ environment of Section C has been developed. Milestone 3 has been completed. Milestone 4 is currently in progress.	DEnab	Finalized	2024-05-27 11:44:55.823	25	Apr 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
200004	1246	2024-06-03 08:55:27.776	1.   Work on all subsystems of ELINT DZ9000S has been completed and lab trials have been conducted successfully.\r\n\r\n2.   The system installation and setting to work has been completed on site on 10 Feb 22.\r\n\r\n3.   Phase I of ATPs (testing of system sensitivity and parameter measurement accuracy) has been successfully completed. \r\n\r\n4.   On air trials using Test Transmitter has been completed for SUPERHET.  Trials with PNS HIMMAT conducted in July 22. Trials with P3C are planned during this month (Oct 22). \r\n\r\n5.   Work will continue on recovery of modules made good using spares from PN inventory as well as on addressing observations by SS/PAT.\r\n\r\n6.   Two work orders have been issued for this project. All milestones for both projects were complete pending acceptance by PAT. However, system was struck by lighning on 7 Nov 22. \r\n\r\n7.   Considerable damage happened due to the lightning. Recovery of the system has been completed. \r\n\r\n8.   Upgradation of lightning Protection System (LPS) by SS through MES was completed in June. \r\n\r\n9.   ATP Phase II (Final SATs) have been completed on 26-27 Jun 23 and analysis of performance is complete. \r\n\r\n10.   System evaluated by SMEs of ELINT system from 19 - 23 Feb 24. System recommended for acceptance by SMEs. Formal acceptance awaited by Acceptance committee.	DCom	Finalized	2024-06-10 10:00:51.365	25	May 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
200008	1245	2024-06-03 08:55:14.067	1.   Milestone 1 has been completed and accepted.\r\n\r\n2.   One of the Radars was made available onboard in April 22 and data tapping activity has been completed.\r\n\r\n3.   Milestone 2 has been completed and submitted on 15 May.\r\n\r\n4.   Development of PoC/prototype has been completed and lab trials  by ship staff (Milestone 3) was conducted successfully on 1 Dec 22\r\n\r\n5.   Installation of 01xLED completed on 17th Mar 23. Ship was subsequently in SRA, which has been completed in June 23.\r\n\r\n6.   03xLEDs (total) installed onboard in Nov 23.\r\n\r\n7.   02 x OJ-194 displays tested with dummy sweep of SPS-49 Radar and 01 x OJ-197 tested with Fruno Radar Display.\r\n\r\n8.   Currently, all relevant Radars onboard are defective. STW and SATs will be conducted upon availability of Radars.\r\n\r\n9.   Alternative functionality of LEDs, i.e., plan for provision of display IMSS, NIXIS and TDL on screens was submitted for approval by NHQ, which was aproved in April 24\r\n\r\n10.   The displays have been installed onboard. The project will be closed upon receipt of acceptance certificate from SS.	DCom	Finalized	2024-06-10 10:00:58.949	25	May 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
200013	1248	2024-06-03 08:55:57.462	1.   T0 established in May 23\r\n\r\n2.   Global Plan and CDR (MS 2 and 3) completed and accepted.\r\n\r\n3.   MMI (MS 4) completed and accepted.\r\n\r\n4.   09 x sensors repaired during ship EMP.\r\n\r\n5.   Cable installation and MMI hardware planned during upcoming working window of the ship	DCom	Finalized	2024-06-10 10:00:26.721	25	May 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
200014	1249	2024-06-03 08:56:08.226	1.   T0 established on 15 Jun 23\r\n\r\n2.   Global Plan completed and accepted in Dec 23\r\n\r\n3.   CDR completed and accepted in Dec 23. PRO awaited.\r\n\r\n4.   Instllation of pipes and valves completed during EMP of the ship.\r\n\r\n5.   Payment for MS-I and partial paymet (MS-I) have been received. Ordering of IGS plant and installation of cable will be undertaken on confirmation of availability of funds for the project by NHQ.	DCom	Finalized	2024-06-10 10:00:35.737	25	May 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
